\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court strikes down Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against US gunmakers\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 467 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2025\par 15:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit alleged that \uc2 Smith & Wesson\uc2  and Interstate Arms aided the illegal trafficking of firearms to drug cartels\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court }}}\uc2  on Thursday spared two American gun companies from a lawsuit by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico }}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government accusing them of aiding illegal firearms trafficking to drug cartels and fueling gun violence on the south side of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Mexico border }}}\uc2 . <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/05/supreme-court-decision-ruling-catholic-charity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court backs Catholic charity group in unemployment taxes case }}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 The justices, in a unanimous ruling, overturned a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision that had allowed the lawsuit to proceed against the firearms maker \uc2 Smith & Wesson\uc2  and distributor Interstate Arms. The lower court had found that Mexico plausibly alleged that the companies aided and abetted illegal gun sales, harming its government.\par \par \uc2 The companies had argued for the dismissal of Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s suit, filed in Boston in 2021, under a 2005 US law called the Protection of Lawful Commerce in Arms Act that broadly shields gun companies from liability for crimes committed with their products. The Boston-based first circuit court of appeals decided in 2024 that the alleged conduct by the companies fell outside these protections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMexico alleges that the companies aided and abetted unlawful sales routing guns to Mexican drug cartels. The question presented is whether Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s complaint plausibly pleads that conduct. We conclude it does not,\u8221\'20\'1D the liberal justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  wrote for the supreme court on Thursday morning. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/05/supreme-court-reverse-discrimination-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court sides with heterosexual woman in \u8216\'20\'18reverse discrimination\u8217\'20\'19 case }}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 The case came to the supreme court at a complicated time for US-Mexican relations as Donald Trump pursues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on-again, off-again tariffs }}}\uc2  on Mexican goods imported into the US. Trump has also accused Mexico of doing too little to stop the flow of synthetic drugs such as the opioid fentanyl and migrant arrivals at the border, even though Mexico has stepped up efforts to prevent migrants from reaching the border in recent years.\par \par \uc2 Mexico had claimed that the companies have deliberately maintained a distribution system that included firearms dealers who knowingly sell weapons to third-party, or \u8220\'20\'1Cstraw\u8221\'20\'1D, purchasers who then traffic guns to cartels in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The suit also accused the companies of unlawfully designing and marketing their guns as military-grade weapons to drive up demand among the cartels.\par \par \uc2 Mexico in the lawsuit sought monetary damages of an unspecified amount and a court order requiring \uc2 Smith & Wesson\uc2  and Interstate Arms to take steps to \u8220\'20\'1Cabate and remedy the public nuisance they have created in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Gun violence fueled by trafficked US-made firearms has contributed to a decline in business investment and economic activity in Mexico. \par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250605el65002mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
