\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Another snake-oil salesman\u8217\'20\'19s pitch\u8217\'20\'19: US workers wary of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s steel deal\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 977 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 June 2025\par 04:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president believes his \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  agreement will revive America\u8217\'20\'19s steel industry \u8211\'20\'13 but workers are skeptical\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump, once \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/03/trump-nippon-us-steel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 totally against}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D Nippon Steel of Japan\u8217\'20\'19s controversial $14bn takeover bid for \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , the second largest US steel producer, is now hailing the deal as a turning point for the struggling industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to call this section a rust belt any more,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/trump-tariffs-steel-japan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  at a plant in West Mifflin, Pennsylvania, on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19ll be a golden belt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers are not holding their breath as they await details. \u8220\'20\'1COur members know from decades of negotiating contracts: trust nothing until you see it in writing,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 David McCall\uc2 , president of \uc2 United Steel Workers\uc2 , said in a statement last week.\par \par \uc2 And veterans of the sector, which has withered for decades, are dubious.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is another snake-oil salesman\u8217\'20\'19s pitch to make him look good and reward the billionaires and millionaire executives and stakeholders for \uc2 US Steel\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Doug May, who worked for 43 years as a steel worker at a mill in Granite City, Illinois, from the age of 19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a proven flip-flopper. Just look at his trade cases: on again, off again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump ditched his opposition to the deal \u8211\'20\'13 which \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/nippon-steel-japan-cfius-economy-biden-099564a3cddca587af0d7340e0c15ed6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  in January, citing national security concerns \u8211\'20\'13 last week, claiming it would create tens of thousands of jobs.\par \par \uc2 At Friday\u8217\'20\'19s Pennsylvania rally, the president also announced he was doubling US tariffs on foreign steel to 50%. \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be yet another BIG jolt of great news for our wonderful steel and aluminum workers,\u8221\'20\'1D he later claimed on social media.\par \par \uc2 As Nippon looks to swoop on \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , however, staff are still waiting on clarity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre we still going to be employed when this whole thing goes through, and are there going to be improvements to our plant?\u8221\'20\'1D Mikayla Prescott, a worker at the Irvin site where Trump spoke on Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.post-gazette.com/news/politics-nation/2025/05/31/trump-nippon-us-steel-mon-valley/stories/202506010097"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Pittsburgh Post-Gazette}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s not benefiting the workers,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, \u8220\'20\'1Cthen what\u8217\'20\'19s the point?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Following his retirement in 2016, May has followed international trade deals involving steel and watched the negative impacts of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uswlocals.org/soar-chapter-7-34-2/latest-articles/why-retired-steelworker-soar-doug-may-isn-t-done-fighting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foreign steel imports}}}\uc2  on the US industry.\par \par \uc2 May said the president \u8220\'20\'1Crecognized [the] disenchantment and anger\u8221\'20\'1D over the decline of the US steel industry but expressed distrust and disapproval of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric and promises in supporting the deal.\par \par \uc2 While the deal is said to include a \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden share\u8221\'20\'1D that will be issued to the federal government, details have not been disclosed. \uc2 US Steel\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/trump-tariffs-steel-japan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterized}}}\uc2  the deal as an acquisition.\par \par \uc2 United Steel Workers\uc2 , which did not participate in the discussions around the acquisition of \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw.org/press-release/usw-statement-on-u-s-steel-nippon-partnership/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  has been found to have violated US trade laws in 13 different cases.\par \par \uc2 The union\u8217\'20\'19s most recent contract with \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , signed in 2022 and set to expire at the end of 2026, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://investors.ussteel.com/news-events/news-releases/detail/7/u-s-steel-announces-ratification-of-new-collective"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represents 11,000 workers }}}\uc2 at the company.\par \par \uc2 US Steel\uc2  bought the Granite City plant, where May used to work, out of bankruptcy in 2003. The plant was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bnd.com/news/local/article17747042.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily idled}}}\uc2  for months in 2009 due to the recession, the first time in the plant\u8217\'20\'19s over 100-year history, and following another idling of the plant in December 2015, \uc2 US Steel\uc2  announced in March 2018 it was reopening the plant, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2018/03/07/us-steel-reopening-plant-and-bringing-back-jobs-ceo-on-trump-tariffs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 citing}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 25% tariffs on steel imports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are once again pouring American steel into the spine of our country,\u8221\'20\'1D the president, then in his first term, declared at a rally at Granite City. \u8220\'20\'1CYou are the ones who are making America great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 May disputed Trump, or his tariffs, as the reason for the reopening, which he suggested was a result of the cyclical nature of the industry. In 2016, the \uc2 US Steel\uc2  chief executive had said the plant was idled due to market conditions and that it would be brought back when conditions improve.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGranite City was going to start back up anyway,\u8221\'20\'1D said May. \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t just flip a switch just because Trump came to town.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s promises in 2018 to bring back \u8220\'20\'1Chope and prosperity\u8221\'20\'1D to Granite City, problems continued. The plant\u8217\'20\'19s blast furnace was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stlpr.org/economy-business/2023-11-28/u-s-steel-idles-steelmaking-at-granite-city-plant-could-lay-off-majority-of-workforce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 idled}}}\uc2  partially in 2019, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumlocalnews.com/mo/st-louis/news/2024/12/24/us-steel-granite-city"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 then its second was idled }}}\uc2 in late 2023, which \uc2 US Steel{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw.org/press-release/usw-decries-uss-decision-to-idle-steelmaking-at-granite-city-works/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  blamed }}}\uc2 on the autoworkers\u8217\'20\'19 strike at the big three automakers. \uc2 United Steel Workers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stlpr.org/economy-business/2023-11-28/u-s-steel-idles-steelmaking-at-granite-city-plant-could-lay-off-majority-of-workforce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued }}}\uc2 the decision was a targeted attack on unionized workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump really had steel workers\u8217\'20\'19 backs, he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prospect.org/labor/2025-03-17-trump-pick-union-busting-attorney-key-labor-law-position-nlrb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-union appointments}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D May added. \u8220\'20\'1CHe wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/27/trump-safety-cuts-workplace-risks-niosh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decimating}}}\uc2  Osha [the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration\uc2 ]. He wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be doing everything he\u8217\'20\'19s done: a long list of things that prove that he\u8217\'20\'19s not supportive of unions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 May said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \u8216\'20\'18partnership\u8217\'20\'19 that those at the rally are celebrating, despite scant details of investments being shared, could become your very nemesis in a short period of time. Solidarity with USW leadership and members across the country is critical going forward. Once the shit hits the fan, commitments are unfulfilled, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/09/21/us-steel-union-opposition-sale-nippon-steelworkers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 non-union electric arc furnace actions}}}\uc2  will be used as a contract bargaining weapon and the rally is a forgotten memory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is a \u8220\'20\'1Cvast difference between public relations and putting commitments in writing\u8221\'20\'1D, McCall, the USW president, said in a statement last week. \u8220\'20\'1CIssuing press releases and making political speeches is easy. Binding commitments are hard,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe devil is always in the details, and that is especially true with a bad actor like \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  that has again and again violated our trade laws, devastating steel communities in Pennsylvania and elsewhere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US Steel\uc2  did not respond to multiple requests for comment on criticisms from \uc2 United Steel Workers\uc2  on the deal.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250604el64000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
