\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Vought says Trump may not need Congress\u8217\'20\'19s approval to cut federal jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Olivares in New York \par \uc2 637 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2025\par 12:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amid bipartisan opposition, director of management and budget office says Trump prefers to use \u8216\'20\'18executive tools\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2 , the director of the office of management and budget (OMB), on Sunday cast doubt on the constitutional obligation of the White House to ask Congress to sign off on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/29/elon-musk-trump-doge-adviser-exit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sweeping cuts}}}\uc2  to the federal workforce spearheaded by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vought indicated the White House preferred to rely on \u8220\'20\'1Cexecutive tools\u8221\'20\'1D for all but a \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D fraction of the cuts instead of submitting the whole package of jobs and agency slashing that took place via the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge), to the congressional branch for its official approval.\par \par \uc2 The White House budget director, in an interview with CNN on Sunday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/01/trump-tax-bill-white-house-budget-director"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also defended}}}\uc2  the widespread future cost-cutting proposed by the US president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/what-is-trump-big-beautiful-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One Big Beautiful Bill Act}}}\uc2  that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2025/may/22/house-vote-trump-tax-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed by}}}\uc2  the House last week, which covers budget proposals for the next fiscal year starting in October. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/01/trump-tax-bill-white-house-budget-director"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US budget chief calls fears that cuts to benefits will lead to deaths \u8216\'20\'18totally ridiculous\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 But, as Dana Bash, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union host, pointed out, Doge cut \u8220\'20\'1Cfunding and programs that Congress already passed\u8221\'20\'1D. And while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/29/elon-musk-trump-doge-adviser-exit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 those cuts}}}\uc2 , cited by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/key-takeaways-musk-trump-send-off"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the departing}}}\uc2  Musk as being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/elon-musk-leaving-white-house-doge-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worth $175bn}}}\uc2 , are tiny {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/25/elon-musk-trump-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared}}}\uc2  with the trillion or more he forecast, Vought said OMB was only going to submit about $9.4bn to Congress this week for sign-off. That amount is understood to mostly cover the crushing of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USAID agency}}}\uc2  and cuts to public broadcasting, which have prompted outrage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/01/npr-lawsuit-trump-war-on-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and lawsuits}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Leaders of Congress from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-senate-republicans-call-trump-enshrine-spending-cuts-law-2025-03-28/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 both parties}}}\uc2  have pressed for the Trump administration to send details of all the cuts for its approval. \u8220\'20\'1CWill you?\u8221\'20\'1D Bash asked Vought.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe might,\u8221\'20\'1D Vought said, adding that the rest of the Doge cuts may not need official congressional approval.\par \par \uc2 As one of the architects of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/project-2025-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , the rightwing initiative created to guide the second Trump administration, Vought is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/01/trump-tax-bill-white-house-budget-director"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on a quest}}}\uc2  to dismantle the federal workforce, consolidate power for the US president and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/16/russ-vought-trump-project-2025-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to continue}}}\uc2  the Doge cuts.\par \par \uc2 Vought said that one of the executive tools the administration has is the use of \u8220\'20\'1Cimpoundment\u8221\'20\'1D, which involves the White House withholding specific funds allocated by Congress. Since the 1970s, a law has limited the presidency from engaging in impoundment \u8211\'20\'13 typically requiring the executive branch to implement what Congress signed into law.\par \par \uc2 Bash said: \u8220\'20\'1CI know you don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that that is constitutional, so are you just doing this in order to get {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/01/us-supreme-court-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the supreme court}}}\uc2  to rule that unconstitutional?\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/01/us-supreme-court-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stakes are high for US democracy as conservative supreme court hears raft of cases}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Vought said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not in love with the law.\u8221\'20\'1D But he also said, in response to criticism from some on Capitol Hill: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not breaking the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, on the spending bill, the \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2025-05/61422-Reconciliation-Distributional-Analysis.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBO}}}\uc2 ) and many experts say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/24/trump-tax-bill-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it could swell}}}\uc2  the US deficit by $3.8tn, and business tycoon Musk said it \u8220\'20\'1Cundermines the work the Doge team is doing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vought disagreed. \u8220\'20\'1CI love Elon, [but] this bill doesn\u8217\'20\'19t increase the deficit or hurt the debt,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Vought \u8211\'20\'13 and later on Sunday, the House speaker, Mike Johnson, on NBC \u8211\'20\'13 argued that critics\u8217\'20\'19 calculations do not fully account for extending the 2017 Trump tax cuts and slashing regulation.\par \par \uc2 Vought also chipped in that Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe architect, the visionary, the originator of his own agenda\u8221\'20\'1D, rather than \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s blueprint for the administration, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , although he did not deny that the two have dovetailed.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250601el610028n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
