\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Trump takes \u8216\'20\'18wrecking ball\u8217\'20\'19 to workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights amid global \u8216\'20\'18freefall\u8217\'20\'19, new report says\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 686 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2025\par 22:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 International Trade Union Confederation\uc2  issued report showing conditions for workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights across the globe have worsened\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/workers--rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights}}}\uc2  across every continent in the world are in a \u8220\'20\'1Cfreefall\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ituc-csi.org/global-rights-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2025 Global Rights Index }}}\uc2 released by the \uc2 International Trade Union Confederation\uc2 , the largest trade union federation in the world.\par \par \uc2 The index noted workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights and democracy around the world are often under attack by \u8220\'20\'1Cfar-right politicians and their unelected billionaire backers. Whether it\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  in the US or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/javier-milei"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Javier Milei}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Eduardo Eurnekian\uc2  in Argentina, we see the same playbook of unfairness and authoritarianism in action around the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the US, the index cited \u8220\'20\'1Cthe \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  administration has taken a wrecking ball to the collective labour rights of workers and brought anti-union billionaires into the heart of policymaking\u8221\'20\'1D. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/27/trump-safety-cuts-workplace-risks-niosh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s safety research cuts heighten workplace risks, federal workers warn}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 These actions, according to the index, include stripping union protections from 47,000 workers at the \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2 , attempting to revoke civil service protections for large swaths of federal employees and firing a member of the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , leaving it without a quorum.\par \par \uc2 Luc Triangle, secretary general of the \uc2 International Trade Union Confederation\uc2 , said the report covers events up until March 2025, but these trends have continued to worsen in the US since then.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://federalnewsnetwork.com/workforce/2025/03/federal-labor-mediation-agency-cuts-staff-down-to-skeleton-crew/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drastically cut staff }}}\uc2 at the \uc2 Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/11/trump-labor-flra-firing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  a board member of the \uc2 Federal Labor Relations Authority\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/03/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-exempts-agencies-with-national-security-missions-from-federal-collective-bargaining-requirements/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued }}}\uc2 an executive order revoking collective bargaining rights for the majority of federal employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn more and more countries, we have elected leaders that once they are elected democratically, they are taking action against democratic values,\u8221\'20\'1D said Triangle. \u8220\'20\'1CThe first target of those leaders in many countries is they attack trade human rights and workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, because we are the biggest defenders of democratic values and in that sense also their biggest opponents as largest social movement in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Three out of five global regions saw conditions for workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights worsen, including the Americas and Europe hitting their worst scores on the index since it was established in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Only seven out of 151 nations surveyed by the index had a top-tier rating on workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, down from 18 in 2015.\par \par \uc2 Workers\u8217\'20\'19 access to justice was restricted in 72% of nations surveyed, the worst on record, 87% of countries violated the right to strike and 80% violated the right to collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 The worst countries for workers, according to the report, are Bangladesh, Belarus, Ecuador, Egypt, Eswatini, Myanmar, Nigeria, the Philippines, Tunisia and Turkey.\par \par \uc2 Only three countries, Australia, Mexico and Oman, saw their ratings improve from 2024.\par \par \uc2 Triangle warned that the billionaire backers of these politicians have come out of the shadows and only expanded their wealth and control over important parts of society, in a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoup\u8221\'20\'1D by billionaires of democratic institutions globally that are driving these deteriorating conditions for workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last four or five years with Covid and increased inflation, people lost purchasing power and that\u8217\'20\'19s the breeding ground for extremist parties to get voters to vote for extremist parties, which actually don\u8217\'20\'19t offer any solution for the working people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Triangle.\par \par \uc2 The federation of unions is pushing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ituc-csi.org/fordemocracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign}}}\uc2  for democracy that delivers in opposition to the framework model {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ituc-csi.org/IMG/pdf/billionaires_vs_workers_en.pdf?42239/17d02f28b7d7bfe98cbfc6ec0271816295892513d97d86d2d66cdb4d1aa4194c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  in the US, and other billionaires and far-right political leaders around the world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe five richest people in the world {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oxfam.org.uk/media/press-releases/wealth-of-five-richest-men-doubles-since-2020-as-wealth-of-five-billion-people-falls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than doubled their wealth}}}\uc2  over the last five years, while 60% of the population of the world got poorer. We are investing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nationalinterest.org/blog/reboot/3-trillion-thats-how-much-world-spends-arms-each-year-181113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly US$3tn}}}\uc2  as a world into arms and into weapons and there is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oxfamamerica.org/explore/stories/do-the-rich-pay-their-fair-share/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfair taxation}}}\uc2 . So if we want to find the money for delivering to working people to what they really need \u8211\'20\'13 good wages, more jobs, rights, social protections \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a matter of political choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250601el61002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
