\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump announces 50% steel tariffs and hails \u8216\'20\'18blockbuster\u8217\'20\'19 deal with Japan\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino and Robert Mackey \par \uc2 1,053 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2025\par 13:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President tells Pennsylvania rally tariffs will aid workers but questions raised over nature of \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  investment\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced on Friday he was doubling foreign tariffs on steel imports to 50%, as the president celebrated a \u8220\'20\'1Cblockbuster\u8221\'20\'1D agreement for Japan-based \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  to invest in \uc2 US Steel\uc2  during a rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Surrounded by men in orange hardhats at a \uc2 US Steel\uc2  plant in West Mifflin, Trump unveiled the new levies, declaring that the dramatic rate increase would \u8220\'20\'1Ceven further secure the steel industry in the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody is going to get around that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of the tariff rate hike from what was 25%.\par \par \uc2 In a social media post after the conclusion of his remarks, Trump announced that the 50% tariffs on steel would also apply to imported aluminum and would take effect on 4 June. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/trump-fires-kim-sajet-national-portrait-gallery-director"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says he fired National Portrait Gallery chief in latest conflict with arts}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be yet another BIG jolt of great news for our wonderful steel and aluminum workers,\u8221\'20\'1D he declared in the post.\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear how the announcement would affect the trade deal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/08/cars-steel-and-hormone-fed-beef-the-key-points-of-the-ukus-trade-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 negotiated earlier this month}}}\uc2  that saw tariffs on UK steel and aluminum reduced to zero.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Friday announcement came a day after a federal appeals court temporarily allowed his tariffs to remain in effect, staying a decision by a US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-court-blocks-trumps-liberation-day-tariffs-2025-05-28/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trade court}}}\uc2  that blocked the president from imposing the duties.\par \par \uc2 The trade court ruling, however, does not impede the president\u8217\'20\'19s ability to unilaterally raise tariffs on steel imports, an authority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cfr.org/expert-brief/trumps-tariffs-arent-over-they-face-major-challenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted}}}\uc2  under a national security provision called section 232 of the Trade Expansion Act.\par \par \uc2 The precise relationship between \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  and \uc2 US Steel\uc2  raised questions on Friday, even for some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies. The president has thrown his full support behind the deal, months after insisting he was \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/03/trump-nippon-us-steel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 totally against}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D a $14.9bn bid by \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  for its US rival.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union had previously urged Trump to reject Nippon\u8217\'20\'19s bid, dismissing the Japanese firm\u8217\'20\'19s commitments to invest in the US as \u8220\'20\'1Cflashy promises\u8221\'20\'1D and claiming it was \u8220\'20\'1Csimply seeking to undercut our domestic industry from the inside\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to steelworkers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  insisted that \uc2 US Steel\uc2  would \u8220\'20\'1Cstay an American company\u8221\'20\'1D after what he is now calling \u8220\'20\'1Ca partnership\u8221\'20\'1D with Nippon.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ussteel.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Steel\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2  links to a standalone site with the combined branding of the two companies that features {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bestdealforamericansteel.com/transaction-benefits-for-all-stakeholders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  describing the transaction as \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 US Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agreement to be acquired by NSC\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bestdealforamericansteel.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website touting the deal}}}\uc2 , there were also multiple references to \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acquisition of \uc2 US Steel\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and the \u8220\'20\'1Cpotential sale of \uc2 US Steel\uc2  to \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Even pro-Trump commentators on Fox expressed bafflement over the exact nature of the deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is being described as \u8216\'20\'18a partnership\u8217\'20\'19, this deal between Nippon and \uc2 US Steel\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but then it\u8217\'20\'19s described as an acquisition on the \uc2 US Steel\uc2  website,\u8221\'20\'1D Fox host Laura Ingraham {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Acyn/status/1928600393401221487"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed out}}}\uc2  on her Friday-night show.\par \par \uc2 She asked a guest from another pro-Trump outlet, Breitbart: \u8220\'20\'1CWho owns the majority stake in this company?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the guest said he did not know, Ingraham suggested Trump might not be aware of the details. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know if he was fully informed about the terms of the deal. We just don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/03/us-blocks-us-steel-nippon-steel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  Nippon\u8217\'20\'19s acquisition, citing national security concerns, during his final weeks in office.\par \par \uc2 During his remarks at the rally, Trump gloated that the Nippon investment would once again make the American steelmaker \u8220\'20\'1Csynonymous with greatness\u8221\'20\'1D. He said protections were included to \u8220\'20\'1Censure that all steel workers will keep their jobs and all facilities in the United States will remain open and thriving\u8221\'20\'1D and said Nippon had committed to maintaining all of \uc2 US Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s currently operating blast furnaces for the next decade.\par \par \uc2 The president also promised that every US steel worker would soon receive a $5,000 bonus \u8211\'20\'13 prompting the crowd to start a round of \u8220\'20\'1CU-S-A!\u8221\'20\'1D chants.\par \par \uc2 Trump told the steelworkers in attendance that there was \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of money coming your way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to call this section a rust belt any more,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19ll be a golden belt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the event, Trump invited local members of \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  on to the stage to promote the Nippon deal, which saw its leader break with the union to support it. Praising the president, Jason Zugai, vice-president of Irvin local 2227, said he believed the investments would be \u8220\'20\'1Clife-changing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the powerful \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union remained wary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur primary concern remains with the impact that this merger of \uc2 US Steel\uc2  into a foreign competitor will have on national security, our members and the communities where we live and work,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  president, \uc2 David McCall\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIssuing press releases and making political speeches is easy. Binding commitments are hard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump framed the administration\u8217\'20\'19s drive to boost domestic steel production as \u8220\'20\'1Cnot just a matter of dignity or prosperity or pride\u8221\'20\'1D but as \u8220\'20\'1Cabove all, a matter of national security\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He blamed \u8220\'20\'1Cdecades of Washington betrayals and incompetence and stupidity and corruption\u8221\'20\'1D for hollowing out the once-dominant American steel industry, as the jobs \u8220\'20\'1Cmelted away, just like butter\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want America\u8217\'20\'19s future to be built with shoddy steel from Shanghai. We want it built with the strength and the pride of Pittsburgh,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In his remarks at a US steel plant, Trump also repeated many of the false claims that have become a feature of his rallies including the lie that the 2020 election was stolen from him. He gloated over his 2024 victory and, gesturing toward his ear that was grazed by a would-be assassin\u8217\'20\'19s bullet last year at a rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, said it was proof that a higher power was watching over him.\par \par \uc2 He also called on congressional Republicans to align behind his \u8220\'20\'1Cone big, beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D, urging attendees to lobby their representatives and senators to support the measure.\par \par \uc2 Lois Beckett and Callum Jones contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250530el5u003bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
