\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Unions representing Harvard workers fear Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18authoritarian turn\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 935 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 May 2025\par 15:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 International students and employees are \u8216\'20\'18afraid to speak out\u8217\'20\'19 as White House escalates push to control enrollment\par \par \uc2 Labor unions representing undergraduate, graduate, postdoctoral and academic workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/harvard-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard University}}}\uc2  criticized the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/trump-harvard-international-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevent}}}\uc2  Harvard from enrolling foreign students, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the single largest concentrated deportation threats against a unionized workforce in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A judge on 29 May extended an injunction blocking the Trump administration from revoking Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s ability to host international students, which would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-harvard-international-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affect}}}\uc2  5,000 current students and 2,000 graduates in a post-graduation work programme. Some 4,000 student workers represented by unions at Harvard who would be impacted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration\u8217\'20\'19s threat to international scholars is a huge attack on thousands of \uc2 UAW\uc2 -represented workers on Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s campus. We are seeing escalations against immigrant workers across the country and this is no different,\u8221\'20\'1D said the director of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  Region 9A, Brandon Mancilla. \u8220\'20\'1CThe labor movement must see these attacks as what they are \u8211\'20\'13 an attempt to divide workers and create false enemies in a time of rampant corporate greed.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-harvard-international-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge expands order protecting Harvard from Trump block on enrolling international students}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Sudipta Saha, a fourth-year PhD candidate in population health sciences at Harvard who holds citizenship with Canada and Bangladesh, and is a member of the executive board of the Harvard Graduate Students Union, explained the fears the move has instilled in international student workers on campus who are worried about their visa status, education and research.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if Harvard wins this particular case, the broader authoritarian turn that this represents is still being successful, because a lot of people are worried about whether they can actually speak out,\u8221\'20\'1D said Saha. \u8220\'20\'1CInternational students who have been asking me, have been asking each other, is it safe to go on the record? Is it safe to even write an op ed? And I think when people are asking questions like that, that kind of shows how already, how successful this kind of crackdown has been.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do a lot of vital work. There are people working on robotics, cancer drugs and Alzheimer\u8217\'20\'19s research. All of that is impacted when they\u8217\'20\'19re forced to stop,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CAll of this research work is tangled with a ton of other industries that are not necessarily within the university, from development of these pharmaceutical drugs to research equipment, all of those things are affected if they were forced to stop their work and leave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/international-student-visa-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted}}}\uc2  interviews for all student exchanges and visas and secretary of state \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/28/us/politics/china-student-visas-revoke.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed}}}\uc2  to begin revoking visas of students from China with ties to the China Communist party or working in critical fields. <aside class="element element-pullquote element--supporting">\par \par \uc2 The labor movement must see these attacks as what they are \u8211\'20\'13 an attempt to divide workers and create false enemies <footer> Brandon Mancilla, \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  </footer> </aside>\par \par \uc2 Ellen Yi, a Rhodes scholar from China who was admitted to a doctoral program at Harvard, was set to join Harvard in fall 2025, but is now looking for different options.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel a strong sense of insecurity and uncertainty. The policy keeps swinging back and forth and we don\u8217\'20\'19t know what is the next step of the government,\u8221\'20\'1D said Yi. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very pessimistic about the future and I\u8217\'20\'19m looking for some safer options.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to Rubio\u8217\'20\'19s threats of revoking visas from Chinese students, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CI was not very surprised, but still very disappointed, frustrated and kind of panicked, because the policy statement was very unclear,\u8221\'20\'1D adding it remains unclear how the Trump administration will define connections to the Chinese Communist party or critical fields.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI find this absurd,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ozan Bayta\u351\'01\'5F, a postdoctoral researcher at \uc2 Harvard Medical School\uc2  from Turkey. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a clear attack on the universities, freedom of speech, academic freedom and science, and there\u8217\'20\'19s a clear intention to purge the current system of many non-citizen workers who are very talented.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He cited Maureen Martin, the director of immigration services at Harvard, who wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.harvard.edu/federal-lawsuits/wp-content/uploads/sites/17/2025/05/0046.-05-28-2025-DECLARATION-re-9-Memorandum-in-Support-of-Motion-Supplemental-Declaration-of-Maureen-Martin-by.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court declaration}}}\uc2  that the revocation notice has made students afraid to attend graduation ceremonies, have forced international students to reconsider their futures at Harvard and inquire about transferring, and that incoming international students have already reported experiencing issues in obtaining visas. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/trump-harvard-federal-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump orders agencies to cut all federal ties with Harvard}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany internationals, non-citizen workers are afraid to speak out. Many want to leave. Many don\u8217\'20\'19t want to come back to the US, because they think their future plans may be interrupted by a whimsical move from the government at any moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Baytas added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe best of the best in the world wants to come here to Harvard because there are opportunities. There are many good research labs, and they simply won\u8217\'20\'19t come here, and the science here will suffer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite the policies and rhetoric coming from the Trump administration, Bayta\u351\'01\'5F argued that student workers and unions, in and out of the legal system, intend to fight back.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in the US here say stand up, fight back, so I am confident academic freedom will rise,\u8221\'20\'1D he concluded. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very hopeful, despite all the failings of the current administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harvard and the White House did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250530el5u0025x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
