\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Salutes, Maga hats and mass layoffs: \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  at Doge \u8211\'20\'13 a timeline\b0\par\par\uc2 Nick Robins-Early and Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 1,456 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 May 2025\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Trump adviser\u8217\'20\'19s time as a special government employee has ended. We look back on his tenure\par \par \uc2 In his 130 days as a special government employee, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man slashed his way through federal agencies, laying off government employees and gaining access to data that will underpin a dismantling of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in the Trump administration is without modern precedent. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at some key moments in the brief tenure Musk had as a federal employee.\par \par \uc2 20 January\par \par \uc2 Inauguration and an infamous salute\par \par \uc2 Musk is at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s side, as are a host of other tech billionaires, as he is inaugurated. He also issues an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/21/elon-musk-nazi-roman-salute-difference-trump-inauguration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparent fascist-style salute}}}\uc2  on stage at an inauguration celebration, twice.\par \par \uc2 20 January\par \par \uc2 Doge is created\par \par \uc2 The president issues an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/establishing-and-implementing-the-presidents-department-of-government-efficiency/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive order}}}\uc2  that creates Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D by renaming the \uc2 United States Digital Service\uc2  agency, which previously handled governmental tech issues. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order includes only a vague mandate to modernize government technology and increase efficiency, but within days it becomes clear Musk and his team have far more expansive aims.\par \par \uc2 January and February\par \par \uc2 Doge makes its way across government\par \par \uc2 Musk and Doge pop up at the offices of numerous government agencies, starting with the \uc2 General Services Administration\uc2 , to question federal employees and start gathering data and access to government systems.\par \par \uc2 28 January\par \par \uc2 Mass layoffs, \u8216\'20\'18fork in the road\u8217\'20\'19, and buyouts begin\par \par \uc2 Doge\u8217\'20\'19s early days make headlines for targeting masses of government workers with layoffs and pushing others to resign, with more than 2 million employees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/trump-federal-workers-buyouts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 receiving an email}}}\uc2  titled \u8220\'20\'1CFork in the road\u8221\'20\'1D that encourages staffers to take a buyout. The emails, which ask, \u8220\'20\'1CWhat did you accomplish this week?\u8221\'20\'1D become a signature of Musk and his new bureau, sent again and again whenever staff began to prey on a new herd of government employees.\par \par \uc2 Early February\par \par \uc2 USAID\uc2  is gutted and workers stand up to Musk\par \par \uc2 As Doge staffers storm into the \uc2 United States Agency for International Development\uc2  (\uc2 USAID\uc2 ) in early February, they find themselves in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/05/musk-doge-takeover-usaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heated standoff}}}\uc2  with security officials who try to bar them from accessing a secure room which holds sensitive and confidential data. The confrontation ends with \uc2 USAID\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top security official being put on administrative leave, while Doge gains access to its systems. With no one to stop them, Doge staffers begin the process of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/05/musk-doge-takeover-usaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hollowing out the agency}}}\uc2  that had once been the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest single supplier of humanitarian aid. More than 5,600 \uc2 USAID\uc2  workers around the world {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/musk-doge-usaid-firings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are fired}}}\uc2  in the ensuing weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe spent the weekend feeding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USAID}}}\uc2  into the wood chipper,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk boasts days later on X, his social media platform.\par \par \uc2 3 February\par \par \uc2 Musk says he deletes key government software creator\par \par \uc2 Musk tells a rightwing influencer on X that the GSA\u8217\'20\'19s 18F office, which helped build software projects such as the \uc2 IRS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s free tax filing service, was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeleted\u8221\'20\'1D in response to an inaccurate post accusing the group of being radical leftists.\par \par \uc2 13 February\par \par \uc2 Musk says he needs to \u8216\'20\'18delete\u8217\'20\'19 government agencies\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do need to delete entire agencies,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/13/elon-musk-doge-delete-agencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tells}}}\uc2  attenders at a World Governments Summit in Dubai. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t remove the roots of the weed, then it\u8217\'20\'19s easy for the weed to grow back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 13 February\par \par \uc2 Probationary workers are fired\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/13/elon-musk-doge-delete-agencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 orders agencies to fire thousands}}}\uc2  of probationary workers \u8211\'20\'13 a designation that applies to employees who have been at their jobs for less than a year, including those who may have been recently promoted. Other workers soon receive an email from Doge that demand they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/24/elon-musk-federal-workers-chaos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 list five things}}}\uc2  they did last week or face termination, a chaotic request that also turns out to be an empty threat. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/23/elon-musk-tells-us-federal-workers-to-explain-what-they-achieved-last-week-or-be-fired"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cabinet officials}}}\uc2  privately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/04/21/doge-musk-trump-federal-employees-emails/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deem it nonsensical}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 15 February\par \par \uc2 Protesters target \uc2 Tesla\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tesla\uc2  takedown\u8221\'20\'1D protest movement and boycott starts taking off, targeting Musk\u8217\'20\'19s car company with protests at dealerships. A protest on this date in New York City at a showroom has a solid turnout.\par \par \uc2 23 February\par \par \uc2 Musk gloats at conservative conference\par \par \uc2 At the Conservative Political Action Conference (CPAC), Musk stands on stage in a black Maga hat, sunglasses and gold chain, gleefully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/23/cpac-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wielding a chainsaw}}}\uc2  that was gifted to him by Javier Milei, the rightwing Argentinian president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis chainsaw is for bureaucracy!\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CI am become meme.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 1 March\par \par \uc2 18F workers laid off\par \par \uc2 In the middle of the night, workers at 18F are notified that they will be laid off en masse.\par \par \uc2 Early March\par \par \uc2 Courts start to block some Doge actions\par \par \uc2 Court cases filed earlier in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term begin producing rulings that curtail Doge\u8217\'20\'19s layoffs and temporarily block its access to data. Judges rule that the Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/13/federal-court-orders-fired-workers-doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 needs to reinstate}}}\uc2  probationary workers they fired, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/mar/20/musk-doge-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limit some Doge access}}}\uc2  to databases at agencies such as the \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/13/elon-musk-doge-court-ruling-records"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 order Musk\u8217\'20\'19s team}}}\uc2  to turn over internal records it had been seeking to keep private.\par \par \uc2 Mid-March\par \par \uc2 Health department slashed\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/04/rfk-jr-doge-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announces}}}\uc2  it is cutting 10,000 jobs to align with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order on Doge. In a display of the chaos that Doge had inspired, the US health secretary, Robert F Kennedy Jr, weeks later admits about 2,000 of those workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/04/rfk-jr-doge-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were fired in error}}}\uc2  and would need to be reinstated.\par \par \uc2 Mid-March\par \par \uc2 White House tries to salvage \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reputation\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Tesla\uc2  protests are working \u8211\'20\'13 stocks are falling. In response, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/11/trump-tesla-boycott-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump appears}}}\uc2  on the White House driveway in front of several parked Teslas, telling reporters he is going to buy one of them and praising Musk as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpatriot\u8221\'20\'1D. Others in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orbit, including the Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , also post sales pitches for the automaker.\par \par \uc2 20 March\par \par \uc2 Musk attacks courts as they try to curb administrative actions\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to court rulings against Trump is a constant stream of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/mar/22/elon-musk-doge-judges-usaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacks against the judicial system}}}\uc2  on X, which include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/07/republicans-trump-musk-attacks-us-judges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands}}}\uc2  that lawmakers \u8220\'20\'1Cimpeach the judges\u8221\'20\'1D and claims there is a \u8220\'20\'1Cjudicial coup\u8221\'20\'1D under way against Trump. Musk repeatedly amplifies far-right influencers saying the US should emulate El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s strongman president, \uc2 Nayib Bukele\uc2 , whose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/21/fears-for-democracy-in-el-salvador-after-president-claims-to-be-coolest-dictator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 party ousted}}}\uc2  supreme court judges in 2021 in a slide toward authoritarianism.\par \par \uc2 30 March\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and Musk protests builds steam around the world\par \par \uc2 A fully fledged international protest movement against \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and Musk is building. Thousands of people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/feb/16/protesters-target-tesla-stores-in-us-over-elon-musks-cost-cutting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gather at showrooms}}}\uc2  from Sydney to San Francisco in a day of action, with organizers stating that \u8220\'20\'1Churting \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is stopping Musk\u8221\'20\'1D. Vandalism against \uc2 Tesla\uc2  dealerships, charging stations and cars also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/mar/15/vandalized-tesla-elon-musk-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intensifies around the world}}}\uc2 , including multiple {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2025/mar/27/tesla-bombing-suspect-las-vegas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 molotov cocktail attacks}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/mar/05/leftwing-vulkan-group-claim-responsibility-tesla-factory-pylon-arson-attack-berlin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 incidents of arson}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump and Musk call the attacks domestic terrorism, while Pam Bondi, the attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://amp.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/20/charges-tesla-violent-destruction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vows to crack down}}}\uc2  on anyone targeting \uc2 Tesla\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 1 April\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin supreme court race delivers Musk rebuke\par \par \uc2 Musk poured money into a Wisconsin supreme court race that would have tilted the swing state\u8217\'20\'19s high court toward conservatives. He and his groups spent more than $20m on this race, including a giveaway of $1m checks on stage. Susan Crawford, the Democrat, wins the race handily, showing Musk\u8217\'20\'19s money couldn\u8217\'20\'19t buy everything.\par \par \uc2 22 April\par \par \uc2 Poor \uc2 Tesla\uc2  performance forces Musk to refocus\par \par \uc2 A first-quarter earnings call reveals \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s performance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/apr/22/tesla-sales-musk-white-house-exit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was even worse}}}\uc2  than expectations, with a 71% drop in profits and 9% drop in revenue year over year. Musk announces he will spend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/apr/22/tesla-sales-musk-white-house-exit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly less time}}}\uc2  working on Doge starting some time in May.\par \par \uc2 30 April\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s hat performance at cabinet meeting\par \par \uc2 In a cabinet meeting, Musk puts on two literal hats \u8211\'20\'13 a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark Maga\u8221\'20\'1D hat covered by a \u8220\'20\'1CGulf of America\u8221\'20\'1D hat. After Trump compliments the double-caps, Musk jokes: \u8220\'20\'1CThey say I wear a lot of hats\u8221\'20\'1D. This is potentially Musk\u8217\'20\'19s final cabinet meeting.\par \par \uc2 May\par \par \uc2 Musk starts to fade from political limelight\par \par \uc2 May finds a less vocal Musk than the aggressive tone he took the rest of the year, providing fuel for protests and lost revenue for \uc2 Tesla\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 27 May\par \par \uc2 Musk starts to signal departure from Trump\par \par \uc2 As Congress debates Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D that would slash government services, Musk says he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/elon-musk-disappointed-by-trump-big-beautiful-bill-doge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disappointed}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D by the bill because it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t cut enough on domestic policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think a bill can be big or it can be beautiful. But I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if it can be both,\u8221\'20\'1D he tells \uc2 CBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 30 May\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s exit leaves government permanently changed\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s time as a special government employee comes to an end, capping off the 130 days he is allowed to serve in this role.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250530el5u001e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
