\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Stock markets rise around the world after Trump tariffs blocked by US court \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Almeida \par \uc2 4,594 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 May 2025\par 14:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US market follows European and Asian stocks higher after<a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/28/us-court-blocks-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/28/us-court-blocks-trump-tariffs}}}\uc2 "> a federal court blocks Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18liberation day\u8217\'20\'19 tariffs</a>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T14:13:10.146Z">3.13pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Closing post\par \par \uc2 Time to wrap up\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 A US trade court has ruled \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping tariffs regime illegal, after several lawsuits argued the President has exceeded his authority, left US trade policy dependent on his whims and unleashed economic chaos.\par \par \uc2 The three-judge panel said they were not passing judgment on the \u8220\'20\'1Cwisdom or likely effectiveness of the president\u8217\'20\'19s use of tariffs as leverage\u8221\'20\'1D. Instead, their ruling centred on whether the trade levies had been legally applied in the first place. Their use was \u8220\'20\'1Cimpermissible not because it is unwise or ineffective, but because [federal law] does not allow it\u8221\'20\'1D, the decision explained.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets cheered the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, with the US dollar rallying against a basket of other currencies, although it has since pared back these gains. Stocks in rose the US on Thursday. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/28/us-court-blocks-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US federal court blocks Trump from imposing sweeping tariffs}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 However investors are still weighing whether the ruling from the trade court in New York will be enough to block Trump from pursuing his trade tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  think if the court ruling is upheld, Trump could pursue his other tariffs through the same means. They wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CIf the ruling did remain in place, preventing the use of tariffs under IEEPA, one option for the administration would be to expand the use of other tariff instruments, like the Section 232 on national security grounds, which have been used for autos, steel and aluminium tariffs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has claimed authority to set trade tariffs under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act, or \u8220\'20\'1CIEEPA\u8221\'20\'1D. The law has historically been used to impose sanctions on enemies of the US or freeze their assets. Trump is the first US president to use it to impose tariffs.\par \par \uc2 But the Court of International Trade in New York has said the US Constitution gives Congress exclusive authority to regulate commerce with other countries, and that is not overridden by the president\u8217\'20\'19s emergency powers.\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The UK has said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-68381ec58f08f86f308afa92#block-68381ec58f08f86f308afa92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it wants to accelerate negotiations to conclude a trade deal}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-6838599d8f085db8a3ae16bc#block-6838599d8f085db8a3ae16bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House adviser }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-6838599d8f085db8a3ae16bc#block-6838599d8f085db8a3ae16bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kevin Hassett}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-6838599d8f085db8a3ae16bc#block-6838599d8f085db8a3ae16bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has said three more trade deals are nearly done}}}\uc2 , and that the trade court ruling would not affect trade negotiations\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-68380df68f08ca2304a68c16#block-68380df68f08ca2304a68c16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Reeves}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-68380df68f08ca2304a68c16#block-68380df68f08ca2304a68c16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has said the government will push big pension funds to invest in British assets}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-6838148d8f08f86f308afa48&filterKeyEvents=false#liveblog-navigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-6838148d8f08f86f308afa48&filterKeyEvents=false#liveblog-navigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said he will leave his role in the Trump administration}}}\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T14:09:27.217Z">3.09pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 More than 60,000 low-paid workers have received back pay worth \u163\'00\'A37.4m after their employers failed to meet the legal minimum wage level.\par \par \uc2 Some of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent employers were caught out paying below the minimum wage, following investigations by \uc2 HM Revenue & Customs\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Pizza Express\uc2  , \uc2 British Airways\uc2  and the outsourcing firm \uc2 Capita\uc2  were among 518 businesses forced to pay wages that fell short of the minimum wage over a period of years.\par \par \uc2 German-owned supermarket chain \uc2 Lidl\uc2  and \uc2 Halfords\uc2  were also on a \u8220\'20\'1Cname and shame\u8221\'20\'1D list of culprits issued by the department for business and trade.\par \par \uc2 Capita\uc2  was the worst offender after it failed to pay \u163\'00\'A31.5m to 5,543 workers.\par \par \uc2 The investigations were conducted between 2015 and 2022, but have only recently been completed and back-payments agreed.\par \par \uc2 Last year the previous Conservative administration said a separate group of 524 businesses had failed to pay the minimum wage affecting 172,000 workers, giving rise to a \u163\'00\'A316m back-pay bill.\par \par \uc2 Minister for Employment Rights, Justin Madders said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no excuse for employers to undercut their workers, and we will continue to name companies who break the law and don\u8217\'20\'19t pay their employees what they are owed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The National Living Wage for workers aged 21 and over rose in April from \u163\'00\'A311.44 an hour to \u163\'00\'A312.21 an hour.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T13:42:06.747Z">2.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the US market, shares in the cosmetics business Elf Beauty are up by about 30% , after the company announced last night that it agreed to buy Hailey Bieber \u8217\'20\'19s beauty brand, Rhode , in a $1bn deal.\par \par \uc2 Hailey Bieber, the model wife of pop singer Justin Bieber, launched the company three years ago. It reported $212m worth in net sales in the 12 months ended in March.\par \par \uc2 Bieber said she would \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue as founder and step into an expanded role of chief creative officer and head of innovation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T13:37:08.630Z">2.37pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US stocks rise after court block on tariffs and \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  results\par \par \uc2 US stocks have risen at the opening bell in New York, with the blue chip S&P 500 index up 0.8%, after a federal court blocked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-683835328f0823849b10c822#block-683835328f0823849b10c822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nvidia reported a 69% rise in quarterly revenue}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The tech heavy Nasdaq index rose 1.5%, and shares in \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  bounced by 5.6% in early trading.\par \par \uc2 It is not clear whether the rally will last today as investors weigh whether Trump will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-683803ff8f08ca2304a68bc5#block-683803ff8f08ca2304a68bc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still pursue tariffs through means outside the International Emergency Economic Powers Act}}}\uc2  (IIEEPA).\par \par \uc2 The US dollar, which initially rallied strongly on news of the court ruling, has now fallen against a basket of other major currencies by 0.45%.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T13:01:43.791Z">2.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 White House adviser confident tariff ruling will be overturned\par \par \uc2 Economic adviser to the White House Kevin Hassett has said he is confident the trade court ruling that blocked most of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade tariffs will be overruled.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2 , he said:\par \par \uc2 If there are little hiccups here or there because of decisions that activist judges make, then it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t just concern you at all, and it\u8217\'20\'19s certainly not going to affect the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 He added that three more trade deals \u8220\'20\'1Cbasically look like they\u8217\'20\'19re done\u8221\'20\'1D, though he did not specify which countries.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T12:56:27.546Z">1.56pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US economy shrank at start of year\par \par \uc2 The US economy shrank in the first quarter of the year, with gross domestic product decreasing by 0.2%, according to the second estimate released from the \uc2 Bureau of Economic Analysis\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/apr/30/economy-gdp-q1-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It first estimated that GDP had fallen by 0.3%.}}}\par \par \uc2 The fall was driven partly by weaker consumer spending and an increase in imports as Americans bought foreign goods before tariffs came into effect.\par \par \uc2 The estimated 0.2% drop from January to March is the first contraction in three years and puts the US on the brink of a technical recession, defined by two quarters of negative growth.\par \par \uc2 Separate data showed filings for US jobless claims rose last week. Jobless benefits applications rose by 14,000 to 240,000 for the week ending 24 May, according to the \uc2 US Labor Department\uc2 . Analysts had forecast 226,000 new applications. <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lisaabramowicz1/status/1928067913472184605"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/lisaabramowicz1/status/1928067913472184605}}}\uc2 ">\par \par \uc2 US continuing jobless claims have risen to the highest level since 2021. It's taking longer for people to get jobs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vW2cKhV7Jv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vW2cKhV7Jv}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Abramowicz (@lisaabramowicz1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lisaabramowicz1/status/1928067913472184605?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 29, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T13:20:45.834Z">at 2.20pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T11:12:26.286Z">12.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Closer to home, there are some new figures today on the rate of inflation experienced by British households.\par \par \uc2 Overall UK household costs rose by 2.6% in the year to March, according to the \uc2 Office for National Statistics\uc2 . That marks a deceleration from 2.9% in the year to December 2024.\par \par \uc2 Private renters experienced the biggest rise in costs, with these households experiencing the highest annual inflation rate of 3.6% in March. Meanwhile households who owned their homes experienced an inflation rate of 1.8%, and those with a mortgage had a rate of 2.8%.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T10:53:42.832Z">11.53am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The White House is also under pressure from rising interest rates on US debt. Last week the lower house in Congress passed a tax bill funded largely by extra borrowings. It is estimated the giveaways will add $5tn to US debt levels.\par \par \uc2 Olivier Blanchard\uc2  , an economics professor at the Massachussetts Institute of Technology and a former chief economist at the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  , said the tax bill had spooked investors, and especially those that wanted to buy bonds that last 10 or 30 years, concerned that they might not get their money back.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I were an investor, i would worry about buying a thirty year maturity treasury [bond], because god knows what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Bloomberg News.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would buy a one year [bond] because there\u8217\'20\'19s not much risk. I mean, even if I think that the [tax] policy is crazy, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to get my money back after one year. But if I buy a 10 year, I start saying, yeah, things could happen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, the utter fiscal irresponsibility of this administration is clearly what explains higher rates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T10:56:03.603Z">at 11.56am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T10:39:44.825Z">11.39am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  results push European tech stocks higher\par \par \uc2 Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-683807038f08ca2304a68bd5#block-683807038f08ca2304a68bd5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bumper set of quarterly results from Nvidia}}}\uc2  has rippled over to the European stock markets too. Shares in the Dutch semiconductor equipment maker ASML have risen by 2.4% today, and the Stoxx Europe tech index has risen by 0.8%.\par \par \uc2 Over in the US, futures for the tech-heavy Nasdaq were up by as much as 2%, and shares in \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  itself are up 6% in pre-market trading.\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , another leader in artificial intelligence technology, are also up 2.6%. Last night its chief executive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-blocked-by-us-court-stock-markets-rise-in-asia-news-economics-business-live?page=with%3Ablock-6837fd8e8f08f86f308af98e#block-6837fd8e8f08f86f308af98e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk announced he will leave his role in the Trump administration}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T09:50:16.764Z">10.50am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The chief executive of \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown\uc2 , \uc2 Dan Olley\uc2 , is leaving the investment broker after less than two years in the top job.\par \par \uc2 Richard Flint\uc2  , an independent non-executive director, will act as chief executive on an interim basis, subject to approval from the City regulator.\par \par \uc2 Olley will remain in post for a three-month handover period, and be available to the business for a further two months, \uc2 Hargreaves\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Last year the company agreed to a \u163\'00\'A35.4bn takeover by a consortium of private equity firms.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T13:53:46.793Z">at 2.53pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T09:14:04.607Z">10.14am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 More scepticism arriving today as investors weigh whether the ruling from the trade court in New York will be enough to block Trump from pursuing his trade tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Mark Haefele\uc2  , chief investment officer at UBS Global Wealth Management , said:\par \par \uc2 In our view, tariffs are unlikely to disappear completely, as the administration could rebuild some of its tariff agenda through certain sections of the Trade Act of 1974. For investors, we continue to highlight volatility in the near term as more headlines emerge.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile analysts Joachim Klement and Susana Cruz , of the broker Panmure Liberum , say the likelihood oof tariffs being cancelled has increased but is not their \u8220\'20\'1Cbase case\u8221\'20\'1D. They wrote:\par \par \uc2 Indeed, we expect that tariffs have been delayed, but not cancelled. Instead, the Trump administration will likely use other legal authorities like Section 301 of the Trade Act to impose similar tariffs, but with a slower and more deliberate approach.\par \par \uc2 This means that on the one hand, extreme tariffs and rapidly changing tariffs are less likely to happen going forward, which reduces uncertainty somewhat.\par \par \uc2 But in the short term, the court ruling, and the subsequent legal challenges will add significant uncertainty to the mix, making it even harder for US businesses to plan their capex and thus reduce US GDP growth due to a decline in investment activity.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T09:21:44.691Z">at 10.21am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T08:55:41.767Z">9.55am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 UK seeks to accelerate US trade deal\par \par \uc2 The UK has said it wants to accelerate negotiations to conclude a trade deal with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the wake of the US court ruling that the sweeping tariffs he imposed on imports from more than 60 countries were illegal.\par \par \uc2 Despite \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  sealing the first deal with Trump since his so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cliberation day\u8221\'20\'1D at the start of April no legal text exists to bring the concessions he won into force.\par \par \uc2 The UK is also still threatened with a 10% reciprocal tariff on all exports outside the deal which was seen as a life saver for the car and steel industries.\par \par \uc2 The business secretary, Jonathan Reynolds , is expected to meet US commerce secretary Howard Lutnick at a meeting of the \uc2 OECD\uc2  in Paris next Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UK government\uc2  spokesperson played down the US court ruling on Thursday plainly indicating it would continue to negotiate despite a technical opening to walk away from the deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are matters for the United States to determine domestically and we note this is only the first stage of legal proceedings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were the first country to secure a deal with the US in a move to protect jobs across key sectors, from autos to steel, and we are working to ensure that businesses can benefit from the deal as quickly as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 Trade experts have said the US court\u8217\'20\'19s verdict just added more uncertainty to the global markets already heavily disrupted by the volatility of US trade policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis court ruling doesn\u8217\'20\'19t affect the tariffs that the UK negotiated down on cars and steel, but clearly adds another layer of complexity and uncertainty to what Trump is doing when businesses don\u8217\'20\'19t know what tariffs their product would face in the US that can\u8217\'20\'19t be good for the economy,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 David Henig\uc2  , director of think tank European Centre for International Political Economy .\par \par \uc2 The EU is also in the middle of tense trade negotiations with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration following last week\u8217\'20\'19s threat to impose tariffs of 50% on all exports. It was already facing a 20% tariff on all exports as well as sectoral tariffs on autos and steel and aluminium, with both sides pausing measures and counter measures for 90 days until the beginning of July.\par \par \uc2 Its lead negotiator \uc2 Maro\u353\'01\'61 \u352\'01\'60ef\u269\'01\'0Dovi\u269\'01\'0D\uc2  is also expected to meet with US commerce secretary Howard Lutnick in Paris next week at the \uc2 OECD\uc2  council meeting with EU sources saying a call between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Sunday with \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  unlocking a route to proper negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T09:33:55.646Z">at 10.33am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T08:41:18.096Z">9.41am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Also in the UK, some bleak figures from the car manufacturing industry, where production hit its lowest monthly output in more than 70 years.\par \par \uc2 Car and commercial vehicle production dropped 15.8% to 59,203 in April, according to figures from the \uc2 Society of Motor Manufacturers and Traders\uc2  (SMMT). Monthly vehicle output has not been that low since 1952, excluding 2020 when the pandemic shut down most manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 The decline was because of a late Easter, SMMT said, as well as \u8220\'20\'1Cmodel changeovers and lower demand in key export markets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T08:26:03.816Z">9.26am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The UK looks like it is losing out on the broader rally in Europe , with the FTSE 100 index down slightly by 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 The online car marketplace \uc2 Auto Trader\uc2  is at the bottom of the index, with shares down by 12%. It reported a 5% rise in revenue to \u163\'00\'A3601m in the year ended in March, below analyst expectations of \u163\'00\'A3606m.\par \par \uc2 Demand for used cars has been very strong, but that has been a problem for \uc2 Auto Trader\uc2 . Analysts at the broker \uc2 Peel Hunt\uc2  write:\par \par \uc2 The resilient car market has created headwinds for \uc2 Auto Trader\uc2 , as the\par \par \uc2 accelerated speed of vehicle sales on its platform weighs on ARPR [average revenue per retailer] growth.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T08:27:10.676Z">at 9.27am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T08:07:57.770Z">9.07am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Investors are watching the US dollar , which is currently up 0.1% against a basket of leading currencies and is one of the top performers in the G10 forex market today, says \uc2 Kathleen Brooks\uc2  , a research director at the broker XTB .\par \par \uc2 Sell the dollar was one of the biggest \u8216\'20\'18tariff trades\u8217\'20\'19, so now that tariffs are in jeopardy, an unwind of this position is to be expected.\par \par \uc2 However, for now, the focus is on a recovery in USD/JPY, and losses in the euro and the pound vs. the dollar have been minimal so far.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T07:57:41.776Z">8.57am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Rachel Reeves\uc2  to push big pension funds to back British assets\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the \uc2 UK government\uc2  has said it will require the biggest pension funds in the country to invest in British assets.\par \par \uc2 It \u8220\'20\'1Cwill take a reserve power in the Pension Schemes Bill to set binding asset allocation targets\u8221\'20\'1D for investments in private makets, the Treasury said on Thursday. It will also secure \u163\'00\'A327.5bn for \u8220\'20\'1Clocal investment priorities\u8221\'20\'1D for Local Government Pension Scheme authorities.\par \par \uc2 The government also confirmed plans to pool multiple pension funds into bigger \u8216\'20\'18megafunds\u8217\'20\'19 which manage \u163\'00\'A325bn or more in assets. It aims to consolidate the 86 administering LGPS authorities into six pools.\par \par \uc2 The Labour government has been reviewing ways to overhaul the private pension system. In May, Reeves ruled out mandating that pension funds must allocate money to British assets, after 17 pension bosses signed up to a voluntary agreement to invest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/13/uk-pension-funds-investment-british-firms-mansion-house-accord"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 5% of their assets in UK private markets.}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T08:00:59.811Z">at 9.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T07:28:36.822Z">8.28am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Davos founder launches criminal complaint against accusers, according to a report from the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Klaus Schwab, the founder of the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2 , has reportedly launched a criminal complaint against the whistleblowers whose accusations led to his ousting.\par \par \uc2 Schwab founded the WEF in 1971 but stepped down in April after the board launched an investigation after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/apr/24/wef-launches-investigation-into-founder-klaus-schwab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whistleblowers reportedly accused him of manipulating research, using company funds to pay for private massages, and asking junior staff to withdraw thousands of dollars on his behalf}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Financial Times\uc2  reports this morning that Schwab said he would fight the \u8220\'20\'1Cstupid and constructed\u8221\'20\'1D allegations, and that his lawyers had filed a complaint for defamation and coercion with the public prosecutor in Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T07:15:59.160Z">8.15am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 European markets rally after Trump tariff ruling\par \par \uc2 Stock markets across Europe are rallying this morning as investors wake up to news that a trade court in New York has blocked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cliberation day\u8221\'20\'1D tariffs.\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s FTSE 100 blue chip index has ticked up 0.1%, while the German Dax rallied 0.9%. France\u8217\'20\'19s CAC 40 has risen 1%.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T07:08:33.256Z">8.08am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Tariffs are dominating the headlines this morning but some of the market optimism has also come from \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 , which reported its first quarter results last night.\par \par \uc2 The chip designer, which has been at the heart of the AI spending boom, reported a 69% surge in revenue to $44.1bn in its quarter ended on 27 April, higher than expected.\par \par \uc2 The ompany has projected revenue of $45bn in the second quarter, meeting analyst forecasts even as it said that restriction on shipments of AI chips to China would cost it $8bn in sales.\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  were up 4.9% in after-hours trading. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/28/nvidia-q1-2025-earnings-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nvidia beats Wall Street expectations even as Trump tamps down China sales}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T07:37:12.346Z">at 8.37am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T07:00:41.241Z">8.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Tariffs on autos, steel and aluminium remain in place\par \par \uc2 The court in the US was not asked to address some industry-specific Trump has issued on cars, steel and aluminium under a different statute.\par \par \uc2 But analysts at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  think if the court ruling is upheld, Trump could pursue his other tariffs through the same means. They wrote:\par \par \uc2 If the ruling did remain in place, preventing the use of tariffs under IEEPA, one option for the administration would be to expand the use of other tariff instruments, like the Section 232 on national security grounds, which have been used for autos, steel and aluminium tariffs.\par \par \uc2 But this is clearly a setback for their tariff strategy, and it\u8217\'20\'19s also going to complicate its current attempts to negotiate concessions from trading partners, given the possibility the tariffs might not come into force once the 90-day extension period is over.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T07:01:53.498Z">at 8.01am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T06:45:27.856Z">7.45am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Court ruling might not change final outcome for big US trading partners, says Goldman analyst\par \par \uc2 Even with the court action, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade policies could still affect other big economies, analysts are warning.\par \par \uc2 Alec Phillips , an analyst at the investment bank \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  , wrote:\par \par \uc2 This ruling represents a setback for the administration\u8217\'20\'19s tariff plans and increases uncertainty but might not change the final outcome for most major U.S. trading partners.\par \par \uc2 Trump has claimed authority to set trade tariffs under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act, or \u8220\'20\'1CIEEPA\u8221\'20\'1D. The law has historically been used to impose sanctions on enemies of the US or freeze their assets. Trump is the first US president to use it to impose tariffs.\par \par \uc2 But the Court of International Trade, which is in New York, has said the US Constitution gives Congress exclusive authority to regulate commerce with other countries, and that is not overridden by the president\u8217\'20\'19s emergency powers.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T06:34:19.495Z">7.34am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk announces he will leave his role in Trump administration\par \par \uc2 It has been busy in the US overnight. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has said he will leave his role in the Trump administration. <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1927877957852266518"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1927877957852266518}}}\uc2 ">\par \par \uc2 As my scheduled time as a Special Government Employee comes to an end, I would like to thank President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  for the opportunity to reduce wasteful spending.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DOGE?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DOGE}}}\uc2  mission will only strengthen over time as it becomes a way of life throughout the government.\u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1927877957852266518?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 29, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 The billionaire boss of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has played a leading role at the department of government efficiency, or \u8220\'20\'1CDOGE\u8221\'20\'1D. His 130-day mandate as a special government employee in the Trump administration was set to expire about 30 May.\par \par \uc2 He had already been signalling his departure from Washington and a commitment to refocus on his businesses. He also criticised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new tax bill, calling it too expensive and a measure that would undermine his work to make the government more efficient. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/29/elon-musk-announces-exit-from-us-government-role-after-breaking-with-trump-on-tax-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk announces exit from US government role after breaking with Trump on tax bill}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T06:21:45.915Z">7.21am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Investors say stock markets will rally but 'not the end of the tariff story'\par \par \uc2 Hopes that tariffs might be blocked has helped lift stocks in Asia, but there is likely to be much more uncertainty ahead, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Prashant Newnaha\uc2  , senior Asia-Pacific rates strategist, at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  , said:\par \par \uc2 The knee-jerk reaction for equities to rally and bond yields to back up on the tariff pause makes sense.\par \par \uc2 However, with tariffs now in the appeal process and likely heading to the Supreme Court, uncertainty is back. Expect to see this lead to delays in investment and hiring. The pause also puts tariff revenue at risk which could bring deficit issues back on the radar.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Gary Ng , senior economist at \uc2 Natixis\uc2  , says:\par \par \uc2 The decision will fuel temporary risk-on sentiment in equities and lower bond yields as the market dials back inflation expectations driven by tariffs.\par \par \uc2 However, this is not the end of the tariff story. There is no clarity as the legal battle will continue and it does not change the fact that Trump will find ways to reshape global trade order.\par \par \uc2 Yunosuke Ikeda , head of macro research at \uc2 Nomura\uc2  , said:\par \par \uc2 At this point it\u8217\'20\'19s almost impossible to know if the tariffs will be completely unwound by this. But in the hypothetical situation that they are, it\u8217\'20\'19s natural to see dollar appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Basically Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs will lead to stagflation pressure on the U.S. economy, so reversing those tariffs would be a positive for the dollar.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-29T06:09:05.400Z">7.09am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Introduction: Trump tariffs blocked by US court in New York\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 A federal court in the US has blocked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from imposing sweeping trade tariffs under an emergency powers law.\par \par \uc2 A three-judge panel at the court of international trade argued that Trump has exceeded his authority, left US trade policy dependent on his whims and unleashed economic chaos.\par \par \uc2 The court wrote:\par \par \uc2 The Worldwide and Retaliatory Tariff Orders exceed any authority granted to the President by IEEPA to regulate importation by means of tariffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26The court does not pass upon the wisdom or likely effectiveness of the president\u8217\'20\'19s use of tariffs as leverage. That use is impermissible not because it is unwise or ineffective, but because [federal law] does not allow it.\par \par \uc2 There are reports that the Trump administration has filed a notice of appeal. White House officials have already publicly challenged the court\u8217\'20\'19s authority n the case. A White House spokesperson told Reuters that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot for elected judges to decide how to properly address a national emergency\u8221\'20\'1D. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/28/us-court-blocks-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US federal court blocks Trump from imposing sweeping tariffs}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 News that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs may be unlawful was welcomed by stock markets in Asia. In Japan the Nikkei 225 index rallied by 1.9%, while in China the SSE Composite rose by 0.8% and Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s Hang Seng rose by 1.1%. The South Korean Kospi index rallied by 1.8%.\par \par \uc2 In the UK, the blue chip FTSE 100 index is also poised to rise when markets open at 8am, with futures up 0.82%.\par \par \uc2 The agenda\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9:30AM BST: ONS estimates of inflation for different household types\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1:30PM BST: Second reading of US GDP\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1:30PM BST: US weekly jobless claims\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-29T06:28:42.111Z">at 7.28am BST</time> \par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250529el5t000us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
