\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I have to worry each month\u8217\'20\'19: social security cuts incite fears of payment disruptions\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,135 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 May 2025\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Agency has been significant target of Doge while nearly 69 million Americans receive benefits\par \par \uc2 Retiree and disability beneficiaries are worried about delays in payments, processing and services amid cuts being made to the US\u8217\'20\'19s social security system under the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Angel Morgan, a 44-year-old disability benefits recipient in Nashville, Tennessee, said she felt like she was \u8220\'20\'1Crunning in circles\u8221\'20\'1D navigating long lines at her local social security office and difficulties in trying to make an appointment online to talk about her benefits and how to participate in the Ticket to Work program, which provides career development services for disability beneficiaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI struggle with social settings and these things just make it worse. Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about the struggles we go through and won\u8217\'20\'19t quit until we are all bankrupt and either dead or wanting to die,\u8221\'20\'1D said Morgan.\par \par \uc2 An average of nearly 69 million Americans will receive social security benefits a month in 2025, most of them older people or those with disabilities.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/06/musk-doge-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agency}}}\uc2  has been a significant target of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) and its former leader \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has called social security \u8220\'20\'1Cthe biggest Ponzi scheme of all time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Attacks on social security are not new \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans have long {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/heritage-foundation/heritage-foundation-gunning-your-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed }}}\uc2 to privatize social security and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/raising-the-retirement-age-for-social-security-would-cut-benefits-by-thousands-of-dollars-each-year/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raise}}}\uc2  the retirement age to 69 years old \u8211\'20\'13 but the latest salvoes are having a profound impact on the agency and those who rely upon it.\par \par \uc2 The office of the inspector general, the watchdog of the \uc2 Social Security Administration (SSA)\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oig.ssa.gov/news-releases/2024-08-08-record-breaking-backlog-increases-improper-payments-by-over-1b/#:~:text=As%20a%20backlog%20of%20payment,%241.1%20billion%20in%20improper%20payments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  in late 2024 of staffing shortages causing record backlogs and improper payments due to the lack of staff available to address the backlogs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike most, I am concerned with the future of social security. With the limited employees, both in numbers and experience, there is no way that SSA can function,\u8221\'20\'1D said a longtime retired SSA employee and consultant for the agency who requested to remain anonymous.\par \par \uc2 According to the SSA, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ssa.gov/news/press/releases/2025/#2025-04-29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 3,500 employees}}}\uc2  have taken voluntary separation or buyout agreements, as the agency is seeking to cut staff by at least 7,000, to 50,000 workers, which will be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ssa.gov/policy/docs/statcomps/supplement/2022/2f1-2f3.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowest staffing}}}\uc2  at the agency in decades. The agency is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govexec.com/workforce/2025/04/dudek-calls-entire-ssa-offices-be-converted-new-schedule-f/404755/?oref=ge-topic-lander-featured-river"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planning}}}\uc2  to strip civil service protections from all employees in offices around the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis plan will dramatically impact the ability of SSA to timely process disability decisions, hearings, and appeals for claimants all over the country, who are already waiting too long,\u8221\'20\'1D said the American Federal Government Employees Social Security Administration general committee in a statement on the conversion plan.\par \par \uc2 The employee cuts have come amid a battle for Doge to gain data access and greater authority at the agency.\par \par \uc2 In March, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/mar/20/musk-doge-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court blocked}}}\uc2  Doge from gaining access to data at the \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2  containing the personal data of millions of Americans. The Trump administration is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fedscoop.com/doge-social-security-supreme-court/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently pushing }}}\uc2 for the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to weigh in and give Doge access.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for commissioner of the SSA, \uc2 Frank Bisignano\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.finance.senate.gov/chairmans-news/wyden-opposes-bisignano-nomination-to-lead-social-security-ahead-of-floor-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  been involved in Doge\u8217\'20\'19s actions at the agency and is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/social-security-frank-bisginano-doge-elon-musk-38760fac2a0fe244e86b741938db0363"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-professed}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CDoge person\u8221\'20\'1D. Bisignano was confirmed by the Senate this month. Doge\u8217\'20\'19s actions at the agency have included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/social-security-offices-closures-doge-trump-b2b1a5b2ba4fb968abc3379bf90715ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelling }}}\uc2 leases for dozens of social security offices across the US.\par \par \uc2 In interviews with the Guardian, social security beneficiaries reported already experiencing delays and increased fears they will be denied benefits or not receive payments they depend on to survive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo far my disability payment has shown up on time, but I sit on pins and needles each month waiting to see if it will,\u8221\'20\'1D said a 65-year-old disability recipient in Virginia who requested to remain anonymous. \u8220\'20\'1CYou just barely survive with just social security. That\u8217\'20\'19s why it would be immediately life-changing for so many of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Morgan also said her benefits were not enough to barely survive amid rising costs of living.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo be told that we may lose our benefits, and if we complain, means we are fraudsters, that stings. We depend on these checks to pay rent, buy food, medicine and gas,\u8221\'20\'1D Morgan added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have the means to sell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/apr/24/donald-trumps-meme-coin-value-surges-after-gala-dinner-invites"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meme coins}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gettrumpsneakers.com/?srsltid=AfmBOopuXoU6pq0zYKq7S5-w0GP0Fnh3wXzdyI2ByGRVb6APBKRC9dnY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gold shoes}}}\uc2  for donations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A 69-year-old retiree in California said they were still waiting on backpay and a benefit increase agreed in January 2025.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe cost of living is rapidly increasing and it\u8217\'20\'19s becoming increasingly difficult to make ends meet,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CI need this benefit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A 70-year-old retiree in Indiana said: \u8220\'20\'1CFor the first time in my life, my wife and I are stressed out and worried if I will get my payment and if it will be on time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Judi, an 85-year-old retiree in Washington, explained that she had never worried in the past 20 years whether her social security check would show up until recently.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery month since the beginning of this regime, I am concerned. Will my check be there? Will there be some excuse for the check not coming? Will they cut the amount? And who are these people who have access to my private information? Information that the \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2  always kept private,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Lorrie Bennett, 63, a disability benefits recipient in Louisville, Kentucky, said her payout date recently changed without notice and she was put on fraud alert to monitor her accounts over concerns about her data being compromised due to Doge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t know until the payment didn\u8217\'20\'19t show up. When I contacted the SS Administration they didn\u8217\'20\'19t see anything in the system showing the change,\u8221\'20\'1D Bennett said.\par \par \uc2 A 66-year-old retiree in Los Angeles said they were going to wait until age 70 to claim benefits but applied on 1 February this year, concerned about the Trump administration cutting benefits. \u8220\'20\'1CI was checking every few weeks to see when I would be approved, and on May 1, I saw that I was still not approved three months later,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 They called the SSA phone service line for assistance and were told the person handling their application had left the agency. \u8220\'20\'1CHad I not called, my application would still be in limbo,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 Arthur Gross, 72, of Woodside, New York, said he had been receiving socialsecurity retirement benefits for two years, but had delayed paying bills and switched out automatic bill payments due to uncertainty of receiving timely payments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow with the Trump and Musk destruction of federal agencies in general and social security in particular, I have to worry each month until my payment shows up,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gross.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2  did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250520el5k001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
