\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump pick for workplace safety agency sparks fears heat protections will be derailed\b0\par\par\uc2 Dharna Noor \par \uc2 1,402 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 May 2025\par 17:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Under David Keeling, a former UPS and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  executive, \uc2 Osha\uc2  is expected to thwart protections on extreme heat\par \par \uc2 As the US prepares for what could be another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.accuweather.com/en/weather-forecasts/summer-weather-forecast-for-the-us-in-2025/1768530"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record-breaking hot summer}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his pick to lead the nation\u8217\'20\'19s workplace safety agency are expected to derail the creation of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first-ever federal labor protections from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/extreme-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extreme heat}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump in February nominated David Keeling to lead the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration (Osha)\uc2 . Keeling formerly served as an executive at the \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  (UPS) and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 both of which have faced citations from Osha for worker injuries and deaths amid heat exposure. The companies deny the deaths were heat-related.\par \par \uc2 Under Keeling, Osha is expected to thwart heat protections. After years of pressure from organized labor, the agency in 2021 began working to create a federal heat standard, and last year rolled out a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/jul/02/biden-extreme-heat-proposaal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft rule}}}\uc2  aimed at requiring access to water, shade, breaks and training which the Biden administration estimated would protect 36 million workers.\par \par \uc2 But corporations have pushed to gut the rules, and there are concerns among safety advocates and some workers that Keeling could help them do so. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/14/trump-federal-layoffs-ripple-effect-us-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18So many are devastated\u8217\'20\'19: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s federal firings and their ripple effect}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Seth Pacic, a UPS delivery driver and union steward in Dallas, Texas, who has experienced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/aug/23/ups-delivery-workers-air-conditioning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heat exhaustion}}}\uc2  on the job, said he feared \u8220\'20\'1Cany meaningful policy to combat heat injuries will be put on hold while he holds the position\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Keeling served as the vice-president of global health and safety at UPS from 2018 to 2021, and as the director of road and transportation safety at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  from 2021 to 2023. Both companies have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/sep/07/ups-heat-death-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/24/amazon-delivery-service-partner-anti-union-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backlash}}}\uc2  for heat-related workplace incidents.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.levernews.com/workers-overheated-and-died-under-trumps-workplace-safety-nominee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent review of federal records}}}\uc2  by investigative outlet the Lever found that during Keeling\u8217\'20\'19s tenure, Osha fined the two companies a combined $2m for more than 300 workplace safety citations, including for heat-related incidents.\par \par \uc2 In the past decade, more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.osha.gov/severe-injury-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 170 UPS workers}}}\uc2  have been hospitalized due to heat exposure, including more than 50 during Keeling\u8217\'20\'19s tenure. And at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newjerseymonitor.com/briefs/lawsuit-seeks-records-related-to-amazon-worker-deaths/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://6abc.com/california-ups-driver-dies-signs-of-heatstroke-esteban-chavez-heat-related-deaths/12023790/#:~:text=UPS%20driver%20dies%20day%20after,believes%20it's%20linked%20to%20dehydration."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UPS}}}\uc2 , at least seven workers died after extreme heat exposure in recent years with at least three of those deaths occurring when Keeling was at the companies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/sep/07/ups-heat-death-texas#:~:text=On%206%20August%2C%2037%2Dyear,related%2C%20which%20UPS%20has%20denied"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Both companies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nj.com/middlesex/2024/11/amazon-workers-died-at-nj-warehouses-and-we-dont-know-enough-about-how-advocates-say.html#:~:text=Amazon%20officials%20called%20all%20three,to%20slacken%20workplace%20safety%20rules."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  any of the deaths were both heat-related and job-related.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are companies that are known to be not that great when it comes to dealing with extreme heat,\u8221\'20\'1D said Juley Fulcher, a worker health and safety advocate at consumer advocacy non-profit \uc2 Public Citizen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reached for comment, Courtney Parella, the spokesperson for the Department of Labor, Osha\u8217\'20\'19s parent agency, said: \u8220\'20\'1COsha\u8217\'20\'19s mission to protect workers\u8217\'20\'19 health and safety remains a clear priority for this administration. David Keeling was nominated to advance that mission and engage stakeholders thoughtfully on policy and rulemaking decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both UPS and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  defended their heat policies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/operations/how-amazon-keeps-employees-and-drivers-safe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon has said its practices }}}\uc2 meet state and federal requirements and, in some cases, go beyond them. UPS has said it has comprehensive training and protocols to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.ups.com/us/en/our-company/great-employer/5-ways-ups-is-improving-heat-safety-for-employees.html#:~:text=We've%20provided%20more%20than,up%20to%2017%20degrees%20F."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support employees}}}\uc2  which it is continuously working to improve.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt UPS, we focus on safety every day and always look for ways to improve. Over the past five years, we\u8217\'20\'19ve invested more than 33m hours and nearly $2bn on safety training,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becca Hunnicutt, a spokesperson for UPS. \u8220\'20\'1CWe report all recordable injuries to Osha and train our employees to seek immediate treatment if they recognize or report any signs or symptoms of heat stress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added that the company supplies materials including water, ice and electrolytes to employees and has partnered with various firms to train them on heat safety and provide them with cooling fabrics.\par \par \uc2 Sam Stephenson, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe take the health and safety of our employees incredibly seriously \u8230\'20\'26 For example, all of our fulfillment centers have climate-controlled systems that are monitored throughout the day; all of our \uc2 Amazon\uc2  branded delivery vehicles have air conditioning; and we\u8217\'20\'19ve invested $59m to insulate our vans to help reduce the internal temperatures for our delivery partners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the recent Lever reporting \u8220\'20\'1Coversimplifies complex issues and provides broad generalizations in an effort to purposefully mislead its readers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has not been cited for any heat-related deaths,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSafety is our top priority across all our operations and any implication, stated or otherwise, is false.\u8221\'20\'1D Though Osha did {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://warehouseworkers.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/KSBD-CalOSHA-Heat-Citations-01-31-24.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cite}}}\uc2 Amazon\uc2  for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.communityforwardredlands.com/amazon-cited-for-unsafe-working-condition-at-san-bernardino-warehouse/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heat-related conditions}}}\uc2 , he said the company has appealed.\par \par \uc2 In previous statements both UPS and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  have defended their heat policies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/operations/how-amazon-keeps-employees-and-drivers-safe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon has said its practices }}}\uc2 meet state and federal requirements and, in some cases, go beyond them. UPS has said it has comprehensive training and protocols to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.ups.com/us/en/our-company/great-employer/5-ways-ups-is-improving-heat-safety-for-employees.html#:~:text=We've%20provided%20more%20than,up%20to%2017%20degrees%20F."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support employees}}}\uc2  which it is continuously working to improve.\par \par \uc2 Keeling said he was unable to comment for the piece until he is confirmed by the Senate. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohsonline.com/articles/2021/06/02/three-things-to-learn-about-safety-from-front-line-employees.aspx?m=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a 2021 op-ed}}}\uc2 , he wrote that he began his work at UPS in 1985 as a package handler \u8211\'20\'13 a role which showed him the importance of \u8220\'20\'1Csafety and wellness\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as \u8220\'20\'1Csleep and hydration\u8221\'20\'1D. That experience informed his work as a safety executive, he wrote, encouraging him to \u8220\'20\'1Cseek out the input and perspective of frontline employees\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2 , which represents UPS employees and some \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers, endorsed Keeling\u8217\'20\'19s nomination over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tdu.org/ups-amazon-boss-nominated-to-head-osha"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissent}}}\uc2  from some members of the rank and file.\par \par \uc2 Heat protections\par \par \uc2 Federal health and safety experts first recommended Osha create a national heat standard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/IN11701"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 50 years ago}}}\uc2 . In the intervening years, US summers have warmed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/10/us-summer-temperatures-rising-climate-science#:~:text=How%20much%20warmer%20summer%202021%20was%20compared,have%20warmed%20by%202F%20(1C)%20or%20more."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly}}}\uc2  due to the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Labor estimates that more than 400 US workers died from heat-related causes between 2011 and 2021. Many experts believe that to be a vast understatement; \uc2 Public Citizen{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizen.org/wp-content/uploads/Boiling-Point-Public-Citizen-06-28-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimates}}}\uc2  the true number is up to 2,000 a year, with an additional 170,000 heat-related injuries and illnesses annually.\par \par \uc2 A federal heat standard, experts say, could drastically decrease those numbers. But Osha is under no obligation to finalize the rule under Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey could put it on a shelf and say, we\u8217\'20\'19re just not going to do anything with this,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fulcher.\par \par \uc2 Recent cuts to regulatory staff at Osha could make it difficult for the agency to finalize a rule \u8220\'20\'1Ceven if they wanted to\u8221\'20\'1D, said Jordan Barab, former deputy assistant secretary of labor at Osha from 2009 to 2017. But if it musters up the ability to work on the rule, the agency could gut it, Barab said.\par \par \uc2 Corporations, including UPS, have spent millions lobbying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/jul/31/heat-protections-workers-big-business-lobbies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against}}}\uc2  the standard. In public comments to Osha on the 2024 draft rule, many companies contested provisions that would mandate breaks for workers, trigger certain protections when the temperature crosses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.morganlewis.com/pubs/2024/07/osha-issues-landmark-proposed-heat-rule-for-indoor-and-outdoor-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 80F and 90F}}}\uc2 , and require that new and returning workers face limited heat exposure.\par \par \uc2 A weakened final rule could also exempt certain workers and workplaces, Barab said.\par \par \uc2 Osha will host a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.osha.gov/news/newsreleases/osha-trade-release/20250416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public hearing}}}\uc2  on the federal heat standard next month.\par \par \uc2 Confirmation pending\par \par \uc2 Keeling\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearing has yet to be scheduled. During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, the Senate never brought his nominee for Osha head up for a vote. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/06/trump-niosh-worker-safety-group"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump is dismantling a key worker safety group. It\u8217\'20\'19s another betrayal of the working class | Devan Hawkins}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 If given the opportunity, Senators should press the nominee on potential \u8220\'20\'1Cfavoritism\u8221\'20\'1D toward UPS and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , said Fulcher.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s always a potential question about conflict when someone is regulating companies where they worked,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd these are two huge, massive companies that employ hundreds of thousands of people and are going to certainly be the subject of a lot of complaints.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senators should ask Keeling questions \u8220\'20\'1Cwith workers in mind\u8221\'20\'1D, said Antoine Andrews, who has worked at UPS in Brooklyn, New York, for 29 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope they think of the hardworking people getting up every day to support themselves and their loved ones and keep the country running,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andrews, who also serves as a union steward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need people who are going to protect workers from the crisis of heat,\u8221\'20\'1D Andrews said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut Keeling? We\u8217\'20\'19re afraid he will be biased in the other direction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250515el5f001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
