\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Trump is dismantling a key worker safety group. It\u8217\'20\'19s another betrayal of the working class\b0\par\par\uc2 Devan Hawkins \par \uc2 914 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2025\par 10:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Niosh\uc2  has been protecting workers\u8217\'20\'19 health and safety for 50 years, affecting everyone from coalminers to firefighters\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced his tariffs in the White House Rose Garden last month, he proclaimed: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re standing up for the American worker.\u8221\'20\'1D While it remains to be seen what impact these tariffs will have on American workers, his words were belied by the fact that just a day before this announcement, hundreds of workers at the \uc2 National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health\uc2  (\uc2 Niosh\uc2 ) \u8211\'20\'13 an organization that has stood up for US workers since 1970 \u8211\'20\'13 discovered that they had been laid off.\par \par \uc2 Niosh\uc2  was founded as part of the Occupational Health and Safety Act with the purpose of \u8220\'20\'1Cdeveloping and establishing recommended occupational safety and health standards\u8221\'20\'1D. The organization has been on the frontline of protecting worker health and safety ever since. Its work has focused on understanding the risks faced by millions of workers throughout the country who put their safety on the line every day to perform their jobs. For example, \uc2 Niosh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Fire Fighter Fatality Investigation and Prevention Program investigates fatalities to understand their circumstances and make recommendations, ensuring that more of these workers, who risk their lives for others daily, can be safer in the line of duty. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/apr/01/trump-workers-unions-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump claimed he was pro-worker. His new order shows how absurd that was | Steven Greenhouse}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Far from being a caricature of a federal body firmly entrenched in the Beltway, \uc2 Niosh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s work is spread across the country. One of \uc2 Niosh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s most notable sites is its Morgantown, West Virginia, facility. Located in the heart of coal country for decades, it has focused on studying the health impacts of coalmining \u8211\'20\'13 particularly black lung disease \u8211\'20\'13 which has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2018/02/22/climate/black-lung-resurgence.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notable increases in recent years}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wvmetronews.com/2025/04/02/hhs-laying-off-185-at-morgantown-niosh/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nearly 200 workers}}}\uc2  were fired from the Morgantown location, which will severely hamper this work. (Some were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2025/04/29/cdc-black-lung-screening-coal-miners/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily rehired}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 Niosh\uc2  also supports surveillance programs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/extramural-programs/php/about/state-surveillance.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 run out of 23 states}}}\uc2 . These state-based programs focus on the unique needs of the workforce in those areas. For several years, I was fortunate to have been an epidemiologist with such a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mass.gov/orgs/occupational-health-surveillance-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 program in Massachusetts}}}\uc2 , where my colleagues and I focused on understanding and preventing health challenges ranging from bloodborne pathogen exposure among healthcare workers, to asthma risk among cleaners, to fatalities in the construction industry.\par \par \uc2 Since its founding, \uc2 Niosh\uc2  has been a nimble organization, adapting to and studying new and emerging threats. The World Trade Center Health Program, which is administered by \uc2 Niosh\uc2 , was created to study the health impacts of responding to those terrorist attacks \u8211\'20\'13 ranging from traumatic injuries and respiratory disease to cancer and mental health \u8211\'20\'13 while providing support for those responders.\par \par \uc2 In a similar way to its response to the September 11 attacks, in the grip of the epidemic of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/substance-use/opioids-and-work/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opioids}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/stress/suicide/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suicides}}}\uc2  that have cost tens of thousands of lives over the past two decades, \uc2 Niosh\uc2  has sought to understand the workplace component of these challenges. These efforts have helped to shed light on the pathway linking occupational injuries to a high risk of drug overdoses among workers in certain occupations, particularly in the construction industry, and contribute to efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10170552/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevent these deaths}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the Covid-19 pandemic, \uc2 Niosh\uc2  studied the risks faced by frontline workers. The pandemic also highlighted one of \uc2 Niosh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s most essential functions: air filtration ratings. \uc2 Niosh\uc2  tests, approves and certifies respirators to ensure that workers are protected from airborne risks ranging from silica dust to lead. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/05/the-guardian-view-on-trumps-shock-therapy-warehouse-and-transport-workers-are-the-first-victims-of-a-class-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Guardian view on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shock therapy: warehouse and transport workers are the first victims of a class war | Editorial}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Niosh\uc2  also supports the future of occupational safety and health workers. \uc2 Niosh{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/extramural-programs/php/about/tpgs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traineeship programs}}}\uc2  across the country provide support to students studying occupational health and safety. I was fortunate to be supported by such a program when I was in graduate school. Throughout the country, hospital employee safety departments, union workplace safety committees, and community occupational health and safety advocacy organizations are staffed by others like myself who received this support.\par \par \uc2 Now is the worst possible time for \uc2 Niosh\uc2  to be dismantled. Traditional workplace hazards still remain. In 2023, the last year with available data, there were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/cfoi.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 5,283 fatal occupational injuries}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 one every 99 minutes. Violent injuries at work are a growing concern, particularly among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/21650799221079045"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 healthcare workers}}}\uc2 . Increasing temperatures caused by climate change place many vulnerable workers at high risk for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.osha.gov/heat-exposure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 illness, injury and death}}}\uc2 , while extreme weather events, such as the wildfires that devastated southern California earlier this year, threaten the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/emres/about/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health and safety of emergency workers}}}\uc2 . Emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence are changing the nature of work, presenting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blogs.cdc.gov/niosh-science-blog/2021/05/24/ai-future-of-work/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new dynamics and hazards}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We need \uc2 Niosh\uc2  to study these emerging threats and safeguard workers.\par \par \uc2 It remains to be seen what will happen to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://local12.com/news/local/lives-on-line-hundreds-workers-face-layoffs-part-of-federal-budget-cuts-president-donald-trump-tariff-budgets-money-economy-jobs-laid-off-workers-niosh-safety-health-fed-cdc-funding-funds-tax-taxpayer-doge-cincinnati-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remainder of the organization}}}\uc2  and the programs supported by \uc2 Niosh\uc2  throughout the country. Regardless of what occurs, we should support the current and former workers of the organization and carry forward its mission, just as \uc2 Niosh\uc2  workers have advocated for the health and safety of workers across this country since the organization\u8217\'20\'19s inception.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Devan Hawkins is a writer and researcher from Massachusetts. He is the author of the book Worthy and Unworthy: How the Media Reports on Friends and Foes\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250509el59002uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
