\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump health cuts create \u8216\'20\'18real danger\u8217\'20\'19 around disease outbreaks, workers warn\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,473 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2025\par 09:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Key programs from child-support services to HIV treatment also gutted, leaving global populations vulnerable\par \par \uc2 Mass terminations and billions of dollars\u8217\'20\'19 worth of cuts at the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) have gutted key programs \u8211\'20\'13 from child support services to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/aids-and-hiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HIV}}}\uc2  treatment abroad \u8211\'20\'13 and created a \u8220\'20\'1Creal danger\u8221\'20\'1D that disease outbreaks will be missed, according to former workers.\par \par \uc2 Workers at the \uc2 HHS\uc2 , now led by Robert F Kennedy Jr, and in public health warned in interviews that chaotic, flawed and sweeping reductions would have broad, negative effects across the US and beyond.\par \par \uc2 While Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration is cutting the \uc2 HHS\uc2  workforce from 82,000 to 62,000 through firings and buyouts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://doge.gov/savings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grant cuts}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) have also had a stark impact on state governments \u8211\'20\'13 and resulted in firings at state public health agencies.\par \par \uc2 At the South Carolina department of public health, for example, more than 70 staff were laid off in March due to funding cuts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDisease surveillance is how we know when something unusual is happening with people\u8217\'20\'19s health, like when there are more food-poisoning cases than usual, or a virus starts spreading in a community,\u8221\'20\'1D an epidemiologist at the department, whose role was eliminated, said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the system that lets us spot patterns, find outbreaks early, and respond before more people get sick.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you lose public health staff, you lose time, you lose accuracy, you lose responsiveness, and ultimately that affects people\u8217\'20\'19s health,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CWithout us, outbreaks can fly under the radar, and the response can be delayed or disorganized. That\u8217\'20\'19s the real danger when these roles get cut.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s invisible work, until it\u8217\'20\'19s not. You may not think about it day to day, but it\u8217\'20\'19s protecting your drinking water, your food, your kids\u8217\'20\'19 schools and your community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s public health department declined to comment on specifics, but noted employees hired through grants are temporary. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen funding for grants is no longer available, their employment may end, as happened with some temporary grant employees who were funded by these grants,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 In Washington, the \uc2 HHS\uc2  has been cut harder by Doge than any other federal department. Hundreds of grants to state, local and tribal governments, as well as to research institutions, have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://taggs.hhs.gov/Content/Data/HHS_Grants_Terminated.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated}}}\uc2 , worth over $6.8bn in unpaid obligations.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HHS\uc2  receives about a quarter of all federal spending, with the majority disbursed to states for health programs and services such as Medicare and Medicaid, the insurance programs; medical research; and food and drug safety. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s budget proposal calls for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/5280245-biden-hhs-secretary-slams-trump-nih-cuts-its-a-demolition-plan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cutting}}}\uc2  the department\u8217\'20\'19s discretionary spending by 26.2%, or $33.3bn.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr, who has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 history}}}\uc2  of promoting conspiracy theories and medical misinformation, was nominated by Trump and approved by the Senate along party lines, with \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  the sole Republican dissenter.\par \par \uc2 Following a reduction in force of 10,000 employees on 1 April, Kennedy Jr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/04/04/rfk-jr-said-hhs-would-rehire-thousands-of-fired-workers-that-wasnt-true-00274034"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  20% of the firings were in error and that those workers would be reinstated, though that has not happened.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 HHS\uc2  spokesperson blamed any such errors on data-collection issues, and did not comment on any other aspects of the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reporting.\par \par \uc2 Aids relief program \u8216\'20\'18dismantled\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , an operating division of the \uc2 HHS\uc2 , employees working on maternal and child health at the President\u8217\'20\'19s Emergency Plan for Aids Relief (Pepfar) program were shocked to be included in the reduction in force, as earlier in the administration their work had received a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/global-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-trump-administrations-foreign-aid-review-status-of-pepfar/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 waiver}}}\uc2  for parts of the program from federal funding freezes.\par \par \uc2 All federal experts on HIV prevention in children overseas were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/08/health/cdc-hiv-mothers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  as part of the reduction in force.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur concern initially was that it was a mistake with the name. We hoped around that time it came out that there were 20% errors, that we would be included,\u8221\'20\'1D said an epidemiologist who was included in the reduction in force, but requested to remain anonymous as they are currently on administrative leave. They also noted that they were in the middle of planning and delivering a new pediatric HIV treatment medication set to be dispersed this year, and that that work was now at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/global-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-trump-administrations-foreign-aid-review-status-of-pepfar/#:~:text=Background%20on%20PEPFAR&text=PEPFAR%20has%20been%20reauthorized%20by,long%20as%20Congress%20appropriates%20funding."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 risk}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They said 22 epidemiologists in the branch of their CDC division had been fired. Pepfar was created in 2003 by \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  to prevent mother-to-child HIV transmission and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/global-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-trump-administrations-foreign-aid-review-status-of-pepfar/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 credited}}}\uc2  with saving 26 million lives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were very shocked on April 1 that we were put immediately on admin leave,\u8221\'20\'1D said another epidemiologist affected by the reduction in force at the CDC. \u8220\'20\'1CWe really feel our branch being cut was a mistake. The state department had said services were a priority and needed to continue, but then we were cut by \uc2 HHS\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They noted HIV treatment had already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/goats-and-soda/2025/04/14/g-s1-59863/hiv-aids-drugs-usaid-zambia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopped}}}\uc2  in regions of countries that had been reliant on \uc2 USAID\uc2  programs, such as Zambia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is one of the most successful global health programs in history, data driven with high levels of accountability and the dollars spent achieve impact. Our concern now is, yes, they are continuing Pepfar in name, but they are dismantling all the systems and structure that allowed it to succeed,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe US made a huge investment in this program in 20 years and a lot of it is now undone. We\u8217\'20\'19ve now disrupted those systems that could have reduced and eventually removed US investment in these programs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Long-term impact\u8217\'20\'19 on US families\par \par \uc2 Inside the \uc2 HHS\uc2 , the \uc2 Administration for Children and Families\uc2  is responsible for enforcing court-ordered child-support payments. For every dollar it receives in federal funding, ACF says it is able to collect $5 in child support.\par \par \uc2 A child-support specialist with the \uc2 HHS\uc2 , who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation, said reductions in force at the department have increased workloads on those who were not fired by multiple times, making it so state and tribal agencies have no way of ensuring they are compliant with federal requirements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe regional staff with direct oversight of the program are gone,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are entire regions that have two staff members managing a quarter of the work for the program with no management, no support, no knowledge of the program.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the Trump administration took office, the agency was under an unofficial stop-work order, where staff were not permitted to provide guidance or support to grantees or even answer phones, until late February, the specialist said. A reduction in force followed on 1 April, when, the child-support specialist claimed, about half the ACF staff working on child support were fired.\par \par \uc2 Their department is responsible for overseeing child-support programs at state, tribal and local levels. States \u8220\'20\'1Ccould very well lose millions of dollars in funding\u8221\'20\'1D if ACF does not provide key training and assistance and the states do not have qualified staff, the specialist cautioned. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that is the long-term impact to vulnerable children and families in the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe entire function of the program is to give economic stability to children and families, so that they do not depend on any other government program, or their reliance on these programs is lower, because the children are supported by both parents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A living hell\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services\uc2 , also within the \uc2 HHS\uc2 , one of 300 workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hospicenews.com/2025/03/27/hhs-lays-off-10000-employees-300-at-cms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terminated}}}\uc2  as part of a reduction in force claimed it had been illegal, and had not followed any proper procedures. The \uc2 National Treasury Employees Union\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.healthcaredive.com/news/hhs-layoffs-illegal-rif-kennedy-trump/744865/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  a grievance over how the firings were carried out, including incorrect information on notices.\par \par \uc2 They explained that, on 1 April, they received a generic letter informing them of an intent of reduction in force. Hours later, they were locked out of their government logins. \u8220\'20\'1CWe started emailing the management that was left, trying to get clarification on what our status was. Nobody could give us an answer,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said.\par \par \uc2 On 7 April, they discovered through their paystub that they had been placed on administrative leave, despite never receiving a notice. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t receive an RIF notice until weeks later, after requesting it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBased on my tenure, and as a disabled veteran, I should at least have a chance of reassignment,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not mad about losing my job. It happens. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been laid off. The first time was in the private sector, and it was way more humane, more empathetic, and I was given different offers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis, on the other hand, is unbridled hate. This administration has gone out of their way to make it a living hell for all of its public servants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250511el5b000rv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
