\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US-UK trade deal has saved jobs at \uc2 Jaguar Land Rover\uc2  , says Mandelson\b0\par\par\uc2 Lisa O'Carroll \par \uc2 558 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2025\par 16:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Government sources say some of company\u8217\'20\'19s 30,000 UK staff were at risk before agreement to cut car tariffs\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s limited trade deal with the US has immediately prevented job losses at \uc2 Jaguar Land Rover\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plant in the West Midlands, Britain\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the US has said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis deal has saved those jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Peter Mandelson\uc2  said in an interview on CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty big achievement, in my view, and I\u8217\'20\'19m very pleased that the president has signed it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Government sources said JLR had plans for imminent cuts among its 30,000 staff in the UK but had not informed unions in the hope that a deal with the US could be struck to eliminate the 25% tariffs on exports of cars to the US. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/08/new-ukus-trade-deal-is-a-relief-for-starmer-but-doubts-and-tariffs-remain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New UK-US trade deal is a relief for Starmer but doubts, and tariffs, remain}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s import taxes had threatened to cripple British high-end carmakers before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/08/trump-and-starmer-confirm-breakthrough-us-uk-trade-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they were reduced from 27.5% to 10%}}}\uc2  in a deal announced on Thursday by Trump and \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  , with JLR only last week resuming exports to the US after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/apr/05/jaguar-land-rover-us-shipments-trumps-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 30-day pause}}}\uc2  following the US president\u8217\'20\'19s announcement of tariffs last month.\par \par \uc2 Government insiders confirmed the decision to go for a quick deal while they could, announcing what they said was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/08/trump-and-starmer-confirm-breakthrough-us-uk-trade-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a breakthrough agreement}}}\uc2  to eliminate tariffs on car and steel exports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was important to us to be able to bank the progress that we had made at this stage,\u8221\'20\'1D said an insider.\par \par \uc2 The UK business secretary, Jonathan Reynolds, told the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s Newsnight programme on Thursday that the UK was at risk of thousands of people losing their jobs in the automotive sector within days, with one senior government insider indicating the job losses would have been at JLR.\par \par \uc2 Reynolds said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis was very, very serious. It means people would have lost their jobs without this breakthrough, and it would have been a real economic hit to the UK. We got to a position where we\u8217\'20\'19re able to make announcements \u8230\'20\'26 that have averted some very difficult things happening in the UK.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Darren Jones, the chief secretary to the Treasury, suggested the real life impact of the loss of thousands of jobs in the car sector would have been far deeper and could have affected more than 100,000 families employed directly and indirectly in the sector.\par \par \uc2 Adrian Mardell\uc2  , the JLR chief executive, hailed the agreement, saying it would help to sustain 250,000 jobs. \u8220\'20\'1CWe warmly welcome this deal which secures greater certainty for our sector and the communities it supports,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 UK car exports to the US attracted a 2.5% tariff before Trump decided to slap a further 25% import tax on foreign cars.\par \par \uc2 The 25% tariff meant that, if passed on to the consumer, the price of the lowest-cost Range Rover Evoque could have risen by nearly $12,500 (\u163\'00\'A39,400) and added $27,000 to an entry-level Range Rover that typically sells for more than $100,000.\par \par \uc2 Tariffs apply on delivery date rather than order date, which means vehicles shipped last week will no longer be subjected to the 25% tariff.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250509el590025x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
