\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Protesters arrested as Columbia calls in New York police to clear Gaza solidarity sit-in \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Mackey (now); Lucy Campbell, Marina Dunbar and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 12,608 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 May 2025\par 03:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. You can read more of our US politics coverage <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics">here</a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics">here</a}}}\uc2 >\par \par \uc2 * <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/columbia-university-police-pro-palestinian-protests">Columbia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/columbia-university-police-pro-palestinian-protests">Columbia}}}\uc2  University calls in police to clear pro-Palestinian protesters</a>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T01:55:34.715Z">2.55am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This brings our coverage of the second Trump administration to a close for the day. We will return on Thursday to keep our real-time chronicle going, but in the meantime, here are a few of the day\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge blocked the government from deporting migrants to Libya, amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/07/us-planning-to-deport-migrants-to-libya-despite-hellish-conditions-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that the US military planned to fly detained immigrants there this week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  withdrew his nominee for surgeon general, Fox News contributor Dr Janette Nesheiwat , one day before her confirmation hearing. Later in the day, he nominated a wellness influencer close to RFK Jr to take her place.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  called in the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  to clear a Gaza solidarity sit-in at a campus library, resulting in about 75 arrests.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/07/federal-reserve-interest-rate-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to lower interest rates}}}\uc2  as questions around the global economic outlook mount amid Trump\u8217\'20\'19s erratic rollout of an aggressive trade strategy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said there would be more information in the next day on a potential new proposal for a hostage release deal and ceasefire in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stockholm\u8217\'20\'19s city council rejected a \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely bizarre\u8221\'20\'1D demand from the US embassy in Sweden to abandon the city\u8217\'20\'19s diversity, equity and inclusion policies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voice of America , the US-funded broadcaster, will now run video provided by One America News , an openly partisan, virulently pro-Trump, far-right broadcaster.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T02:02:59.014Z">at 3.02am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T01:44:01.159Z">2.44am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump picks physician-turned-wellness influencer close to RFK Jr for surgeon general\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/trump-surgeon-general-nominee-casey-means"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nominating Dr Casey Means}}}\uc2 , a physician-turned-wellness influencer who is close to health secretary Robert F Kennedy Jr as his new nominee for surgeon general after withdrawing his initial pick for the job, Fox News contributor Dr Janette Nesheiwat , one day before her confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 Trump wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114468502752133916"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a social media post}}}\uc2  on Wednesday that Means \u8220\'20\'1Chas the potential to be one of the finest Surgeon Generals in United States History\u8221\'20\'1D. Without explaining why he had withdrawn the nomination of his first pick, Trump wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CSecretary Kennedy looks forward to working with Dr. Janette Nesheiwat in another capacity at \uc2 HHS\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Means and her brother, former lobbyist Calley Means , served as key advisers to Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential campaign and helped broker his eventual {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/rfk-jr-trump-speech-arizona-a2638f89ddcb5de03edbe4574ca17d45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement of Trump}}}\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T02:05:02.402Z">at 3.05am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T01:32:38.336Z">2.32am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 About 75 protesters were arrested on Wednesday night after \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  called on the New York police department to clear a a pro-Palestinian sit-in at a reading room in the school\u8217\'20\'19s Butler library, the student-run Columbia Daily Spectator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.columbiaspectator.com/news/2025/05/07/shipman-authorizes-nypd-to-assist-in-securing-butler-library-as-pro-palestinian-protest-continues/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the direct request of \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  is responding to an ongoing situation on campus where individuals have occupied a library and are trespassing,\u8221\'20\'1D the police said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NYPDnews/status/1920254883531280826"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  earlier in the evening.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T01:35:06.037Z">at 2.35am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T01:23:50.336Z">2.23am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Columbia sit-in documented by students who support and oppose Gaza solidarity protests\par \par \uc2 As we\u8217\'20\'19ve reported, the sit-in at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Butler library on Wednesday was documented on social media by Columbia journalism students and by students who support the Gaza solidarity protest movement. But Columbia students who oppose the protests were also there to document what happened.\par \par \uc2 The very first moments of the sit-in were captured on video by Shoshana Aufzien a first year student at Columbia\u8217\'20\'19s Barnard College who describes herself as an \u8220\'20\'1Cunapologetic Zionist\u8221\'20\'1D. <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/shoshanaaufzien/status/1920197081907560568"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/shoshanaaufzien/status/1920197081907560568}}}\uc2 ">\par \par \uc2 BREAKING: Protesters are occupying Butler Library {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Columbia?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Columbia}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rn7yprxqqs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rn7yprxqqs}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shoshana Aufzien\u62359\'F3\'97 (@shoshanaaufzien) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/shoshanaaufzien/status/1920197081907560568?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the school year, Aufzien went undercover to shoot video of pro-Palestinian activists for the conservative \uc2 Free Press\uc2  that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@israelinusa/video/7457609427164695839"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared on TikTok}}}\uc2  by the Israeli embassy in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Free Press\uc2  was founded by Bari Weiss , who led a pro-Israel student movement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2005/04/01/education/panels-report-on-faculty-at-columbia-spurs-debate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 during her time as a Columbia undergraduate}}}\uc2  that accused pro-Palestinian professors of antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 Aufzien, who referred to the protesters as a \u8220\'20\'1Clynch mob\u8221\'20\'1D, also shared video of the protesters refusing to a demand from security to show their identification cards that was posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X by a group of Jewish and Israeli Columbia students. <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CUJewsIsraelis/status/1920209703512023262"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/CUJewsIsraelis/status/1920209703512023262}}}\uc2 ">\par \par \uc2 Protesters attempting to stampede public safety to avoid being identified as they leave {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4yiYXbvGk2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4yiYXbvGk2}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Columbia Jewish & Israeli Students \u10017\'27\'21 (@CUJewsIsraelis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CUJewsIsraelis/status/1920209703512023262?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Meghnad Bose , a post-graduate fellow at the Columbia Journalism Review, reported on X that security officers prevented journalists from entering the library during the sit-in, but he shared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MeghnadBose93/status/1920217977250594820"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  he obtained from inside the building that gives a sense of the protest at its height. <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="https://twitter.com/MeghnadBose93/status/1920217977250594820">\par \par \uc2 BREAKING: Footage shared below shows pro-Palestine protesters inside Columbia University\u8217\'20\'19s Butler Library. Watch closely towards the end of the video.\par \par \uc2 Note: This is separate from another clip which shows campus security physically manhandling protesters, mentioned in my previous\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ENul8V57Wa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ENul8V57Wa}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meghnad Bose (@MeghnadBose93) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MeghnadBose93/status/1920217977250594820?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T01:30:15.689Z">at 2.30am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T00:16:11.900Z">1.16am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Columbia student protesters arrested and led away in handcuffs by police\par \par \uc2 A graduate student at Columbia Journalism School, Sharla Steinman , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Sharla_Steinman/status/1920266015092494503"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports on Twitter/X}}}\uc2  that at least 50 people have been arrested for taking part in the brief occupation of Butler library on campus.\par \par \uc2 Five minutes ago, another student at the journalism school, Somaiyah Hafeez , shared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sommulbaloch/status/1920271222652252433"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  of more than a dozen protesters, handcuffed with zip ties, being led away by police officers to an \uc2 NYPD\uc2  bus. Most were wearing keffiyehs \u8211\'20\'13 the traditional black and white scarf that has long been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/may/14/palestinian-keffiyeh-symbol-of-my-identity-should-not-be-afraid-to-wear-it-public"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a symbol of Palestinian identity}}}\uc2 . <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="https://twitter.com/sommulbaloch/status/1920271222652252433">\par \par \uc2 More arrests at 8:14pm. One student was taken out on a stretcher earlier. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ncTxx7KUcE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ncTxx7KUcE}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Somaiyah Hafeez (@sommulbaloch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sommulbaloch/status/1920271222652252433?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 8, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T00:23:39.761Z">at 1.23am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T00:06:07.767Z">1.06am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 NYPD\uc2  enters \uc2 Columbia university\uc2  library, says student group\par \par \uc2 Video {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920259955447189991"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted online}}}\uc2  by the student activist group Columbia University Apartheid Divest shows that officers from the New York police department have entered the Butler library reading room they occupied on Wednesday afternoon in a show of solidarity with the people of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The video shows the students, facing officers in riot gear, locked arms and chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CWe must love and support each other. We have nothing to lose but our chains!\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920259955447189991"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920259955447189991}}}\uc2 ">\par \par \uc2 We know this moment is fleeting, and that we do not have the capacity to hold it permanently at this time. But one day, this entire building and all the knowledge it holds will be liberated for good, and every book will belong to the free children of the world. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MBikqSzNUJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MBikqSzNUJ}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CU Apartheid Divest (CUAD) (@ColumbiaBDS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920259955447189991?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T00:21:07.985Z">at 1.21am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T23:48:21.008Z">12.48am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Columbia security officers block protesters from leaving library sit-in unless they show ID \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The student-run {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.columbiaspectator.com/news/2025/05/07/protesters-attempt-to-leave-reading-room-protest-as-public-safety-demands-identification/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia Spectator reports}}}\uc2  that protesters who staged a pro-Palestinian \u8220\'20\'1Cemergency rally\u8221\'20\'1D in a reading room in \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Butler library have been blocked from leaving the room by campus security officers unless they show their identification.\par \par \uc2 The protesters have refused to do so, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://communications.news.columbia.edu/news/important-information-regarding-disruption-butler-room-301"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  from the Columbia office of public affairs.\par \par \uc2 About 100 protesters took over the reading room this afternoon and held up a banner reading \u8220\'20\'1CStrike for Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920202929442558244"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 images posted on social media}}}\uc2  by the activist group Columbia University Apartheid Divest showed. <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="https://twitter.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920202929442558244">\par \par \uc2 POV: chanting with your comrades in the liberated zone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zmpz6QaiKN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zmpz6QaiKN}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CU Apartheid Divest (CUAD) (@ColumbiaBDS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920202929442558244?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the protest also gathered outside the library in response to a call from those inside.\par \par \uc2 The independent reporter Samuel Braslow shared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SamBraslow/status/1920232897853714772"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  of one supporter of the protest outside the building being evacuated after sustaining an injury as public safety officers pushed people away from the entrance. <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="https://twitter.com/SamBraslow/status/1920232897853714772">\par \par \uc2 Someone is injured as public safety officers push protesters out of the entrance. Protesters clear a path as someone carries the injured protester out. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Bp5XW4ffdr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Bp5XW4ffdr}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Samuel Braslow (@SamBraslow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SamBraslow/status/1920232897853714772?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T23:55:54.159Z">at 12.55am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T23:29:28.893Z">12.29am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  calls in New York police department to help clear Gaza solidarity sit-in\par \par \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  called in the New York police department to help clear Gaza solidarity activists who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MeghnadBose93/status/1920205494263611454"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 occupied the campus\u8217\'20\'19s main library}}}\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Students who witnessed protesters being detained by campus security officers at Butler library shared video on social media of protesters being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/itslaylas/status/1920229365805113774"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 placed in handcuffs}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MeghnadBose93/status/1920217977250594820"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 manhandled}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Activists accused the security officers of initiating violent scuffles, while the school blamed the protesters.\par \par \uc2 Claire Shipman , the university\u8217\'20\'19s acting president, said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://communications.news.columbia.edu/news/update-butler-library-disruption-statement-acting-president-claire-shipman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  that protesters had refused to leave the building despite being warned that a failure to comply result in disciplinary action and possibly arrest for trespassing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDue to the number of individuals participating in the disruption inside and outside of the building, a large group of people attempting to force their way into Butler Library creating a safety hazard, and what we believe to be the significant presence of individuals not affiliated with the University, Columbia has taken the necessary step of requesting the presence of \uc2 NYPD\uc2  to assist in securing the building and the safety of our community,\u8221\'20\'1D Shipman said in the statement. \u8220\'20\'1CSadly, during the course of this disruption, two of our Columbia Public Safety Officers sustained injuries during a crowd surge when individuals attempted to force their way into the building and into Room 301. These actions are outrageous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Columbia University Apartheid Divest , or CUAD, the student movement that established a tent encampment on campus last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ColumbiaBDS/status/1920243093523091873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on social media: \u8220\'20\'1CPublic safety has assaulted dozens of protestors so far and is refusing to let people in and out of the building despite an active fire alarm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpirits remain high in the liberated zone despite the imminent NYPD SRG raid,\u8221\'20\'1D the group reported from inside the library following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DQxl3fezf5A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 televised comments}}}\uc2  from New York\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2 , that the police were on their way to the campus.\par \par \uc2 Read more from my colleague Lauren Gambino: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/columbia-university-police-pro-palestinian-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia University calls in police to clear pro-Palestinian protesters}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T23:53:18.327Z">at 12.53am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T23:00:11.159Z">12.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  says he won't retire: 'I'm going out feet first'\par \par \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , the chief justice of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , has no intention of retiring, ever, he said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/live/c1BeJxIrtyE?feature=shared"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview}}}\uc2  on Wednesday in his native Buffalo, New York. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going out feet first\u8221\'20\'1D, Roberts told his old friend, US district judge Lawrence Vilardo.\par \par \uc2 Roberts was speaking at what was billed as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfireside chat\u8221\'20\'1D during a celebration of the 125th anniversary of the United States District Court for the Western District of New York. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c1BeJxIrtyE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 livestreamed discussion}}}\uc2  is still going on.\par \par \uc2 The chief justice also repeated his rejection of calls from supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the removal of judges who have issued rulings against his illegal executive orders. \u8220\'20\'1CImpeachment is not how you register disagreement with a decision\u8221\'20\'1D, Roberts said.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T23:03:59.314Z">at 12.03am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T22:48:29.525Z">11.48pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Stockholm City Council rejects 'bizarre' demand from US embassy to end diversity, equity and inclusion policies\par \par \uc2 The US Embassy in Sweden \u8220\'20\'1Cis demanding that its suppliers and cooperating partners stop using diversity, equity and inclusion policies, or risk an end to their relationship\u8221\'20\'1D, Sweden\u8217\'20\'19s state broadcaster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sverigesradio.se/artikel/us-embassy-presses-stockholm-city-council-to-stop-dei-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stockholm City Council\u8217\'20\'19s urban planning office received a letter from the embassy with the \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely bizarre\u8221\'20\'1D demand council member Jan Valeskog said. His office would not comply, Valeskog told a local radio station, since diversity, equity and inclusion are important to the city government.\par \par \uc2 Valeskog added that the embassy was free to end its relationship with his office if it likes. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the US terminates its relationship with the city planning office, the embassy will have difficulty getting a building permit if they want to rebuild, for example. That\u8217\'20\'19s their headache, not ours\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 The embassy was asked for comment by Radio Sweden, but declined to do so.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T22:50:34.488Z">at 11.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T21:36:58.884Z">10.36pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Federal judge rules deportation flight to Libya would violate court order\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Massachusetts ruled on Wednesday in favor of immigrant rights advocates who asked him to block the government from deporting migrants to Libya, amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/07/us-planning-to-deport-migrants-to-libya-despite-hellish-conditions-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that the US military planned to fly detained immigrants there this week.\par \par \uc2 District court judge Brian Murphy issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.mad.282404/gov.uscourts.mad.282404.91.0_4.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an order}}}\uc2  clarifying that a previous injunction he had issued already barred such flights. The judge wrote that he had explained on 30 April that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  may not evade this injunction by ceding control over non-citizens or the enforcement of its immigration responsibilities to any other agency, including but not limited to the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there is any doubt \u8212\'20\'14 the Court sees none \u8212\'20\'14 the allegedly imminent removals, as reported by news agencies and as Plaintiffs seek to corroborate with class-member accounts and public information, would clearly violate this Court\u8217\'20\'19s Order,\u8221\'20\'1D Murphy clarified.\par \par \uc2 In a rare show of unity, Libya\u8217\'20\'19s rival governments had already responded to news reports by saying that they would refuse to accept any deportees from the United States.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was asked on Wednesday if his administration was planning to send migrants to Libya, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/live/MydfT0rCkZ8?si=51qkSQ2D2KE7Isuc&t=650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the president replied}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know. You\u8217\'20\'19ll have to ask Homeland Security please.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jul/15/fresh-evidence-of-violence-at-libyan-detention-centres-as-boats-turned-back"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brutal conditions}}}\uc2  in Libyan detention centers for migrants forcibly returned after trying to reach Europe across the Mediterranean have been known about for years. In 2021, \uc2 Amnesty International{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/mde19/4439/2021/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that it had obtained more than 50 witness accounts documenting severe beatings, sexual violence, extortion and forced labor in the centers.\par \par \uc2 Trump himself has previously made it clear that he is well aware that Libya is far from a safe place.\par \par \uc2 During his first campaign for the presidency in 2016, Trump blamed \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  for the violence in post-revolutionary Libya.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLibya is in ruins. Our ambassador and three other really brave Americans are dead,\u8221\'20\'1D then candidate Trump said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-youngstown-state-university-youngstown-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a speech}}}\uc2  in August 2016. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Obama and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  should have never attempted to build a democracy in Libya\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 However, Trump was actually for the intervention in Libya before he was against it.\par \par \uc2 In early 2011, when he was flirting with a run for the presidency, Trump demanded immediate action to topple Col. Muammar el-Gaddafi in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/-4hR4O4Yjmw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on the YouTube channel}}}\uc2  he used to promote his gameshow The Apprentice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t believe what our country is doing,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said on 28 February 2011, two weeks before the Obama administration received security council authorization \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.un.org/press/en/2011/sc10200.doc.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to protect civilians}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D in Libya. \u8220\'20\'1CGaddafi in Libya is killing thousands of people, nobody knows how bad it is, and we\u8217\'20\'19re sitting around we have soldiers all have the Middle East, and we\u8217\'20\'19re not bringing them in to stop this horrible carnage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should do, on a humanitarian basis, immediately go in to Libya, knock this guy out \u8211\'20\'13 very quickly, very surgically, very effectively \u8211\'20\'13 and save the lives. After it\u8217\'20\'19s all done, we go to the protesters, who end up running the country \u8230\'20\'26 and then say: by the way, from all of your oil, we want reimbursement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T22:30:40.055Z">at 11.30pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T21:09:28.155Z">10.09pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Confirmation hearing off for Trump's surgeon general pick, amid questions over Fox News doctor's resume\par \par \uc2 The Senate confirmation hearing for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee to serve as US surgeon general, Fox News contributor Dr Janette Nesheiwat , has been cancelled amid reports that the White House is withdrawing the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-05-07/white-house-said-to-pull-nomination-for-surgeon-general-pick"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported}}}\uc2  that the White House is pulling its nomination Nesheiwat, who has come under fire for allegedly misleading statements about where she went to medical school and, from vaccine skeptics, for promoting vaccination against Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The confirmation hearing was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/rep/newsroom/press/next-week-senate-help-committee-to-hold-hearing-on-nominations-for-deputy-hhs-secretary-surgeon-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scheduled for Thursday}}}\uc2 , but Nesheiwat\u8217\'20\'19s name has been removed from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.help.senate.gov/hearings/nominations-of-james-oneill-to-serve-as-deputy-secretary-of-health-and-human-services"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revised witness schedule}}}\uc2  by the Senate committee on health, education, labor and pensions.\par \par \uc2 When Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/statement-president-elect-donald-j-trump-announcing-the-nomination-dr-janette-nesheiwat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  the nomination of the Fox News regular, he described Nesheiwat as a \u8220\'20\'1Cproud graduate of the \uc2 University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. However, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-surgeon-general-nominee-dr-janette-nesheiwat-credentials/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reported}}}\uc2  last week, Nesheiwat \u8220\'20\'1Cactually earned her medical degree from the American University of the Caribbean (AUC) School of Medicine, located in St. Maarten\u8221\'20\'1D before completing her residency at the \uc2 University of Arkansas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Until the \uc2 CBS\uc2  report was published, Nesheiwat\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/in/dr-janette-nesheiwat-3483731a/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LinkedIn profile}}}\uc2  incorrectly listed an MD from the University of Arkansas School of Medicine and made no mention of AUC.\par \par \uc2 The network also reported that the doctor previously used a formulation of the Caribbean university\u8217\'20\'19s name that might have misled people into thinking she had attended the \uc2 American University in Washington DC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI completed my medical training and residency at the University of Arkansas Medical Sciences near Little Rock where I served as Chief Resident\u8221\'20\'1D, Nesheiwat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=2083950165019201&id=474431195971114&set=a.578232465590986"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Facebook}}}\uc2  in 2018. \u8220\'20\'1CInitially pursuing training at the \uc2 American University\uc2 , I completed the majority of my studies in London, England, at St. Thomas & Guy\u8217\'20\'19s Hospital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nesheiwat\u8217\'20\'19s nomination has been heavily criticized by Trump supporters from the far-right, including Dr Simone Gold , an emergency physician who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2021/01/14/capitol-riot-covid-vaccine-doctor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 entered the Capitol}}}\uc2  on January 6 2021, and told Trump supporters not to take \u8220\'20\'1Can experimental biological agent deceptively named a vaccine\u8221\'20\'1D. On social media, Gold {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drsimonegold/status/1861169019702698112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complained}}}\uc2  that Nesheiwat had urged Americans to wear masks during the pandemic, said the vaccine was \u8220\'20\'1Csafe and effective\u8221\'20\'1D, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LegendaryEnergy/status/1904379946413281562"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised Facebook and Mark Zuckerberg}}}\uc2  for cracking down on misinformation about the pandemic. \u8220\'20\'1CIs she Dr. Fauci 2.0?\u8221\'20\'1D Gold asked.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s confidante, the Islamophobic, 9/11 truther Laura Loomer campaigned against Nesheiwat on social media, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LauraLoomer/status/1919078288619643187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing}}}\uc2  on Sunday that her \u8220\'20\'1Cpromotion of DEI-focused initiatives\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cher advocacy for the China Virus \u8216\'20\'18vaccine\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D made her \u8220\'20\'1Cunfit for the role of United States Surgeon General\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If Nesheiwat\u8217\'20\'19s nomination has been withdrawn, it will be the second time in a week Trump has lost confidence in her family. Her older sister, Julia , a homeland security adviser to Trump during his first term who also served in the Obama administration, is married to \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2  , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s now former national security adviser.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T21:19:31.438Z">at 10.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T20:39:45.345Z">9.39pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  director Kash Patel pressed on firing agents who investigated January 6 insurrection\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, Kash Patel, testified before a House appropriation subcommittee today, where he dodged questions about whether he would fire more agents who had investigated the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you anticipate firing any additional employees that may have worked in relation to the January 6 investigations?\u8221\'20\'1D asked congresswoman \uc2 Grace Meng\uc2  , the top Democrat on the panel, which held a hearing with Patel on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s budget request.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only way you get fired from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  while I\u8217\'20\'19m the director is if you violate the ethical guidelines or break the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Patel replied.\par \par \uc2 A longtime defender of Trump and critic of the alleged \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D he claims worked against the president during the first term, Patel narrowly won Senate confirmation to lead the federal law enforcement agency in February. He took office weeks after the agency\u8217\'20\'19s interim director disclosed that he had been directed to fire eight senior leaders, and compile a list of all agents who had worked on January 6 cases, prompting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/04/fbi-jan-6-trump-doj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lawsuit}}}\uc2  to stop the list\u8217\'20\'19s creation and sharing.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the list in the hearing, Patel said: \u8220\'20\'1CThat email or memo was sent out prior to my arrival at the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . We have not addressed that specific email since I\u8217\'20\'19ve arrived because the matter\u8217\'20\'19s in litigation in federal court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T20:41:05.991Z">at 9.41pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T19:41:39.452Z">8.41pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The vice-president \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  struck a far more soft, conciliatory tone towards Europe at the Munich leaders meeting in DC this morning than he did {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/jd-vance-stuns-munich-conference-with-blistering-attack-on-europes-leaders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in February this year}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 he even joked about thinking he might not be invited back after that. This time, Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b61de8f08a46beb90cd8f#block-681b61de8f08a46beb90cd8f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly emphasized}}}\uc2  that the US and Europe are \u8220\'20\'1Creal friends\u8221\'20\'1D who are \u8220\'20\'1Con the same team\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and said that things had simply \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b727b8f08e5eed5a9f836#block-681b727b8f08e5eed5a9f836"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 got off track}}}\uc2 , and I\u8217\'20\'19d encourage us all to get back on track together\u8221\'20\'1D. He did stress that the US wants Europe to be \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b70b98f08a46beb90ce90#block-681b70b98f08a46beb90ce90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-sufficient}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and to see 5% spending on defense, and he also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b6a2f8f08e5eed5a9f795#block-681b6a2f8f08e5eed5a9f795"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressed}}}\uc2  the \uc2 EU\uc2  to lower tariffs and regulatory barriers, and to open the door to US weapons.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s only harsh words were saved for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b659c8f08e5eed5a9f73c#block-681b659c8f08e5eed5a9f73c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2 . Russia , he said, was \u8220\'20\'1Casking for too much\u8221\'20\'1D in its peace offer, and said the US is focused on a long-term ceasefire. The Trump administration wants Russia and Ukraine to move towards direct talks with each other as the next step towards peace, he said. On Iran , Vance said \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b6de68f08e5eed5a9f7de#block-681b6de68f08e5eed5a9f7de"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so far so good}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D on nuclear talks, and said Iran should be allowed a \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil nuclear program\u8221\'20\'1D but not a \u8220\'20\'1Cnuclear weapons program\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CSo far we\u8217\'20\'19re on the right pathway,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In his first interview since leaving the White House in January, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accused Trump of \u8220\'20\'1Cmodern-day appeasement\u8221\'20\'1D in his approach to Russia , and said it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfoolish\u8221\'20\'1D to believe \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  will stop the violence if he is handed over parts of Ukraine . He also condemned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive talk toward Panama , Greenland and Canada . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the hell\u8217\'20\'19s going on here?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat president ever talks like that? That\u8217\'20\'19s not who we are. We\u8217\'20\'19re about freedom, democracy, opportunity \u8212\'20\'14 not about confiscation.\u8221\'20\'1D Story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/biden-accuses-trump-of-modern-day-appeasement-towards-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/07/federal-reserve-interest-rate-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kept interest rates on hold}}}\uc2  as questions around the global economic outlook mount amid Trump\u8217\'20\'19s erratic rollout of an aggressive trade strategy. Policymakers at the US central bank cautioned that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe risks of higher unemployment and higher inflation have risen \u8221\'20\'1D as they opted to maintain the benchmark interest rate for the third time in a row. Story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/07/federal-reserve-interest-rate-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/07/us-planning-to-deport-migrants-to-libya-despite-hellish-conditions-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planning}}}\uc2  to deport a group of migrants to Libya , according to reports, despite the state department\u8217\'20\'19s previous condemnation of the \u8220\'20\'1Clife-threatening\u8221\'20\'1D prison conditions in the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said there would be more information in the next day on a potential new proposal for a hostage release deal and ceasefire in Gaza . \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of talk going on about Gaza right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters at the White House today. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll be knowing probably in the next 24 hours.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Danish foreign minister, \uc2 Lars L\u248\'00\'F8kke Rasmussen\uc2  , said he would summon the acting US ambassador to Denmark after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/greenland-spying-us-intelligence-809c4ef2?mod=hp_lead_pos2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the WSJ (paywall) reported}}}\uc2  the Trump administration ordered US intelligence agencies to step up surveillance on Greenland . \u8220\'20\'1CI have read the article \u8230\'20\'26 and it worries me greatly because we do not spy on friends ,\u8221\'20\'1D Rasmussen told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to call in the US acting ambassador for a discussion at the foreign ministry to see if we can confirm this information, which is somewhat disturbing ,\u8221\'20\'1D Rasmussen added. Story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/greenland-spying-surveillance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court granted a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order to bring Turkish Tufts University student, R\u252\'00\'FCmeysa \u214\'00\'D6zt\u252\'00\'FCrk , from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  immigration detention center back to New England for hearings to determine whether her rights were violated . Story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/detained-tufts-student-rumeysa-ozturk-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The upcoming face-to-face meeting in Geneva this weekend between US treasury secretary Scott Bessent and his China counterpart He Lifeng was requested by the Trump administration, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b9c2d8f0835e2df498c7d#block-681b9c2d8f0835e2df498c7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese officials said}}}\uc2 . Bessent had earlier suggested it was the other way around. Asked about it Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681ba2048f0879537969fb86#block-681ba2048f0879537969fb86"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CThey said we initiated it? Well I think they should go back and study their files.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A hard-right, Trump-supporting US news network that perpetuated conspiracy theories about the 2020 election will provide news coverage for Voice of America (VoA), the Trump administration said. The move that OAN, which many see as a pro-Trump propaganda outfit , will provide content for VoA, which has traditionally been a more politically neutral news source, will spur further fears about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on the press. Story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/voice-america-one-america-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US National Institutes of Health\uc2  and the \uc2 Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services\uc2  have partnered to research the causes of the autism spectrum disorder , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b7d6a8f08e5eed5a9f8e9#block-681b7d6a8f08e5eed5a9f8e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 creating a database of autism-diagnosed people}}}\uc2  enrolled in Medicare and Medicaid. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re using this partnership to uncover the root causes of autism and other chronic diseases,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 HHS\uc2  Secretary Robert F Kennedy Jr said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re pulling back the curtain\u8212\'20\'14with full transparency and accountability\u8212\'20\'14to deliver the honest answers families have waited far too long to hear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration is poised to kill federal research into pollution from satellites and rockets , including some caused by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s space companies, raising new conflict-of-interest questions about the billionaire \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and Starlink owner. Story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/space-pollution-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 And finally, a fan of renaming gulfs, Trump plans to announce while on his trip to Saudi Arabia next week that the United States will now refer to the Persian Gulf as the \u8220\'20\'1CArabian Gulf\u8221\'20\'1D or the \u8220\'20\'1CGulf of Arabia\u8221\'20\'1D , none other than the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b5ade8f08f53defa8104a#block-681b5ade8f08f53defa8104a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , citing two US officials. Iranian leaders said the move was \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitically motivated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T03:49:47.616Z">at 4.49am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T19:02:01.315Z">8.02pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US considering exempting baby items like car seats and strollers from Chinese tariffs\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration is considering exempting car seats, baby strollers, cribs and other essential items for transporting children from tariffs on China up to 145%, treasury secretary Scott Bessent said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that Bessent made the comments under questioning from Democratic representative \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  at a House financial services committee hearing that those exemptions were under consideration.\par \par \uc2 Pressley, of Massachusetts, noted that more than 3.5 million babies are born annually and almost all strollers are made in China. \u8220\'20\'1CNow that cost is going up,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, the Trump administration exempted some products produced in China from 25% tariffs including bicycle helmets and child-safety furniture such as car seats and playpens. However, car seat component parts, cribs, bassinets, diaper bags and wooden safety gates were not exempted.\par \par \uc2 Chris Peterson\uc2 , the CEO of \uc2 Newell Brands\uc2 , the maker of \uc2 Graco\uc2  strollers, car seats and other children\u8217\'20\'19s goods, said last week on an earnings call that approximately 97% of baby strollers and 87% of baby car seats in the US are sourced from China. The company has hiked prices of imported baby gear products by about 20% because of tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Peterson said the company has not priced in the latest 125% tariff hike and has temporarily halted shipments from China as it sells a few months of inventory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt some point, we will begin to run out of inventory. Retailers will begin to run out of inventory and we will turn back on reordering from China,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen that happens, because the whole industry sources from China, we would expect that we and the rest of the industry will take additional pricing to offset the tariff cost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T18:33:39.397Z">7.33pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  warns of inflation and jobs risks amid Trump\u8217\'20\'19s erratic trade strategy\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve}}}\uc2  kept interest rates on hold as questions around the global economic outlook mount amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  erratic rollout of an aggressive trade strategy.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers at the US central bank cautioned that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe risks of higher unemployment and higher inflation have risen\u8221\'20\'1D as they opted to maintain the benchmark interest rate for the third time in a row.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUncertainty about the economic outlook has increased further,\u8221\'20\'1D they said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The US president has repeatedly demanded in recent months that the Fed cuts rates \u8211\'20\'13 and even raised the prospect of{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/apr/21/explainer-trump-powell-federal-reserve-chair"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  firing Jerome Powell}}}\uc2 , its chairperson, before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/22/trump-jerome-powell-fed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walking back the comments}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs plan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/03/trump-economy-gdp-jobs-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to knock}}}\uc2  the US economy.\par \par \uc2 The Fed has been sitting on its hands for months, however, citing heightened uncertainty. It last {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/18/fed-cuts-interest-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut rates in December}}}\uc2 , to a range of between 4.25% and 4.5%.\par \par \uc2 As Trump pushed ahead last month with sweeping tariffs on imported goods from much of the world, Powell cautioned this would probably {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/04/trump-tariffs-higher-inflation-slower-growth-fed-chair"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raise prices and slow growth}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 despite the administration\u8217\'20\'19s pledges to revitalize the US economy and reduce the cost of living for millions of Americans. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/07/federal-reserve-interest-rate-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve warns of inflation and jobs risks amid Trump\u8217\'20\'19s erratic trade strategy}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T18:11:33.510Z">7.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump was also just asked about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/07/donald-trump-joe-biden-us-president-latest-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-681b9c2d8f0835e2df498c7d#block-681b9c2d8f0835e2df498c7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments}}}\uc2  I just reported from China that the US initiated this weekend\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming trade meetings in Switzerland , to which he replied:\par \par \uc2 They said we initiated it? Well I think they should go back and study their files.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T18:08:21.757Z">7.08pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said there would be more information in the next day on a potential new proposal for a hostage release deal and ceasefire in Gaza .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of talk going on about Gaza right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters at the White House today. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll be knowing probably in the next 24 hours.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T18:00:35.467Z">7.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 China says US asked for trade meeting in Switzerland\par \par \uc2 The upcoming face-to-face meeting in Geneva this weekend between US treasury secretary Scott Bessent and his China counterpart He Lifeng was requested by the Trump administration, Chinese officials have said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US said repeatedly it wants to negotiate with China. This meeting is requested by the US side,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fmprc.gov.cn/eng/xw/fyrbt/lxjzh/202505/t20250507_11616836.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the foreign ministry spokesperson, Lin Jian, at his regular press conference on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 China will be entering the talks \u8220\'20\'1Cfirmly\u8221\'20\'1D opposed to tariffs, Lin said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SpoxCHN_LinJian?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1920099252698591319%7Ctwgr%5E72f4e19338e7be6cc7e7d27d6588ea6e0f364be2%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2025%2F05%2F07%2Fchina-trump-tariffs-bessent-switzerland.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  on X. \u8220\'20\'1CMeanwhile, China is open to dialogue, but any dialogue must be based on equality, respect and mutual benefit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His comments contradict Bessent\u8217\'20\'19s earlier claims that the high-stakes meeting was taking place in Switzerland by coincidence. \u8220\'20\'1CI was going to be in Switzerland to negotiate with the Swiss,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in an interview on Fox News. \u8220\'20\'1CTurns out the Chinese team is traveling through Europe, and they will be in Switzerland also. So we will meet on Saturday and Sunday.\u8221\'20\'1D China, meanwhile, had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SpoxCHN_LinJian/status/1919886413316997201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  He was going to be in Switzerland at the invitation of the Swiss government.\par \par \uc2 In the last few weeks China has repeatedly denied that it has proactively reached out to the Trump administration to propose trade talks. Instead, Chinese officials said the country was evaluating the possibility of starting trade negotiations with the US after senior US officials reached out \u8220\'20\'1Cthrough relevant parties multiple times\u8221\'20\'1D hoping to start tariff negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T19:51:33.432Z">at 8.51pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T17:33:30.518Z">6.33pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Embattled Voice of America to use newsfeed from hard-right network\par \par \uc2 A hard-right, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2 -supporting US news network that perpetuated conspiracy theories about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 election}}}\uc2  will provide news coverage for Voice of America (VoA), the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake , a special adviser to the body that oversees the government-funded VoA, announced on X that One America News (OAN), which was sued by voting machine companies for promoting claims of election fraud , will provide \u8220\'20\'1Cnewsfeed and video service\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery day I look for ways to save American taxpayers money. Bringing in OAN as a video/news source does both,\u8221\'20\'1D Lake said. \u8220\'20\'1COAN is one of the few family-owned American media networks left in the United States. We are grateful for their generosity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The news that OAN, which many see as a pro-Trump propaganda outfit , will provide content for VoA, which has traditionally been a more politically neutral news source, is a move that will spur further fears about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on the press.\par \par \uc2 OAN, which spread conspiracy theories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/coronavirus-covid-19/pro-trump-oan-pushes-wild-conspiracy-theory-novel-coronavirus-was-created"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about the coronavirus epidemic}}}\uc2 , almost exclusively interviews Republican politicians and rightwing voices, including this week the founder of an organization that denies the existence of the climate crisis. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/voice-america-one-america-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Embattled Voice of America to use newsfeed from hard-right network}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T17:01:14.364Z">6.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Florida has used a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.396519/gov.uscourts.flsd.396519.1249.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 routine court filing}}}\uc2  to lament the exodus of attorneys from the justice department .\par \par \uc2 US district judge Donald Middlebrooks of the middle district of Florida made the comments after four justice department attorneys all informed the court they would be withdrawing from the case because they were leaving the department. Usually, judges grant such requests without much fanfare.\par \par \uc2 But Middlebrooks took the opportunity to call out the lawyers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis case was expertly litigated by a team of lawyers from the \uc2 Civil Rights Division of the United States Department of Justice\uc2 , specifically the Disability Rights Section. Now it appears that multiple members of that team are ending their tenure with the Department,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.396519/gov.uscourts.flsd.396519.1249.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote Middlebrooks}}}\uc2 , who was appointed to the federal bench by \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI will grant the Motions to Withdraw, but I do so with disappointment that capable litigators and dedicated public servants have felt moved to leave their positions with the Department of Justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to \u8220\'20\'1Ccommend\u8221\'20\'1D the lawyers for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe extraordinary efforts they took in arguing these important issues and granted their request to withdraw.\par \par \uc2 More than 250 lawyers have left or are planning to leave the civil rights division, a flood of departures that amounts to about a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/01/civil-rights-division-doj-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 70% reduction in personnel.}}}\uc2  The head of the division, a political appointee, has made it clear in new \u8220\'20\'1Cmission statements\u8221\'20\'1D to each of the sections that their longstanding priorities will shift to more closely align with the president\u8217\'20\'19s priorities.\par \par \uc2 Former and current employees have said that the reduction in personnel makes it virtually impossible for the division to enforce civil rights laws.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:57:56.227Z">5.57pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Court orders detained Tufts student R\u252\'00\'FCmeysa \u214\'00\'D6zt\u252\'00\'FCrk returned to Vermont\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court on Wednesday granted a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order to bring Turkish Tufts University student, R\u252\'00\'FCmeysa \u214\'00\'D6zt\u252\'00\'FCrk , from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  immigration detention center back to New England for hearings to determine whether her rights were violated .\par \par \uc2 A judicial panel of the New York-based US second circuit court of appeals ruled in the case after lawyers representing her and the US justice department presented arguments at a hearing on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u214\'00\'D6zt\u252\'00\'FCrk has been detained in Louisiana for six weeks following an op-ed she cowrote last year that criticized the school\u8217\'20\'19s response to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza}}}\uc2 . The court ordered her to be transferred to \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) custody in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/vermont"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vermont}}}\uc2  no later than 14 May .\par \par \uc2 A district court judge in Vermont had earlier ordered that the 30-year-old doctoral student be brought to the state for hearings to determine whether she was illegally detained. \u214\'00\'D6zt\u252\'00\'FCrk\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers say her detention violates her constitutional rights, including free speech and due process.\par \par \uc2 The justice department, which appealed that ruling, said that an immigration court in Louisiana has jurisdiction over her case. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/detained-tufts-student-rumeysa-ozturk-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Court orders detained Tufts student R\u252\'00\'FCmeysa \u214\'00\'D6zt\u252\'00\'FCrk returned to Vermont}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:59:48.189Z">at 5.59pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:51:18.584Z">5.51pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'We do not spy on our friends': Denmark plans to call in US ambassador over 'disturbing' Greenland spying report\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/miranda-bryant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miranda Bryant}}}\par \par \uc2 The Danish foreign minister, \uc2 Lars L\u248\'00\'F8kke Rasmussen\uc2  , has said he would call in the acting US ambassador to Denmark after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/greenland-spying-us-intelligence-809c4ef2?mod=hp_lead_pos2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal (paywall) reported}}}\uc2  the Trump administration ordered US intelligence agencies to step up surveillance on Greenland .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have read the article in the Wall Street Journal and it worries me greatly because we do not spy on friends ,\u8221\'20\'1D Rasmussen told reporters during an informal meeting of \uc2 EU\uc2  foreign ministers in Warsaw on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to call in the US acting ambassador for a discussion at the foreign ministry to see if we can confirm this information, which is somewhat disturbing,\u8221\'20\'1D Rasmussen added.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/greenland-spying-us-intelligence-809c4ef2?mod=hp_lead_pos1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , published last night, said high-ranking officials working under \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  , the director of national intelligence, issued the instruction to agency heads in a \u8220\'20\'1Ccollection emphasis message\u8221\'20\'1D. Such messages customarily help to set intelligence priorities and direct resources and attention to high-interest targets.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Central Intelligence Agency\uc2  , the \uc2 Defense Intelligence Agency\uc2  and the \uc2 National Security Agency\uc2  were all included in the message. It told chiefs to study Greenland\u8217\'20\'19s independence movement and attitudes to American efforts to extract resources on the island, according to the report, citing two unnamed officials familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The move, which will further alarm Denmark and Europe, underlines the seriousness of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s intent to increase US influence over Greenland. Just last weekend, he refused to rule out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/04/trump-greenland-denmark-military-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 using military force to gain control}}}\uc2  of the island. Denmark, a US ally and \uc2 Nato\uc2  member, has repeatedly vowed that Greenland is not available for sale or annexation. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/greenland-spying-surveillance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Denmark to summon US envoy over report of Greenland spying directive}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:26:14.980Z">5.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'Not a safe place to send anyone': US planning to deport migrants to Libya despite \u8216\'20\'18hellish\u8217\'20\'19 conditions \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lorenzo-tondo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lorenzo Tondo}}}\uc2  in Palermo and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  in New York\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is planning to deport a group of migrants to Libya , according to reports, despite the state department\u8217\'20\'19s previous condemnation of the \u8220\'20\'1Clife-threatening\u8221\'20\'1D prison conditions in the country. Libya\u8217\'20\'19s provisional government has denied the reports.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-may-soon-deport-migrants-libya-military-flight-sources-say-2025-05-07/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters }}}\uc2 cited three unnamed US officials as saying the deportations could happen this week. Two of the officials said the individuals, whose nationalities are not known, could fly to Libya as soon as Wednesday, but they added the plans could still change. \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/06/us/politics/trump-libya-migrants.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also cited a US official confirming}}}\uc2  the deportation plans. It was not clear what Libya would be getting in return for taking any deportees.\par \par \uc2 Human rights groups condemned the reported plans, noting the country\u8217\'20\'19s poor record on human rights practices and harsh treatment of detainees . \uc2 Sarah Leah Whitson\uc2 , the executive director of Democracy for the Arab World Now (Dawn), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sarahleah1/status/1919970587960623322"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Migrants have long been trafficked, tortured and ransomed in Libya. The country is in a civil war. It is not a safe place to send anyone.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Reichlin-Melnick\uc2 , senior fellow at the \uc2 American Immigration Council\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ReichlinMelnick/status/1919947458324349431"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on the platform}}}\uc2  alongside a picture of a Libyan detention facility:\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t look away. This is what Libya\u8217\'20\'19s migrant detention facilities look like. This is what Trump is doing.\par \par \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  called these places a \u8216\'20\'18hellscape\u8217\'20\'19 where beatings are common and sexual violence are rampant. There are reports of human trafficking and even slavery.\par \par \uc2 It comes as the Trump administration expands its aggressive efforts to negotiate the swift deportations of migrants to third-party countries which, as well as Libya , includes Angola , Benin , Eswatini , Moldova and Rwanda , as reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/u-s-deportation-deals-with-angola-equatorial-guinea/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by CBS News}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/05/donald-trump-tariffs-film-industry-alcatraz-russia-israel-us-politcs-live-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6818e7628f08c2e1abc7b66f#block-6818e7628f08c2e1abc7b66f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters}}}\uc2  earlier this week. This is alongside its existing arrangement with El Salvador , which it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/04/28/politics/trump-el-savador-prison-negotiations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has paid millions}}}\uc2  to detain hundreds of migrants in its notorious mega-prison. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/07/us-planning-to-deport-migrants-to-libya-despite-hellish-conditions-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US planning to deport migrants to Libya despite \u8216\'20\'18hellish\u8217\'20\'19 conditions \u8211\'20\'13 reports}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:28:30.964Z">at 5.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:03:55.669Z">5.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US customers could face higher energy bills amid reports that the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) plans to end the Energy Star program whose blue labels have certified energy efficiency on home appliances for more than 30 years, experts warn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you wanted to raise families\u8217\'20\'19 energy bills, getting rid of the Energy Star label would be a pretty good way,\u8221\'20\'1D said Steven Nadel, executive director of the non-profit research organization the \uc2 American Council for an Energy-Efficient Economy\uc2  (\uc2 ACEEE\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The reports of Energy Star\u8217\'20\'19s elimination come after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has railed against showers and toilets that conserve water. In April, he signed an executive order to \u8220\'20\'1Crestore shower freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  reported that staff were told: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Energy Star program and all the other climate work, outside of what\u8217\'20\'19s required by statute, is being de-prioritized and eliminated.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/energy-star-program-ends-utility-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Utility bills could rise as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s EPA to end Energy Star program, experts warn}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T15:52:53.652Z">4.52pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  accused the US courts of preventing him from deporting \u8220\'20\'1Cmurders and other criminals\u8221\'20\'1D in a post on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114466868060900843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur Court System is not letting me do the job I was Elected to do. Activist judges must let the Trump Administration deport murderers, and other criminals who have come into our Country illegally, WITHOUT DELAY!!!\u8221\'20\'1D the president wrote.\par \par \uc2 Recent reports have revealed the intentions of the Trump administration to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/07/us-planning-to-deport-migrants-to-libya-despite-hellish-conditions-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deport immigrants}}}\uc2  to more countries other than the one designated as the immigrant\u8217\'20\'19s country of origin, also called third-country deportations.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T15:37:24.612Z">4.37pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr launches autism project using data from Medicare and Medicaid\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US National Institutes of Health\uc2  and the \uc2 Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services\uc2  have partnered to research the causes of the autism spectrum disorder, creating a database of autism-diagnosed people enrolled in Medicare and Medicaid, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/nih-cms-partner-advance-understanding-autism-through-secure-access-select-medicare-and-medicaid-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agencies announced}}}\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 The partnership will \u8220\'20\'1Cfocus first on enabling research around the root causes of autism spectrum disorder\u8221\'20\'1D in order to help \uc2 NIH\uc2  build a real-world data platform using claims data, electronic medical records, and wearable consumer health-monitoring devices. The agencies said the project will comply with applicable privacy laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re using this partnership to uncover the root causes of autism and other chronic diseases,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 HHS\uc2  Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re pulling back the curtain\u8212\'20\'14with full transparency and accountability\u8212\'20\'14to deliver the honest answers families have waited far too long to hear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s health department has already faced backlash for this project following the announcement that the \uc2 NIH\uc2  would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/22/rfk-jr-autism-nih"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collecting the private medical records}}}\uc2  of many Americans from several different federal and commercial databases.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T15:19:04.057Z">4.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary Scott Bessent described the upcoming meeting with Chinese officials on trade set to begin on Saturday as \u8220\'20\'1Cnegotiations.\u8221\'20\'1D He added that \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  , the White House trade adviser, will not be joining him and US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer at the discussions in Switzerland. He also declined to say which countries are close to reaching trade agreements with the US.\par \par \uc2 When asked during today\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 House Financial Services Committee\uc2  hearing whether discussions with China were considered advanced, Bessent replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI said, on Saturday, we will begin, which I believe is the opposite of advanced.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T15:01:30.867Z">4.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US and Europe 'got a little bit off track', says Vance, as he encourages 'us all to get back on track together'\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Wolfgang Ischinger\uc2  thanks Vance and says he hopes he will come back to the Munich Security Conference again, the vice-president jokes:\par \par \uc2 I appreciate the invitation back. I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/jd-vance-stuns-munich-conference-with-blistering-attack-on-europes-leaders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February}}}\uc2  whether I\u8217\'20\'19d get the invitation back, but it\u8217\'20\'19s good to know that it\u8217\'20\'19s still there.\par \par \uc2 Ischinger lightly interjects \u8220\'20\'1Cwe thought about it\u8221\'20\'1D, to which they both laugh.\par \par \uc2 Vance also congratulates \uc2 Friedrich Merz\uc2  after the conservative leader was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/06/friedrich-merz-german-chancellor-europe-live-latest-news?page=with%3Ablock-6819c36d8f08c2e1abc7bc82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected}}}\uc2  German chancellor.\par \par \uc2 I know that we\u8217\'20\'19ll have a conversation with him in the next couple of days.\par \par \uc2 Vance goes on to say that what he said in his February speech \u8220\'20\'1Capplied as much to the previous American administration as much as it did to any government in Europe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In stark contrast to the tone of his February speech \u8211\'20\'13 as this whole Q&A session has been \u8211\'20\'13 Vance says he means \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the heart and as a friend \u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a tradeoff between policing the bounds of democratic speech and debate, and losing the trust of our people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He says he accepts and understands that \u8220\'20\'1Csome things are outside the realm of political debate\u8221\'20\'1D and every country will draw those lines slightly differently.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to be careful that we don\u8217\'20\'19t draw the lines in such a way that we don\u8217\'20\'19t undermine democratic legitimacy,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not: Europe bad, America good. It\u8217\'20\'19s that I think we got a little bit off track, and I\u8217\'20\'19d encourage us all to get back on track together . We\u8217\'20\'19re certainly willing and able to participate in that work and I hope all of you are too.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:08:10.341Z">at 5.08pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T14:46:23.854Z">3.46pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'We care about Europe being self-sufficient', says Vance\par \par \uc2 Trump would like to see 5% spending on defense in Nato , Vance says.\par \par \uc2 European countries have \u8220\'20\'1Csome catching up to do\u8221\'20\'1D as it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t kept up with that, Vance says.\par \par \uc2 We really want and we really care about Europe being self-sufficient .\par \par \uc2 He says he regrets US foreign policy in the Middle East in 2003: \u8220\'20\'1CI frankly wish we had listened to our European friends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But on the need for Europe to play a bigger role in continental defense, he says \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are fundamentally right and it\u8217\'20\'19s gratifying to see so many of European friends recognise that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I think we\u8217\'20\'19re all aligned on it . It\u8217\'20\'19s just a question of getting there and getting there quickly .\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T14:39:37.112Z">3.39pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The US and China have not had a conversation about a strategic deal on Taiwan , Vance says.\par \par \uc2 He says the Trump administration is working to rebalance global trade in the interest of US workers and manufacturers, and that means China would have to take steps to boost domestic demand.\par \par \uc2 He says the rebalancing would also require cutting more trade deals with \u8220\'20\'1Csome of our friends in Europe but also with some of our more adversarial nations \u8221\'20\'1D, adding that the goal was to do this while maintaining \u8220\'20\'1Cat least an open dialog with [the People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of China].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T14:38:33.410Z">3.38pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Vance says 'so far so good' with Iran nuclear talks\par \par \uc2 Vance describes US talks with Iran as \u8220\'20\'1Cso far so good\u8221\'20\'1D and says there is a deal to be made that would \u8220\'20\'1Creintegrate Iran into the global economy\u8221\'20\'1D while preventing it from getting a nuclear weapon.\par \par \uc2 Iran getting a nuclear weapon is completely off the table for the American administration \u8211\'20\'13 no ifs, ands or butts.\par \par \uc2 Vance says he and Trump hate nuclear proliferation , so much so that Trump would be open to sitting down with Russia and China in the coming years to discuss reducing the number of nuclear weapons in the world at large, Vance says.\par \par \uc2 But there is no way you get to that conversation if you allow multiple regimes all over the world to enter the sprint for a nuclear weapon.\par \par \uc2 And we really think that if the Iran domino falls, you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see nuclear proliferation all over the Middle East \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s very bad for us and for our friends .\par \par \uc2 Vance says the US has been \u8220\'20\'1Cvery happy with the Iranian response to some of the points that we\u8217\'20\'19ve made\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 So far we\u8217\'20\'19re on the right pathway.\par \par \uc2 He says the US doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mind Iran having civil nuclear power, but they can\u8217\'20\'19t also have an enrichment program that allows it to get to a nuclear weapon .\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T14:25:59.878Z">3.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Vance presses EU to lower tariffs and regulatory barriers, and open door to US weapons\par \par \uc2 Vance says discussions between the United States and Europe were ongoing, saying Washington was pressing the \uc2 European Union\uc2  to lower its tariffs and regulatory barriers to improve the trading relationship.\par \par \uc2 In the same way that American markets have been open to European goods, we\u8217\'20\'19d like a lot of European markets to be open to American goods.\par \par \uc2 He says there are agricultural and value-added manufacturing components to that, as well as opportunities for \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican military software and hardware\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He welcomes moves by Europe to expand its own defenses , but says US arms manufacturers should have an opportunity to participate more fully in those efforts.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T13:59:09.229Z">2.59pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Russia 'asking for too much', says JD Vance, as he says both sides need to talk to each other directly to end war in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Vance says the Trump administration wants Russia and Ukraine to agree on some guidelines for talking to each other directly , which he says would be necessary to end the war.\par \par \uc2 Vance says the US views the concessions that Russia had sought as too much .\par \par \uc2 Certainly the first peace offer the Russians put on the table, our reaction to it was: \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re asking for too much .\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Russians are asking for a certain set of requirements, a certain set of concessions, to end the conflict. We think they\u8217\'20\'19re asking for too much .\par \par \uc2 But he says he is not that pessimistic about the chances for ending the conflict and direct talks between Russia and Ukraine is the next step the US wants to see.\par \par \uc2 Right now we would like the Russians and Ukrainians to agree to some basic guidelines for sitting down and talking to one another \u8230\'20\'26 We think that is the next big step we would like to take \u8230\'20\'26 We think it\u8217\'20\'19s probably impossible for us to mediate this entirely without at least some direct negotiation between the two.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T14:05:30.816Z">at 3.05pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T13:45:24.835Z">2.45pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'We are very much real friends': JD Vance says he believes US and Europe 'are on the same team'\par \par \uc2 In marked contrast to his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/jd-vance-stuns-munich-conference-with-blistering-attack-on-europes-leaders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remarks}}}\uc2  back in February, Vance says he believes the US and Europe \u8220\'20\'1Care on the same team\u8221\'20\'1D and it was \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D to think a wedge could be driven between them.\par \par \uc2 He says he has a tendency to think of foreign policy purely in terms of \u8220\'20\'1Ctransactional values\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 in terms of \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat does American get out of it?\u8221\'20\'1D at the expense of the moral and humanitarian side of issues.\par \par \uc2 Vance says he believes that \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally we have to be \u8211\'20\'13 and we are - on the same civilizational team\u8221\'20\'1D .\par \par \uc2 He and Trump believe this means \u8220\'20\'1Ca little bit more European burden-sharing on the defense side\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Call of us\u8221\'20\'1D rethinking the \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity posture of the last 20 years\u8221\'20\'1D which is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot adequate for the next 20 years\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I do think we\u8217\'20\'19re in one of these phases where we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to rethink a lot of big questions, but I do think we should rethink those big questions together . That\u8217\'20\'19s a fundamental belief of both me and the president.\par \par \uc2 He adds:\par \par \uc2 I still think that this European alliance is very important but I think that for it to be important and for us to be real friends with each other \u8211\'20\'13 and I think we are very much real friends \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to talk about the big questions.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T14:11:05.382Z">at 3.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T13:35:13.494Z">2.35pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 JD Vance to deliver remarks at Munich Leaders Meeting in Washington DC\par \par \uc2 The vice-president JD Vance is due on stage at the Munich Leaders Meeting on global security taking place in Washington DC shortly for a Q&A led by \uc2 Wolfgang Ischinger\uc2  , a former German diplomat who chairs the annual Munich Security Conference .\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s appearance earlier this year at that conference was nothing short of stunning and one of the most significant moments in the second Trump administration so far. As my colleague Patrick Wintour {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/jd-vance-stuns-munich-conference-with-blistering-attack-on-europes-leaders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  at the time, European leaders were left stunned as Vance \u8220\'20\'1Claunched a brutal ideological assault on the continent, accusing its leaders of suppressing free speech, failing to halt illegal migration and running in fear from voters\u8217\'20\'19 true beliefs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a hostile, chastising speech that openly questioned whether current European values warranted defence by the US , Vance painted a picture of European politics infected by media censorship, cancelled elections and political correctness. He said:\par \par \uc2 If you are afraid of the voices, the opinions and the conscience that guide your very own people \u8230\'20\'26 If you\u8217\'20\'19re running in fear of your own voters, there is nothing America can do for you, nor for that matter is there anything you can do for the American people .\par \par \uc2 His apparent disdain for Europe was also further revealed in leaked messages during the Signalgate scandal in which he told defense secretary \uc2 Pete Hegseth\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI just hate bailing out Europe again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if his tone is more amicable this morning. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/jd-vance-stuns-munich-conference-with-blistering-attack-on-europes-leaders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance stuns Munich conference with blistering attack on Europe\u8217\'20\'19s leaders}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T16:12:20.966Z">at 5.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T13:14:42.214Z">2.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump plans to announce US will call Persian Gulf \u8216\'20\'18Arabian Gulf\u8217\'20\'19 or 'Gulf of Arabia', officials say\par \par \uc2 A fan of renaming gulfs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  plans to announce while on his trip to Saudi Arabia next week that the United States will now refer to the Persian Gulf as the \u8220\'20\'1CArabian Gulf\u8221\'20\'1D or the \u8220\'20\'1CGulf of Arabia\u8221\'20\'1D , none other than the Associated Press reports, citing two US officials.\par \par \uc2 The move has prompted a push back from Iranian leaders who called it \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitically motivated\u8221\'20\'1D. On Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  current foreign minister weighed in, saying that names of Middle East waterways do \u8220\'20\'1Cnot imply ownership by any particular nation, but rather reflects a shared respect for the collective heritage of humanity\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Abbas Araghchi\uc2  continued on X:\par \par \uc2 Politically motivated attempts to alter the historically established name of the Persian Gulf are indicative of hostile intent toward Iran and its people, and are firmly condemned .\par \par \uc2 Any short-sighted step in this connection will have no validity or legal or geographical effect , it will only bring the wrath of all Iranians from all walks of life and political persuasion in Iran, the US and across the world.\par \par \uc2 The Persian Gulf has been widely known by that name since the 16th century and it has become an emotive issues for Iranians, although usage of \u8220\'20\'1CGulf of Arabia\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CArabian Gulf\u8221\'20\'1D is dominant in many countries in the Middle East. The US military for years has also unilaterally referred to the Persian Gulf as the Arabian Gulf in statements and images it releases.\par \par \uc2 Trump can change the name for official US purposes, but he can\u8217\'20\'19t dictate what the rest of the world calls it, as he has found several months after he declared that the US would refer to the Gulf of Mexico as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-executive-order-gulf-mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGulf of America\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/trump-rename-persian-arabian-gulf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump plans to announce US will call Persian Gulf \u8216\'20\'18Arabian Gulf\u8217\'20\'19, officials say}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T17:12:46.372Z">at 6.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T12:58:30.573Z">1.58pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump administration to stop US research on space pollution, in boon to \uc2 Elon Musk\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is poised to kill federal research into pollution from satellites and rockets , including some caused by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s space companies, raising new conflict-of-interest questions about the billionaire \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and Starlink owner.\par \par \uc2 The pollution appears to be accumulating in the stratosphere at alarming levels. Some fear it could destroy the ozone layer, potentially expose some people to higher levels of ultraviolet radiation or help further destabilize the earth\u8217\'20\'19s climate during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two research projects would\u8217\'20\'19ve had the potential to eventually lead to new regulations, costs or logistical challenges for Musk\u8217\'20\'19s companies and the commercial space industry, experts say.\par \par \uc2 They were part of the office of atmospheric research at the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2  (Noaa), which the Trump administration is now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2025/apr/11/trump-climate-science-nasa-noaa-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposing}}}\uc2  to kill. The administration says it is \u8220\'20\'1Celiminating the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s support of woke ideology\u8221\'20\'1D, but critics say it\u8217\'20\'19s protecting a prolific donor and political ally .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously there\u8217\'20\'19s political motivation, and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business interests are tied up in Noaa\u8217\'20\'19s work,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tim Whitehouse , executive director of the Public Employees for Environmental Responsibilit y non-profit, which has filed a Freedom of Information Act request for emails around the projects.\par \par \uc2 These are programs the government wanted to build up, that had bipartisan support, and suddenly they\u8217\'20\'19re being gutted with no rhyme, reason or adequate explanation. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/space-pollution-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration to stop US research on space pollution, in boon to Elon Musk}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T12:29:56.487Z">1.29pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Maduro did not close our bureau \u8211\'20\'13 Trump did\u8217\'20\'19: Voice of America journalists speak out\par \par \uc2 Carolina Valladares P\u233\'00\'E9rez , a Washington-based correspondent for the government-funded international news service Voice of America , has reported from places where press freedom is severely restricted \u8211\'20\'13 war zones and autocratic states \u8211\'20\'13 in the Middle East and across Latin America. Intimidation and threats from state officials were not unusual \u8211\'20\'13 but she always managed to get the story out.\par \par \uc2 Now for the first time in her career, Valladares P\u233\'00\'E9rez says she has been silenced \u8211\'20\'13 not by a faraway regime, but by the government of the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro did not close our bureau,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, of Venezuela\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian leader. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  closed it. I find this astonishing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Valladares P\u233\'00\'E9rez is one of hundreds of VOA journalists who remain shut out of their newsroom nearly two months after Trump signed a late-night {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/articles/2025/03/the-voice-of-radical-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive order}}}\uc2  aimed at dismantling their parent company, the US Agency for Global Media (USAGM). The journalists{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/03/media/voice-of-america-return-trump-lake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  had been hopeful }}}\uc2 they might be able to return to their broadcasts this week \u8211\'20\'13 VOA was even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/savevoanow/status/1919761569979740239"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 included}}}\uc2  in the rotation of news outlets assigned to cover the president as part of the White House press pool \u8211\'20\'13 but whiplashing court orders have clouded their path forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have 3,500 affiliates around the world \u8211\'20\'13 these are television stations, radio stations, digital affiliates, who depend on our content ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Patsy Widakuswara , VOA\u8217\'20\'19s White House bureau chief, who is the lead plaintiff in a lawsuit challenging the president\u8217\'20\'19s authority to gut an agency chartered by Congress.\par \par \uc2 The void is going to be filled by our adversaries \u8211\'20\'13 it already is. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/voice-of-america-journalists-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Maduro did not close our bureau \u8211\'20\'13 Trump did\u8217\'20\'19: Voice of America journalists speak out}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T12:20:36.719Z">1.20pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 UK in talks with US officials over movie tariffs, says minister\par \par \uc2 Britain is in \u8220\'20\'1Cactive discussions\u8221\'20\'1D with US officials over the extraordinary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/04/trump-tariffs-foreign-movies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100% tariff on all movies produced outside the US}}}\uc2  proposed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , as it tries to protect one of its biggest creative industries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are already in active discussions with the top of the US administration on this subject. We are working hard to establish what might be proposed, if anything, and to make sure our world-beating creative industries are protected,\u8221\'20\'1D creative industries minister Chris Bryant told parliament.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that Bryant noted that Trump had not given any details about his proposal, adding that it was not clear how tariffs could be applied to the film industry, with productions often created and developed across different locations and countries.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bombshell announcement on Sunday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/may/06/british-film-industry-leaders-aghast-at-trumps-movie-tariffs-brian-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left British film industry leaders aghast}}}\uc2 , with the UK, a regular location for some of Hollywood\u8217\'20\'19s biggest movie productions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/may/05/fears-trump-foreign-film-tariffs-wipe-out-uk-movie-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particularly vulnerable}}}\uc2  to any attempt by the US president to prevent American studios shooting overseas. Flummoxed entertainment executives have questioned both the timing of the proposed levy and how it could be enforced.\par \par \uc2 White House officials said \u8220\'20\'1Cno official decisions have been made\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/05/trump-tariffs-foreign-movies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Monday}}}\uc2  and Trump appeared to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/may/06/trump-softens-tone-on-movie-tariff-announcement-gavin-newsom-jimmy-kimmel-fallon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soften his tone yesterday}}}\uc2 , saying he planned to meet and discuss the plans with film industry leaders. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not trying to hurt the industry, I want to help the industry \u8230\'20\'26 So we\u8217\'20\'19re going to meet with the industry. I want to make sure they\u8217\'20\'19re happy with it because we\u8217\'20\'19re all about jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-07T13:06:19.288Z">at 2.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T11:44:48.184Z">12.44pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Iran is aghast at reports from the US that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is planning for the US to offer Saudi Arabia to change the name of the Persian Gulf to the Gulf of Arabia, a move that would cause deep offence in Iran and have large diplomatic repercussions.\par \par \uc2 There has been a decades long dispute between Arab States and Iran about the appropriate terminology for the stretch of water, but historically dating back to the Greeks it has been called the Persian Gulf.\par \par \uc2 Intermediaries are trying to persuade Trump of the diplomatic folly of the move just as Iranian diplomats are trying to convince hardliners in Iran that Trump is serious about negotiating a balanced nuclear deal with Iran.\par \par \uc2 He would make the announcement as a gift to Saudi Arabia as part of his three day tour in the Gulf.\par \par \uc2 One source said \u8220\'20\'1Cit is the height of stupidity, but we are trying to tell the Iranians that Trump will be there for four years, but the Persian Gulf will be there for thousands of years\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The source added that Trump believes the move might be enough to persuade Arab states of the value of normalisation of relations with Israel, one of the great second term goals of Trump diplomacy.\par \par \uc2 Trump has already renamed the Gulf of Mexico the Gulf of America.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T11:26:38.551Z">12.26pm BST</time> <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="526364ae-00a9-42be-8f72-790fb0d4281f" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T11:15:33.069Z">12.15pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is poised to kill federal research into pollution from satellites and rockets, including some caused by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s space companies, raising new conflict-of-interest questions about the billionaire \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and Starlink owner.\par \par \uc2 The pollution appears to be accumulating in the stratosphere at alarming levels. Some fear it could destroy the ozone layer, potentially expose some people to higher levels of ultraviolet radiation or help further destabilize the earth\u8217\'20\'19s climate during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two research projects would have had the potential to eventually lead to new regulations, costs or logistical challenges for Musk\u8217\'20\'19s companies and the commercial space industry, experts say.\par \par \uc2 They were part of the office of atmospheric research at the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2  (Noaa), which the Trump administration is now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2025/apr/11/trump-climate-science-nasa-noaa-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposing}}}\uc2  to kill. The administration says it is \u8220\'20\'1Celiminating the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s support of woke ideology\u8221\'20\'1D, but critics say it\u8217\'20\'19s protecting a prolific donor and political ally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously there\u8217\'20\'19s political motivation, and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business interests are tied up in Noaa\u8217\'20\'19s work,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tim Whitehouse, executive director of the \uc2 Public Employees for Environmental Responsibility\uc2  non-profit, which has filed a Freedom of Information Act request for emails around the projects. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/space-pollution-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration to stop US research on space pollution, in boon to Elon Musk}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T11:07:44.299Z">12.07pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Libya\u8217\'20\'19s government of national unity said on Wednesday it rejects the use of Libyan territory as a destination for deporting migrants without its knowledge or consent.\par \par \uc2 The government also stated there is no coordination with the United States regarding the reception of migrants.\par \par \uc2 The statement comes after US officials indicated that president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration may deport migrants to Libya.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T10:52:38.448Z">11.52am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration may deport migrants to Libya for the first time this week, three US officials said on Tuesday, as part of his immigration crackdown and despite Washington\u8217\'20\'19s past condemnation of Libya\u8217\'20\'19s harsh treatment of detainees.\par \par \uc2 Two of the officials said the US military could fly the migrants to the north African country as soon as Wednesday, but stressed that plans could still change.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon referred queries to the White House. The White House, state department and \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  did not immediately respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Reuters could not determine how many migrants would be sent to Libya or the nationalities of the individuals that the administration is considering for deportation.\par \par \uc2 The Republican president, who made immigration a major issue during his election campaign, has launched aggressive enforcement action since taking office, surging troops to the southern border and pledging to deport millions of immigrants in the United States illegally.\par \par \uc2 As of Monday, the Trump administration has deported 152,000 people, according to DHS.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T10:35:35.526Z">11.35am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  plans to announce on his trip to Saudi Arabia next week that the US will refer to the Persian Gulf as the Arabian Gulf or the Gulf of Arabia, two US officials said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Arab nations have pushed for a change to the geographic name of the body of water off the southern coast of Iran, while Iran has maintained its historic ties to the gulf.\par \par \uc2 The US officials spoke to \uc2 The Associated Press\uc2  on condition of anonymity to discuss sensitive matters. The White House and national security council did not immediately respond to messages seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 The Persian Gulf has been widely known by that name since the 16th century, although use of Gulf of Arabia and Arabian Gulf is dominant in many countries in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The government of Iran \u8211\'20\'13 formerly Persia \u8211\'20\'13 threatened to sue \uc2 Google\uc2  in 2012 over the company\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to label the body of water at all on its maps.\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Google\uc2  Maps in the US, the body of water appears as Persian Gulf (Arabian Gulf). \uc2 Apple\uc2  Maps only says the Persian Gulf.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T10:07:18.137Z">11.07am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  secretary Scott Bessent and chief trade negotiator Jamieson Greer will meet China\u8217\'20\'19s economic tsar He Lifeng in Switzerland this weekend for talks that could be the first step toward resolving a trade war disrupting the global economy.\par \par \uc2 News of the meeting announced by Washington late Tuesday, and later confirmed by Beijing, sent US equity index futures sharply higher, while stock markets in China and Hong Kong also rose as Asian trading began on Wednesday, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 The talks come after weeks of escalating tensions that have seen duties on goods imports between the world\u8217\'20\'19s two largest economies soar well beyond 100%, amounting to what Bessent on Tuesday described as the equivalent of a trade embargo.\par \par \uc2 The deadlock, alongside US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision last month to impose sweeping duties on dozens of countries, has upended supply chains, roiled financial markets and stoked fears of a sharp downturn in global growth.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T09:46:31.815Z">10.46am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Biden warns Europe losing confidence in US under Trump will change course of modern history\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cmodern-day appeasement\u8221\'20\'1D in his approach to Russia and expressed fears that Europe would \u8220\'20\'1Close confidence in the certainty of America\u8221\'20\'1D in his first interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since leaving the White House in January}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe [\uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 ] believes it [Russia] has historical rights to Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0m9mvemxrwo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the BBC}}}\uc2 . Anybody who thought the Russian president would stop if Kyiv conceded territory, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/25/a-carve-up-in-gift-wrapping-trumps-peace-plan-puts-the-sacrifice-on-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as recently proposed by Trump}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cis just foolish\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Delaware as the Allied nations mark the 80th anniversary of the end of the second world war, Biden said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance was \u8220\'20\'1Cmodern-day appeasement\u8221\'20\'1D in reference to the attempts of British prime minister \uc2 Neville Chamberlain\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s to appease Adolf Hitler in the 1930s.\par \par \uc2 He also said he feared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  was going to lose confidence in the \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainty of America and the leadership of America\u8221\'20\'1D and that a breakdown of US-Europe relations under Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwould change the modern history of the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the leaders of European nations would be left \u8220\'20\'1Cwondering, well, what do I do now? \u8230\'20\'26 Can I rely on the United States? Are they going to be there?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI fear our allies around the world are going to begin to doubt whether we\u8217\'20\'19re going to stay where we\u8217\'20\'19ve always been in the last 80 years,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden told Nick Robinson that he found the{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/28/trump-zelenskyy-shouting-match-oval-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  extraordinary meeting}}}\uc2  in the Oval Office between Trump and Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbeneath America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He went on to condemn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s calls for the US to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-vows-to-take-back-panama-canal-in-us-foreign-policy-vision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 take back the Panama canal}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/06/trump-mark-carney-canada-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 make Canada the 51st American state}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/04/trump-greenland-denmark-military-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seize Greenland}}}\uc2 . <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/07/biden-accuses-trump-of-modern-day-appeasement-towards-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden accuses Trump of \u8216\'20\'18modern-day appeasement\u8217\'20\'19 towards Russia}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-07T09:46:31.815Z">10.46am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says \u8216\'20\'18we just want to be friends\u8217\'20\'19 as Canada PM torpedoes 51st state idea\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I will be bringing you the latest news lines over the next hour or so.\par \par \uc2 Firstly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  said he \u8220\'20\'1Cjust want[s] to be friends with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/canada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Canada}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D after his first post-election meeting with the country\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/mark-carney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Carney}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who used the gathering to shoot down any prospect of his country becoming the 51st state.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in the Oval Office, Trump praised Carney \u8211\'20\'13 whose Liberal party won the federal election last week \u8211\'20\'13 for one of the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreatest political comebacks of all time\u8221\'20\'1D, and described the prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s visit as \u8220\'20\'1Can honour\u8221\'20\'1D for the White House.\par \par \uc2 The amicable tone of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting marked a stark contrast with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hostile rhetoric over recent months, as he launched a trade war against his northern neighbour, belittled Carney\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/justin-trudeau"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Trudeau}}}\uc2 , and made repeated threats to crush Canada\u8217\'20\'19s economy with the aim of annexing it.\par \par \uc2 Carney returned the praise, telling Trump he was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctransformational president\u8221\'20\'1D with a strong focus on the economy. But he shot down any idea that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/canada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Canada}}}\uc2  might accede to joining the US as the 51st state \u8211\'20\'13 a proposal again floated by Trump in the meeting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs you know from real estate, there are some places that are never for sale,\u8221\'20\'1D Carney told Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s true,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving met with the owners of Canada over the course of the campaign \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s not for sale,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carney. \u8220\'20\'1CWon\u8217\'20\'19t be for sale, ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNever say never,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump. Carney smiled and mouthed \u8220\'20\'1Cnever, never, never, never.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For the full report on the meeting and further reaction, see here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/06/trump-mark-carney-canada-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says \u8216\'20\'18we just want to be friends\u8217\'20\'19 as Canada PM torpedoes 51st state idea}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US treasury secretary Scott Bessent and US trade representative Jamieson Greer will meet with their Chinese counterparts later this week in Switzerland, in what could be the first step to negotiating an end to the trade war between the world\u8217\'20\'19s two largest economies over tariffs imposed by Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bessent also contradicted a previous claim from Trump that talks with China had been going on for weeks. \u8220\'20\'1CWe haven\u8217\'20\'19t had negotiations,\u8221\'20\'1D Bessent told Fox. \u8220\'20\'1CThe world has been coming to the US, and China has been the missing piece.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump revealed to reporters that three more Israeli hostages have died in Gaza, meaning that just 21 of the hostages taken from Israel on 7 October 2023 remain alive. \u8220\'20\'1CI say 21, because, as of today, it\u8217\'20\'19s 21. Three have died,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At the White House event on the 2026 World Cup, Trump learned from a reporter that Russia is banned from taking part, as a result of its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Columbia University{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://president.columbia.edu/news/preserving-columbias-critical-research-capabilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that it laid off nearly 180 researchers in response to the Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration\u8217\'20\'19s decision to cancel $400m in funding over the Ivy League school\u8217\'20\'19s handling of student protests against the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration may deport migrants to Libya for the first time this week, three US officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/humeyra_pamuk/status/1919919219312931022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tell Reuters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250507el57001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
