\par\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Reform accused of hypocrisy after advertising home working jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 Jamie Grierson \par \uc2 350 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2025\par 01:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Several paid roles at party are not in office despite Nigel Farage\u8217\'20\'19s comments promising \u8216\'20\'18no more work from home\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Reform UK has been accused of hypocrisy after it emerged the party is advertising several jobs offering home working despite promising a clampdown on the policy.\par \par \uc2 The party\u8217\'20\'19s leader, Nigel Farage, told reporters he hoped to emulate \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge), which has attempted to slash federal spending in the US, after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/02/farage-reform-uk-local-elections-beginning-of-the-end-for-tories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record performance in the local elections}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 The party took control of 10 local authorities in England at last week\u8217\'20\'19s local elections, including Durham, Lancashire and Staffordshire. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/06/the-guardian-view-on-labours-drift-and-tory-collapse-reform-fills-a-vacuum-they-created"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Guardian view on Labour\u8217\'20\'19s drift and Tory collapse: Reform fills a vacuum they created | Editorial}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Farage said councils under Reform control could expect to see cuts in areas including work to tackle the climate crisis and to boost diversity, while he pledged to clamp down on staff working from home. The Clacton MP frequently criticised the policy on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 It has since emerged that several paid roles with the party, such as \u8220\'20\'1Cregional director\u8221\'20\'1D, are offering \u8220\'20\'1Chome working with occasional travel\u8221\'20\'1D, prompting accusations of hypocrisy on social media.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, the Labour MP \uc2 Stella Creasy\uc2  said the hypocrisy was \u8220\'20\'1Cglorious\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked what his party\u8217\'20\'19s priorities would be, Farage last week told BBC Radio 4\u8217\'20\'19s Today programme: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are deeply dissatisfied with the way that county councils and unitaries in Britain have been running their budgets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe look at the millions a year being spent, in many cases, on consultants. We look at the money being spent on climate change; on areas that county councils, frankly, shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even be getting involved in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CNo more work from home, increased productivity. That won\u8217\'20\'19t be a magic wand, it won\u8217\'20\'19t solve every problem, but it will be a good start and we\u8217\'20\'19ll be judged on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reform has been contacted for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250506el5600108\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
