\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump administration to cut thousands of jobs from CIA and other spy agencies \u8211\'20\'13 report\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 427 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2025\par 10:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 CIA to lose 1,200 while NSA among other agencies reported to face downsizing amid president\u8217\'20\'19s drive to shrink federal workforce\par \par \uc2 The White House plans to cut staffing at the \uc2 Central Intelligence Agency\uc2  by 1,200 positions while other intelligence agencies including the \uc2 National Security Agency\uc2  will also shed thousands of jobs, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has reported.\par \par \uc2 A person familiar with the plan confirmed the changes to the Associated Press on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has told members of Congress about the planned cuts at the CIA, which will take place over several years and be accomplished in part through reduced hiring as opposed to layoffs, the Post reported on Friday. The cuts include several hundred people who had already opted for early retirement, it said. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/03/trump-news-at-a-glance-president-floats-pentagon-budget-boost-army-may-hold-parade-for-his-birthday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump news at a glance: president floats Pentagon budget boost; army may hold parade for his birthday}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 In response to questions about the reductions, the CIA issued a statement saying its director, John Ratcliffe, was working to align the agency with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s national security priorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese moves are part of a holistic strategy to infuse the agency with renewed energy, provide opportunities for rising leaders to emerge, and better position CIA to deliver on its mission,\u8221\'20\'1D the agency said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the director of national intelligence, \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , did not immediately respond to a message seeking comment. Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s office oversees and coordinates the work of 18 agencies that collect and analyse intelligence.\par \par \uc2 The CIA earlier this year became the first US intelligence agency to join a voluntary redundancy program initiated by Trump, who has vowed to radically downsize the federal workforce in the name of efficiency and frugality. The NSA has already offered voluntary resignations to some employees.\par \par \uc2 The CIA has said it also plans to lay off an unknown number of recently hired employees.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has also eliminated diversity, equity and inclusion programs at intelligence agencies, though a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/21/judge-temporarily-blocks-trumps-anti-dei-purge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 judge has temporarily blocked}}}\uc2  efforts to fire 19 employees working on DEI programs who challenged their terminations.\par \par \uc2 Trump also abruptly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/04/democrats-decry-reported-dismissal-of-nsa-director-tim-haugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired the general}}}\uc2  who led the NSA and the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s Cyber Command, Tim Haugh.\par \par \uc2 Ratcliffe has vowed to overhaul the CIA and said he wants to boost the agency\u8217\'20\'19s use of intelligence from human sources and its focus on China.\par \par \uc2 With the Associated Press and Agence France-Presse\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250506el56002pv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
