\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  to cut 180 jobs due to federal grant revocations\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 526 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2025\par 15:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House axed grants even as college agreed to demands including ceding control of Middle East studies department\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/columbia-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia Universit}}}\uc2 y is slated to cut 180 staffers whose work was supported by federal grants that have now been revoked by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 , the college\u8217\'20\'19s acting president, Claire Shipman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://president.columbia.edu/news/preserving-columbias-critical-research-capabilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have had to make difficult choices and unfortunately, today, nearly 180 of our colleagues who have been working, in whole or in part, on impacted federal grants, will receive notices of non-renewal or termination,\u8221\'20\'1D Shipman said in a lengthy notice posted on Columbia\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 Staff cuts follow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.insidehighered.com/news/government/politics-elections/2025/03/07/trump-admin-cancels-400m-grants-columbia-u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancellation of $400m}}}\uc2  in federal grants and contracts to \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  because of what the Trump administration alleges is the college\u8217\'20\'19s failure to protect students from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/antisemitism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 antisemitic}}}\uc2  harassment. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2025/mar/23/antisemitism-redefinition-jewish-safety-christian-nationalism-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The new definition of antisemitism is transforming America \u8211\'20\'13 and serving a Christian nationalist plan}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 The university {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/21/columbia-university-funding-trump-demands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later yielded }}}\uc2 to a series of changes demanded by the administration, including setting up a new disciplinary committee and initiating investigations into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/06/columbia-university-students-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 students critical of Israel}}}\uc2  and the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Shipman said elsewhere in the notice that the university was continuing discussions with the federal government on funding to resume research activity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are working on and planning for every eventuality, but the strain in the meantime, financially and on our research mission, is intense,\u8221\'20\'1D Shipman wrote, adding that the university was adjusting and in some cases reducing \u8220\'20\'1Cexpenditures based on current financial realities\u8221\'20\'1D as it pursues alternative sources of funding.\par \par \uc2 Shipman said the cuts represented about 20% of the individuals who are funded in part by the terminated grants.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DWe do not make these decisions lightly. We are deeply committed, at Columbia, to the critical work of invention, innovation and discovery,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIncreasing budget constraints combined with uncertainty related to future levels of federal funding for research \u8230\'20\'26 requires us to make difficult choices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have had to make deliberate, considered decisions about the allocation of our financial resources. Those decisions also impact our greatest resource, our people. We understand this news will be hard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Columbia acquiesced to administration demands that laid out measures including banning face masks on campus, empowering security officers to remove or arrest individuals, and taking control of the department that offers courses on the Middle East from its faculty.\par \par \uc2 But the agreement did not automatically lead to a restoration of federal research funding. Despite a $14bn endowment fund, Columbia said on Tuesday that \u8220\'20\'1Cfederal actions\u8221\'20\'1D required it to look across all areas of the university for to cut costs.\par \par \uc2 The university also said it had developed programs to streamline its workforce through attrition, planned to launch a voluntary retirement incentive program, make cuts to administrative expenditures, and \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to make prudent budget decisions that will ensure long-term financial stability across the university\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a deeply challenging time across all higher education, and we are attempting to navigate through tremendous ambiguity with precision, which will be imperfect at times,\u8221\'20\'1D Shipman wrote.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250506el56002be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
