\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attack on federal unions a \u8216\'20\'18test case\u8217\'20\'19 for broader assault, warn lawyers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,088 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2025\par 18:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Executive order cites national security to strip bargaining rights from more than 1 million federal workers\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is seeking to strip collective bargaining rights from large swaths of federal employees in a test case union leaders argue is part of a broader attack on US labor unions that could land before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Trump win would deliver a severe blow to labor unions in the US. Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/union2.t03.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 29.9% }}}\uc2 of all federal workers were represented by labor unions in 2024 compared to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/pdf/union2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11.1% }}}\uc2 for all US workers.\par \par \uc2 On 27 March, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-executive-orders-signed-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued an executive order}}}\uc2 , citing national security, to exempt collective bargaining at several federal departments for more than 1 million workers.\par \par \uc2 The order was made in tandem with lawsuits filed by the Trump administration against federal unions, including against affiliates of the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2  in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/69805239/united-states-department-of-defense-v-american-federation-of-government/?order_by=desc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas court}}}\uc2  where only one judge, a conservative, presides over the court, and the \uc2 National Treasury Employees Union\uc2  chapter 73 in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pacermonitor.com/public/case/57460097/United_States_Department_of_Treasury_v_National_Treasury_Employees_Union_Chapter_73"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, unions filed motions to dismiss the lawsuits, and have filed their own lawsuits against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order. Bipartisan legislation has also been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/2550/cosponsors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  in the House to restore collective bargaining rights for targeted federal workers. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/07/trump-union-workers-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Trump and Musk are setting the example\u8217\'20\'19: how companies are becoming emboldened to be more anti-union}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Rushab Sanghvi, \uc2 AFGE\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s general counsel, expects a decision in their lawsuit against the administration next month. But he expects the four cases are likely to end up in the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Sanghvi sees the administration\u8217\'20\'19s legal action as part of a broader, authoritarian efforts against labor unions, law firms, universities and other opposition to the Trump administration. Authoritarian governments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/activism/labor-union-democracy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historically}}}\uc2 , have prioritized eliminating labor unions in consolidating power, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe stakes for the labor movement are extremely broad,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanghvi. The administration is attempting to get rid of collective bargaining in the federal sector \u8220\'20\'1Cfor anyone they think will oppose them\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s huge for our members but it\u8217\'20\'19s also huge for the labor movement as a whole because they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to stop here. They are going to go further and this is just a test. If they win here, they are just going to keep going and going until they get rid of all unions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 AFGE\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s national president, \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , called the executive order retaliatory. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 AFGE\uc2  is not going to be intimidated by a bully who is throwing a temper tantrum because our union is beating them in the court of law and in the court of public opinion,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelley said.\par \par \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest federation of labor unions in the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-stands-solidarity-unions-challenging-trump-administrations-attack-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaks federal law with an alarming and dangerous escalation of attacks on our most fundamental freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed it is a direct attack on every union, every union contract, and the right to collective bargaining in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis executive order is the very definition of union-busting,\u8221\'20\'1D Shuler {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-president-federal-collective-bargaining-executive-order-very-definition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 AFGE\uc2  and other federal employee unions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/unions-sue-trump-administration-over-move-to-bust-federal-employee-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  a lawsuit in California alleging the order is retaliation for unions speaking out against the administration\u8217\'20\'19s actions.\par \par \uc2 On 21 April, \uc2 AFGE\uc2  affiliates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://glaunion.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/gov.uscourts.txwd_.1172831290.41.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  a motion to dismiss the Trump administration lawsuit in Texas, noting the lawsuit was filed before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order was even made public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe government drafted an executive order and, before the subjects of that order even knew what it said, sued them, doing so before any actual controversy could have possibly existed,\u8221\'20\'1D the motion to dismiss stated.\par \par \uc2 NTEU\uc2  chapter 73 has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pacermonitor.com/public/case/57460097/United_States_Department_of_Treasury_v_National_Treasury_Employees_Union_Chapter_73"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  a motion to dismiss the lawsuit filed against them by the Trump administration in Kentucky on 21 April.\par \par \uc2 The union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nteu.org/-/media/Files/nteu/docs/public/2025/NTEU%20v%20Trump%20PI%204425.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order has nothing to do with national security, but rather is based on \u8220\'20\'1Ca desire to make federal employees easier to fire and to weaken federal sector unions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the lawsuit over the order filed by \uc2 NTEU\uc2  against the Trump administration in Washington DC, federal judge Paul Friedman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://federalnewsnetwork.com/congress/2025/04/judge-blocks-trump-administration-from-nixing-collective-bargaining-for-most-federal-employees/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted}}}\uc2  a preliminary injunction blocking the executive order on 25 April and gave attorneys until 2 May to provide a proposal for how the case should proceed.\par \par \uc2 Suzanne Summerlin, a labor attorney in Washington DC, criticized the lawsuits by the Trump administration, noting the lawsuit in Kentucky was not properly filed, served to the wrong party and demanding rulings \u8220\'20\'1Cbefore any real legal defense can be mounted\u8221\'20\'1D, accusing the attempt and judge\u8217\'20\'19s actions in the case of being a \u8220\'20\'1Cbreakdown\u8221\'20\'1D of basic legal norms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are a full-scale assault on the rights of federal workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Summerlin. \u8220\'20\'1CThrough a sweeping executive order, the Trump administration is attempting to strip collective bargaining rights from entire agencies, declaring that large swaths of the federal workforce are, now, for the first time, after decades of union representation, somehow too \u8216\'20\'18sensitive\u8217\'20\'19 for union representation, with no individualized analysis and no due process.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/28/trump-order-union-rights-federal-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Organizers accuse Trump of trying to silence federal workers with union order}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 She added the lawsuits \u8220\'20\'1Care part of a broader strategy\u8221\'20\'1D to silence federal workers, dismantle their unions, and remove their legal protections, and noted the lawsuits filed by the Trump administration, in Texas and Kentucky, are likely filed in these locations to find a favorable judge to their lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 In the Kentucky lawsuit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://summerlinlabor-my.sharepoint.com/:w:/p/suzanne/EZe2by7UL8hMrgH4F3k9-4kBk6LCJenfEIuHsey-NFvTtQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  against \uc2 National Treasury Employees Union\uc2  chapter 73 rather than the national union in Washington DC, she noted the lawsuit was not properly served to the union, and a continuance request was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/treasury-seeks-friendly-court-in-suit-with-federal-worker-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  by the judge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLegal observers should be raising serious concerns about judicial ethics, forum manipulation, and due process violations,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf this tactic succeeds, any organization, not just unions, could be sued in an unfriendly venue, not served, and still be expected to argue for its rights on the merits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 White House deputy press secretary Anna Kelly did not comment on the motions to dismiss the lawsuits. In an email following the executive order, the White House said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe administration filed a lawsuit to preserve its legal rights against unlawful attempts to curtail the President\u8217\'20\'19s authority. Employees in certain agencies that deal with national security, intelligence, counterintelligence, or investigative functions may not unionize to slow or halt the President\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250501el51001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
