\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Famed Memphis church associated with \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2  damaged by fire\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts \par \uc2 601 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2025\par 23:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Clayborn Temple, base for sanitation workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike that brought King to Memphis in 1968, suffers extensive damage\par \par \uc2 A fire has severely damaged the historic Clayborn Temple in downtown Memphis, which is closely associated with the US civil rights movement and Dr \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The temple was headquarters for the sanitation workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike that brought King to Memphis in 1968. The campaign\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CI Am a Man\u8221\'20\'1D signs were made in the church\u8217\'20\'19s basement, according to the temple\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clayborn.org/about-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website. }}}\par \par \uc2 In 2018, it was designated a national treasure by the \uc2 National Trust for Historic Preservation\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The Memphis fire department chief, Gina Sweat, said at a news conference that the department received a call at about 1.30am local time on Monday morning through a commercial alarm.\par \par \uc2 The blaze was largely contained within an hour, she said, but there were still some hotspots so firefighters will remain on site working throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 The temple had \u8220\'20\'1Csustained significant damage\u8221\'20\'1D, Sweat said, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating fire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDue to the significant damage, we could not go inside the building at that point, so we\u8217\'20\'19re having to fight the fire, the rest of it, from the outside,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Investigators from the fire department, police and the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2  (ATF) were working to determine the cause of the fire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to take some time due to the significant damage to the structure,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s still an active investigation and we\u8217\'20\'19re working diligently and thoroughly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sweat described Clayborn Temple as \u8220\'20\'1Csacred and significant to our entire community\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Memphis\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Paul Young, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CityofMem_Media/status/1916853448563155411?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1916853448563155411%7Ctwgr%5E1162afb81df990a727f26c4f2f69501ffc68e0e7%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newsweek.com%2Fmemphis-church-fire-clayborn-temple-2065040"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  that the fire had \u8220\'20\'1Cravaged one of our city\u8217\'20\'19s greatest treasures\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClayborn is more than a historic building,\u8221\'20\'1D Young said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is sacred ground. It is the beating heart of the civil rights movement, a symbol of struggle, hope and triumph that belongs not just to Memphis but to the world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStanding in the shadow of that steeple, generations of Memphians found their courage,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CToday, in the face of this tragedy, we must find ours once again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe grieve deeply for what has been lost, but we also stand ready to honor Clayborn\u8217\'20\'19s legacy the only way we know how: by coming together to restore, rebuild, and remember.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The National Civil Rights Museum also released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.actionnews5.com/2025/04/28/historic-church-lost-fire-hernando-street-mfd-crews-scene/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2 , describing the temple as a \u8220\'20\'1Csymbol of organized resistance and hope during the 1968 sanitation workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen marchers filled its sanctuary, it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just about better wages; it was about dignity, about declaring that Black lives and labor mattered in a city that often acted indifferent,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement read.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the years since, despite cycles of neglect and efforts at preservation, Clayborn Temple remained a powerful reminder that in the face of obstacles, violence, and hatred, collective action and faith can build something stronger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 King\u8217\'20\'19s eldest son, \uc2 Martin Luther King III\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/OfficialMLK3/status/1916891460613407086"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply saddened by the devastating fire that destroyed the historic Clayborn Temple in Memphis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CClayborn was the starting point for the sanitation workers\u8217\'20\'19 march where my father stood and helped lift up the words \u8216\'20\'18I Am a Man\u8217\'20\'19 to the world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe flames that consumed Clayborn Temple cannot erase its legacy as sacred ground. We honor its history and we are committed to supporting efforts to rebuild this cornerstone of the civil rights movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to local newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commercialappeal.com/story/news/local/2025/04/28/clayborn-templememphis-destroyed-fire/83323040007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Commercial Appeal }}}\uc2 , the temple had been undergoing years of renovations to preserve its structure.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250428el4s003h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
