\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harvard labor unions rally behind non-citizens and workers amid Trump attacks\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 556 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 April 2025\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As Trump administration escalates threats on university, unions call on Harvard leadership to support workers\par \par \uc2 Labor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unions }}}\uc2  and allied organizations representing students, staff, researchers and faculty at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/harvard-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard University }}}\uc2  are holding a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/hgsuuaw/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally }}}\uc2  on 27 April on campus to raise awareness and support for the role workers at the university have in research and education on campus in the face of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2025/apr/19/harvard-trump-administration-timeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacks on the university }}}\uc2  by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The unions have supported Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s stand against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/14/trump-harvard-funding-freeze"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 funding freezes }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2025/apr/16/trump-harvard-funding-threat-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threats to the university }}}\uc2  and are calling on school leadership to work with them, including at the bargaining table, to uphold and support their work and safety.\par \par \uc2 Harvard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2025/apr/21/harvard-sues-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit }}}\uc2  against the Trump administration this past week to block a federal funding freeze of $2.2bn in grants, arguing the freeze violates its first amendment right of academic independence. Harvard officials also refused to comply with demands from the Trump administration that included the appointment of an outside overseer to ensure \u8220\'20\'1Cdiverse\u8221\'20\'1D viewpoints were being taught at the school amid threats to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2025/apr/14/harvard-university-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 review $9bn }}}\uc2  in federal grants and contracts to Harvard.\par \par \uc2 Harvard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecrimson.com/article/2025/3/10/harvard-hiring-freeze/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enacted }}}\uc2  a university-wide hiring freeze in March 2025 in response to uncertainty over the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s actions. The unions noted time caps on the number of years faculty are permitted to teach at Harvard, coupled with the hiring freeze, is resulting in the elimination of small language programs at the university and increases to class sizes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy colleagues, who teach everything from African history to physics to Chinese language courses, are beloved teachers and mentors. But many of them will lose their jobs and be deported at the end of this semester, and no one will be hired to replace them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jules Riegel, a time-capped lecturer in history and literature at Harvard. \u8220\'20\'1CMany fields of study will vanish, and many languages simply won\u8217\'20\'19t be offered.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alexis Miranda, a graduate worker at the \uc2 Harvard School of Public Health\uc2  , added research such as theirs on LGBTQ+ and racial disparities in breast cancer is among the most targeted for cuts by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs students and researchers, we need Harvard to step up and support the areas of research most targeted by the latest funding cuts, including LGBTQ+ health and racial disparities research, so that this vital work can continue,\u8221\'20\'1D Miranda stated.\par \par \uc2 The rally also includes a call for Harvard to protect the non-citizens at Harvard in student and worker roles and assert they have constitutional rights, as non-citizens are being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/apr/25/donald-trump-china-tariffs-global-trade-pete-hegseth-us-politics-latest-updates-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted }}}\uc2  by the Trump administration with the revocation of student visas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring the COVID-19 pandemic, international workers demonstrated their unwavering commitment to the Harvard community, ensuring its safety while risking their own lives and the wellbeing of their families. Now, it is the university\u8217\'20\'19s turn to stand in solidarity with these individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D said Doris Reina-Landaverde, a custodian, shop steward of 32BJ \uc2 SEIU\uc2  , and a temporary protected status holder from El Salvador. \u8220\'20\'1CToday, 1.5 million temporary protected status beneficiaries \u8211\'20\'13 many of whom work tirelessly to uphold the safety and vibrancy of institutions like Harvard \u8211\'20\'13 face uncertainty and the potential loss of their status, just as international students do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harvard was contacted for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250426el4q0018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
