nd no one will be hired to replace them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jules Riegel, a time-capped lecturer in history and literature at Harvard. \u8220\'20\'1CMany fields of study will vanish, and many languages simply won\u8217\'20\'19t be offered.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alexis Miranda, a graduate worker at the \uc2 Harvard School of Public Health\uc2 , added research such as theirs on LGBTQ+ and racial disparities in breast cancer is among the most targeted for cuts by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs students and researchers, we need Harvard to step up and support the areas of research most targeted by the latest funding cuts, including LGBTQ+ health and racial disparities research, so that this vital work can continue,\u8221\'20\'1D Miranda stated. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/07/trump-union-workers-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Trump and Musk are setting the example\u8217\'20\'19: how companies are becoming emboldened to be more anti-union}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 The rally also includes a call for Harvard to protect the non-citizens at Harvard in student and worker roles and assert they have constitutional rights, as non-citizens are being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/apr/25/donald-trump-china-tariffs-global-trade-pete-hegseth-us-politics-latest-updates-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted}}}\uc2  by the Trump administration with the revocation of student visas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring the COVID-19 pandemic, international workers demonstrated their unwavering commitment to the Harvard community, ensuring its safety while risking their own lives and the wellbeing of their families. Now, it is the university\u8217\'20\'19s turn to stand in solidarity with these individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D said Doris Reina-Landaverde, a custodian, shop steward