\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US federal agency texts Barnard College employees to ask if they\u8217\'20\'19re Jewish\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts \par \uc2 1,238 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2025\par 19:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees received text from \uc2 EEOC\uc2  on personal phones linking to survey asking if they are Jewish or Israeli\par \par \uc2 Employees from Barnard College received text messages this week from the federally run \uc2 Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2  (\uc2 EEOC\uc2 ) on their personal phones linking to a voluntary survey asking recipients if they are Jewish or Israeli and whether they have been subjected to harassment or antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 The text, which was reviewed by the Guardian, states that the civil rights agency is \u8220\'20\'1Ccurrently reviewing the employment practices at Barnard College\u8221\'20\'1D and invites current and former employees to complete the linked survey. It is not clear how many college employees received the survey, but it appears to have been sent to a sizable portion of the faculty and other staff.\par \par \uc2 The survey, which appeared to be part of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive investigations into American colleges and universities over antisemitism allegations stemming from pro-Palestinian protests, sparked anxiety among some recipients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of the stated intent, this survey in effect creates a list of Jewish faculty, staff and students at Barnard,\u8221\'20\'1D said Elizabeth Bauer, a Barnard professor and chair of the college\u8217\'20\'19s biology department, who said she was alarmed by the message.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe government is also now requiring undocumented immigrants, including children, to register with DHS. I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen this movie before and I\u8217\'20\'19m horrified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The survey asked whether the respondent currently works at Barnard or has ever been employed there and prompted respondents to select all that apply of the choices: \u8220\'20\'1CI am Jewish\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CI am Israeli\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CI have shared Jewish/Israeli ancestry\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CI practice Judaism\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1COther\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Another question asked: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile working at Barnard College, were you subjected to any of the following because you practice Judaism, have Jewish ancestry, are Israeli, and/or are associated with an individual(s) who is Jewish and/or Israeli?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Respondents could select from options including, \u8220\'20\'1Cunwelcome comments, jokes or discussions\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Charassment, intimidation\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cpressure to abandon, change or adopt a practice or religious belief\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cantisemitic or anti-Israeli protests, gatherings or demonstrations that made you feel threatened, harassed or were otherwise disruptive to your working environment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Other questions asked the respondents\u8217\'20\'19 employment details, supervisor name, date of hire and more.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Hutchinson, an associate professor of American Art History at Barnard, a women\u8217\'20\'19s college affiliated with \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , said when she received the message on her personal phone at 5.39pm ET on Monday, her initial reaction was: \u8220\'20\'1CThis must be some kind of scam, because, how could the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  have my contact information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The message addressed her by name and, initially, Hutchinson said, she didn\u8217\'20\'19t open the links.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was frightened, and wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure what it entailed,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Celia Naylor, a professor in the Africana studies department at Barnard College, also received the message on Monday. She quickly discovered that \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of people I know \u8211\'20\'13 faculty and even some staff \u8211\'20\'13 also received it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As many faculty and staff tried to verify the message\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy in group chats on Monday evening, Barnard\u8217\'20\'19s general counsel, Serena Longley, sent an email about the messages.\par \par \uc2 Longley explained in the email, which was viewed by the Guardian, that the college had \u8220\'20\'1Creceived multiple reports that some employees have received text messages from the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  inviting them to complete a voluntary survey\u8221\'20\'1D. She also said Barnard, Longley \u8220\'20\'1Cwas not given advance notice of this outreach\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CParticipation is entirely voluntary. If you choose to respond, please know that both federal law and Barnard policy strictly prohibit any form of retaliation,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued.\par \par \uc2 Longley sent a follow-up email to Barnard employees on Wednesday, which was also reviewed by the Guardian, explaining that the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  launched an investigation last summer against Barnard \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerning whether or not the College discriminated against Jewish employees on the basis of their national origin, religion and/or race in violation of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBarnard prides itself on being an inclusive and respectful workplace for all people, including our Jewish employees, and has been robustly defending the College against this \uc2 EEOC\uc2  inquiry,\u8221\'20\'1D Longley wrote, adding that the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Clegally entitled to obtain the contact information of Barnard employees so that it could offer employees the option to voluntarily participate in their investigation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBarnard complied with this lawful request,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The college heard from current and former employees in recent days who asked to be notified in advance before their contact information is shared, the email also noted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGoing forward,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cif and when we are required to provide information about staff in connection with an investigation or litigation, we will provide you with advance notice unless we are subject to a court order that prohibits us from doing so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Longley also emphasized that participation in the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  survey was voluntary.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CPer federal law, we cannot comment on investigations, nor can we confirm or deny the existence of an investigation.\u8221\'20\'1D Barnard did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 After hearing others discuss its content, Hutchinson finally opened the survey on Wednesday and found it \u8220\'20\'1Cutterly shocking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very clearly a fishing expedition,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, before noting that the survey \u8220\'20\'1Cis clearly presuming guilt and looking for very specific kinds of evidence for their case\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson also said that while she was grateful for the information provided in Barnard\u8217\'20\'19s emails this week, she felt that they did not \u8220\'20\'1Cacknowledge the reality that the faculty are experiencing a heightened surveillance of our campus that is now intruding into our personal devices on our personal time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 To Hutchinson, the message on Monday was \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D has \u8220\'20\'1Creally ramped up the unease on campus\u8221\'20\'1D, with faculty now feeling vulnerable both in their classrooms and now in their private spaces too.\par \par \uc2 Naylor echoed that faculty, students and staff were concerned about how their personal information was being used by Barnard, and shared with federal agencies. They are unsure of what other personal details have been provided.\par \par \uc2 Debbie Becher, a Barnard sociology professor who is Jewish, spoke to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/23/nyregion/barnard-faculty-eeoc-text-jewish.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times }}}\uc2 this week about the text message and survey, saying that she found it \u8220\'20\'1Ca bit terrifying\u8221\'20\'1D that the federal government \u8220\'20\'1Cwants to know who the Jews are through some text message and Microsoft Office form\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bauer said that not all of the Barnard faculty and staff received the message, adding that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cunclear\u8221\'20\'1D why some did not receive it and others did.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was obvious that the survey was a fishing expedition by the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  to find Title VII violations,\u8221\'20\'1D Bauer said.\par \par \uc2 Colin Wayne Leach, a professor of psychology and Africana Studies at Barnard College, said that \u8220\'20\'1Cas a dean focused on supporting our faculty\u8221\'20\'1D, he had been hearing from many colleagues this week who are upset about the messages.\par \par \uc2 They were \u8220\'20\'1Csurprised\u8221\'20\'1D that the \uc2 EEOC\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwould choose this informal, unannounced, and intrusive way to ask employees to complete a survey on their experiences of such an important topic as anti-semitism at their place of work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Spectator, Columbia\u8217\'20\'19s University paper, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.columbiaspectator.com/news/2025/04/23/eeoc-sends-texts-to-columbia-and-barnard-employees-asking-them-to-complete-survey-for-title-vii-investigation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Wednesday that several members of Columbia\u8217\'20\'19s faculty also received the text message from \uc2 EEOC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Kobrin, co-director of the Institute for Israel and Jewish Studies (IIJS), told the Spectator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.columbiaspectator.com/news/2025/04/23/eeoc-sends-texts-to-columbia-and-barnard-employees-asking-them-to-complete-survey-for-title-vii-investigation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that she and other members of IIJS received}}}\uc2  the message.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250430el4o00324\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
