\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump administration has set Noaa on \u8216\'20\'18non-science trajectory\u8217\'20\'19, workers warn\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2025\par 16:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Researchers left at US climate agency say drastic cuts could leave air \u8216\'20\'18not breathable\u8217\'20\'19 and water \u8216\'20\'18not drinkable\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has shunted one of the \uc2 US federal government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top scientific agencies onto a \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-science trajectory\u8221\'20\'1D, workers warn, that threatens to derail decades of research and leave the US with \u8220\'20\'1Cair that\u8217\'20\'19s not breathable and water that\u8217\'20\'19s not drinkable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Workers and scientists at the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2  (Noaa) are warning of the drastic impacts of cuts at the agency on science, research, and efforts to protect natural resources.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe problems are still there. We still have harmful algal blooms, we still have fisheries that are collapsing, waters you can\u8217\'20\'19t swim in. These problems don\u8217\'20\'19t go away because we fired all the people who were trying to solve a problem,\u8221\'20\'1D said one Noaa veteran, who wished to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CHow do you save the arms and legs or the feet and hands when the core is dying?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The longtime research scientist with more than 20 years at \uc2 Noaa\uc2  has taken early retirement. \u8220\'20\'1CI left because it was just so demoralizing and fearful and scary,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 Trump administration officials are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/11/climate/noaa-research-budget-cuts.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking}}}\uc2  to abolish the scientific research division at Noaa, the Oceanic and Atmospheric Research (Oar) office. It is the latest of a series of cuts at the agency that began the second Trump administration with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.noaa.gov/about-our-agency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 12,000 employees}}}\uc2  around the world, including more than 6,700 engineers and scientists.\par \par \uc2 The cuts are disrupting the collection of data sets, including recordings of global temperatures in the air and ocean, and that data cannot be replaced, said the Noaa veteran.\par \par \uc2 The dismantling of Noaa, they said, would harm work in many areas, from finding solutions to combat harmful algae and improving sustainable fisheries to work on new medicines and industrial products and collecting information for disaster preparation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can look at other countries that are actively making these mistakes, where they have air that\u8217\'20\'19s not breathable and water that\u8217\'20\'19s not drinkable,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s done. I think this is done. The enemies are in the gate. I don\u8217\'20\'19t see any indication so far of anyone stopping it. They\u8217\'20\'19re just letting it burn. I honestly don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how US science will recover.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/10/noaa-firings-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 800}}}\uc2  probationary employees at the agency were fired, reinstated, then refired this month. Employees have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://peer.org/noaa-probationers-endure-insults-piled-atop-injuries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  having their firings backdated and having their health insurance canceled even though premiums were being taken out of their paychecks.\par \par \uc2 Rachel Brittin, worked as the federal deputy director of external affairs at Noaa before she was fired, then reinstated, then fired again as a probationary employee, with just a few months left on her two-year probation.\par \par \uc2 The loss of anybody at Noaa is directly connected to services lost by every individual in the United States\par \par \uc2 Rachel Brittin, Noaa\u8217\'20\'19s former federal deputy director of external affairs\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe whole situation is a mess,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHow is Noaa going to be able to keep up with the services it provides? I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how that\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen, but it\u8217\'20\'19s very scary to me. The loss of anybody at Noaa is directly connected to services lost by every individual in the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Contractors for the agency have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/bret-folger-b49a8b196_opentowork-activity-7316201334695763968-wvfX/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAABX0EmsBNRUZEVXRQZ25DjSs8nSmSdS-1ks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furloughed}}}\uc2  as all Noaa contracts over $100,000 have to now be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/04/01/noaa-commerce-department-contracts-weather-climate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Department of Commerce secretary, Howard Lutnick.\par \par \uc2 Doge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://doge.gov/savings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slated}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ripbs.org/news-and-culture/doge-considering-canceling-key-noaa-building-leases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 31 offices}}}\uc2  and building leases at Noaa for termination around the US. Nearly $4m in funding to \uc2 Princeton University\uc2  as part of a cooperative agreement with \uc2 Noaa\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/10/trump-administration-cuts-princeton-climate-research-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelled}}}\uc2  on 8 April.\par \par \uc2 Fourteen Noaa data services on earthquakes, marine, coastal and estuary science at have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eos.org/research-and-developments/noaa-datasets-will-soon-disappear#:~:text=NOAA%20has%20quietly%20reported%20that,early-%20to%20mid-May."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slated}}}\uc2  for decommissioning, more than twice as many as in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Four regional climate centers providing weather analysis tools and data for 21 states in the US have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-04-17/us-weather-analysis-for-21-states-goes-dark-after-funding-lapse?accessToken=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzb3VyY2UiOiJTdWJzY3JpYmVyR2lmdGVkQXJ0aWNsZSIsImlhdCI6MTc0NDkxNDc4OSwiZXhwIjoxNzQ1NTE5NTg5LCJhcnRpY2xlSWQiOiJTVVZDVVBEV0xVNjgwMCIsImJjb25uZWN0SWQiOiJDODQyRERFMUM0RDI0OUVDQUQ5REU4NDhDQkZGNUNBOCJ9.Qn9AuYPcRbdaqaW7q-Wwwqzb3gaqI6x4mZPF4Habqg0&leadSource=uverify%20wall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gone dark}}}\uc2  after lapses in funding, with the remaining two covering the US set to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7318694400451137537/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 face}}}\uc2  a funding lapse in June.\par \par \uc2 A reduction in force plan to cut an additional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/fired-rehired-and-fired-again-noaa-employees-are-caught-in-a-liminal-state#:~:text=A%20reduction%2Din%2Dforce%20plan,workforce%2C%20is%20on%20the%20horizon."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  10%}}}\uc2  of the agency\u8217\'20\'19s workforce is anticipated and at least several hundred workers have taken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commerce.gov/hr/2025-department-wide-vera/vsip-faqs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voluntary buyouts}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/doug-helton-0514b37_dear-friends-and-colleagues-my-time-at-activity-7319079937154433024-PMPO?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAABX0EmsBNRUZEVXRQZ25DjSs8nSmSdS-1ks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early retirement}}}\uc2  according to Noaa workers interviewed by the Guardian, though Noaa and the Department of Commerce did not disclose the numbers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems clear that the actions that have been taken have intentionally reduced our ability to do our jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D said a Noaa scientist who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re not expected to get anything done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They said due to firings, early retirements and resignations, scientific research teams around the agency have been left with gaps of expertise that can\u8217\'20\'19t be replaced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are scrambling,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are finding workarounds, but its becoming increasingly difficult.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Marty Kardos, a research molecular geneticist at the northwest fisheries science center at Noaa, decided to resign after the agency\u8217\'20\'19s violations of their collective bargaining agreement with workers meant he would be forced to move from Montana to Seattle in a week or resign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe agency is on a non-science trajectory,\u8221\'20\'1D Kardos said, speaking in a personal capacity. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the plans for research we were making for the upcoming years are out of the window. Morale is extremely bad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The attrition of scientists and management at \uc2 Noaa\uc2  is effectively undermining the agency\u8217\'20\'19s ability to sustainably manage fisheries and identify and recover endangered species, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe agency is essentially, openly hostile to their mission and their people,\u8221\'20\'1D Kardos added. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of this seems to be related to deregulation. The agency is responsible for the Endangered Species Act for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species-directory/threatened-endangered"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marine species}}}\uc2  and one way to hamstring the act without repealing it is to get rid of the scientists who help to implement it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re just letting it burn. I honestly don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how US science will recover\par \par \uc2 Noaa scientist\par \par \uc2 The cuts come as the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) and the Trump administration have installed allies in key positions at the agency.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/05/trump-neil-jacobs-noaa-sharpiegate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Neil Jacobs}}}\uc2 , the Trump nominee for Noaa administrator and acting head of Noaa in the first Trump administration, has yet to be confirmed. Jacobs was caught up in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/sep/04/trump-hurricane-dorian-alabama-sharpie-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSharpiegate\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a bizarre 2019 incident when the White House was accused of altering a Noaa map of the predicted path of Hurricane Dorian with a black marker to support an incorrect claim by Trump that the Florida-bound storm would also hit Alabama.\par \par \uc2 A staffer from Doge, Bryton Shang, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/in/brytonshang/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  this month he was appointed as a senior adviser to the Noaa administrator. Shang was one of the two Doge staffers who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/musk-doge-california-water-wildfires-b2711228.html?utm_source=reddit.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flew}}}\uc2  to Los Angeles during the wildfires in January, and attempted to open a large water pump system in California.\par \par \uc2 Erik Noble, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eenews.net/articles/official-dubbed-trumps-eyes-and-ears-is-back-at-noaa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dubbed}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ceyes and ears\u8221\'20\'1D at Noaa during his first administration, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.noaa.gov/about/organization/noaa-organization-chart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back}}}\uc2  at the agency as deputy assistant secretary for oceans and atmosphere and is reviewing contracts at the agency with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/in/keegan-mclaughlin-6673a31bb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keegan McLaughlin}}}\uc2 , a special assistant at the commerce department and former intern for the 2024 Trump campaign.\par \par \uc2 Noaa was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/08/trump-project-2025-hurricanes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 target of Project 2025}}}\uc2 , the conservative roadmap for a second Trump administration. That document pushed to \u8220\'20\'1Cbreak up \uc2 NOAA\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and labeled the agency \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the main drivers of the climate change alarm industry\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnderstanding things lets us make decisions that can put us on a track to things getting better. Knowing bad news doesn\u8217\'20\'19t create the bad news. It lets you be prepared to take actions that may let you avoid the worst consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D the Noaa scientist at Oar added on the Trump appointees and the authority they are being given over scientific decisions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPretending that our resources are inexhaustible doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make them inexhaustible,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think people understand the arrogance of thinking: \u8216\'20\'18Hey, I think I understand this, even though I know nothing about it.\u8217\'20\'19 This whole antithesis to experts, I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand it. Would you want to do that with your own personal health? Why would you do it with any kind of complex system?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Noaa and the Department of Commerce did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250423el4n00291\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
