\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 UK manufacturers to cut jobs \u8216\'20\'18within weeks unless ministers can strike trade deal\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Jillian Ambrose Energy correspondent \par \uc2 533 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2025\par 01:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 11\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bosses from automotive, manufacturing and energy warned MPs about effect of Trump tariffs\par \par \uc2 Britain\u8217\'20\'19s manufacturers will start cutting jobs \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin weeks\u8221\'20\'1D unless the government can strike a deal to safeguard the UK economy from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trade war, industry leaders have told MPs.\par \par \uc2 Senior executives from the UK\u8217\'20\'19s automotive, manufacturing and energy sectors warned a committee of MPs to expect job losses this summer if the US moves ahead with a swathe of global trade tariffs set out by Trump earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The stark warning has emerged as the chancellor, \uc2 Rachel Reeves\uc2 , travels to the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/apr/21/rachel-reeves-case-for-free-global-trade-washington-imf-talks-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to hold her first in-person meeting}}}\uc2  with her American counterpart, Scott Bessent, about striking a new trade agreement to soften the blow of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s looming trade war.\par \par \uc2 Otherwise, the \uc2 UK government\uc2  may need to put in place {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2021/feb/25/covid-furlough-workers-uk-hospitality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Covid-style furlough scheme}}}\uc2  to cover the wages of those likely to lose their jobs this summer, the industry figures said.\par \par \uc2 Mike Hawes\uc2 , the chief executive of the \uc2 Society of Motor Manufacturers and Traders\uc2  (SMMT), said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s moves to upend the global economy were likely to have a \u8220\'20\'1Csevere, significant and immediate\u8221\'20\'1D impact on high-end UK carmakers which serve the US market.\par \par \uc2 He said that lay-offs for carmakers including Rolls-Royce, Bentley, Aston Martin and McLaren would be a last resort to avoid losing \u8220\'20\'1Chighly talented people\u8221\'20\'1D but that would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca question of weeks rather than months\u8221\'20\'1D before job losses begin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe impact is now, which is why we need to make sure either we get a deal very quickly or there is a mechanism to support the industry in the coming weeks and months,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Hawes urged ministers to \u8220\'20\'1Clook again\u8221\'20\'1D at the government furlough scheme, which was used to support workers hard-hit by the impact of the Covid pandemic \u8220\'20\'1Cas a temporary measure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The warnings were echoed by \uc2 Stephen Phipson\uc2 , the chief executive of Make UK, a trade group for manufacturers, who said that companies could start laying off staff by the summer if the UK cannot secure a deal with the US to soften its tariffs of 10% on all goods as well as 25% tariffs on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/11/trump-double-canada-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 steel, aluminium}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/mar/28/which-uk-carmakers-will-be-hit-hardest-by-trumps-latest-import-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cars}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US trade tariffs put in place less than three weeks ago has prompted some manufacturers to cut agency workers and temporary roles, according to \uc2 Steve Turner\uc2 , the assistant general secretary of the \uc2 union Unite\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The looming impact of the trade tariffs threatens to compound the challenges facing UK manufacturers, which face {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/apr/20/why-the-uks-electricity-costs-are-so-high-and-what-can-be-done-about-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some of the highest energy costs in the world}}}\uc2  due to the UK\u8217\'20\'19s heavy reliance on gas.\par \par \uc2 Alan Johnson, a senior executive at \uc2 Nissan\uc2 , told the MPs that the carmaker\u8217\'20\'19s Sunderland factory is one of its most efficient but \u8220\'20\'1Cpays more for its electricity than any other \uc2 Nissan\uc2  plant in the world\u8221\'20\'1D. He said the UK was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a competitive place to be building cars today\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The executives called on ministers to follow through on its plan to put forward its modern industrial strategy alongside plans to drive down energy costs.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250422el4m002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
