\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses administrator confessed child abuse without substantial consequence, lawsuit says\b0\par\par\uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas in New Orleans \par \uc2 1,597 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2025\par 11:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Barry Davis says Joseph Fitzgerald Hall molested him in the 90s, yet Hall kept working for the church nearly unimpeded\par \par \uc2 A US man serving in various administrative roles for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/jehovahs-witnesses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses}}}\uc2  sexually molested a child whom he met while working for the Christian religious sect in New Orleans \u8211\'20\'13 then continued his career virtually unimpeded and moved to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2  after completing a disciplinary suspension of less than a year, he has admitted in writing and in a sworn deposition.\par \par \uc2 The stunning revelations about Joseph Fitzgerald Hall and how he has been managed by the Watchtower Bible and Tract Society of New York that runs the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses are contained in a lawsuit that the abuse survivor has been pursuing against both the group and the administrator.\par \par \uc2 In a recent interview, the survivor, Barry Davis, explained that one of his main reasons for coming forward was to ensure the congregation that Hall later joined in Charlotte, North Carolina, knew the full truth about him. Hall, while testifying under oath in the course of the lawsuit, acknowledged that\u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no requirement to tell someone why you were disfellowshipped\u8221\'20\'1D, which is the term to describe the suspension he served over his abuse of Davis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey should know out there,\u8221\'20\'1D Davis said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis needs to be exposed to anybody it needs to be exposed to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Davis, now 46, also said he shed his anonymity to support others who for years have been speaking out about child abuse within the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses. He contended that the evidence in his case \u8220\'20\'1Cjust kind of drives the nail in\u8221\'20\'1D about the reality of the issue.\par \par \uc2 In his opinion, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CNothing\u8217\'20\'19s changed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 About 8.5 million people globally are active members of the denomination, a primary tenet of which is that the world\u8217\'20\'19s destruction is imminent.\par \par \uc2 Hall, now 60, did not respond to requests for comment about his admissions. In a statement, an attorney representing the Watchtower Society, Billy Gibbens, maintained \u8220\'20\'1Cthe actions of the accused in this lawsuit were his own and contrary to the beliefs and practices of Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe alleged criminal acts occurred outside the scope of any religious activities assigned to the accused by the local congregation,\u8221\'20\'1D Gibbens\u8217\'20\'19 statement said.\par \par \uc2 Gibbens said his side could not elaborate while the case was pending in court. But he also wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is deeply distressing whenever anyone falls victim to such a heinous crime and sin. My clients deeply empathize with all victims of abuse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As he tells it, Davis was about nine when he met Hall, roughly aged 24, through a Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses congregation in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-orleans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Orleans}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Central City neighborhood. Hall promised Davis that he would mold him into one of the so-called Dryades congregation\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cnext great\u8221\'20\'1D leaders if the boy listened properly, according to the plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 But instead, the lawsuit argued, Hall exploited his positions as a ministerial servant and later as an elder within the congregation to get close to Davis. Hall held private Bible studies with Davis, brought him along as he proselytized to potential new converts and shared religious articles from the Watchtower Society with him.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit said Hall ultimately took advantage of that proximity to rape Davis and inflict other sexually abusive acts on him from 1990 to 1996, beginning when the boy was 11. Hall would tell Davis that 12 \u8220\'20\'1Cwas the age of accountability\u8221\'20\'1D, and therefore the boy bore fault for his molestation, the lawsuit said.\par \par \uc2 Davis recalled disclosing his abuse to his mother \u8211\'20\'13 who was a single parent \u8211\'20\'13 along with another elder at their congregation \u8211\'20\'13 by 1998. In February of that year, the elder initiated a type of disciplinary hearing that the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses refer to as a \u8220\'20\'1Cjudicial committee\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Multiple congregation elders who formed part of the committee heard Davis deliver an account of the molestation he endured at the hands of Hall. The committee subsequently disfellowshipped Hall for 11 months \u8211\'20\'13 during which time he was in effect suspended from the congregation \u8211\'20\'13 before he was allowed to return, the lawsuit said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the lawsuit added, the committee instructed Davis to \u8220\'20\'1Crepent\u8221\'20\'1D and quit his \u8220\'20\'1Chomosexual lifestyle\u8221\'20\'1D. The group prohibited Davis from carrying the microphone at congregation gatherings, working behind the literature counter or leading trips to proselytize to prospective new members, along with other privileges.\par \par \uc2 And crucially, the lawsuit said, it ordered Davis to cooperate with the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses in keeping what Hall had done to him secret because it would impugn the sect if word got out. The lawsuit asserted such an instruction violated laws in Louisiana which require religious organizations such as the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses to report any suspected child abuse to state authorities.\par \par \uc2 Davis said he complied with the committee\u8217\'20\'19s wishes for years \u8211\'20\'13 even after he was kicked out of standing in a friend\u8217\'20\'19s wedding when news of his having tried to hold Hall accountable circulated among the congregation.\par \par \uc2 But Davis said he eventually left the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses and moved to the Dallas area in Texas. There, in 2014, about six years after his mother died, he decided to revisit Hall\u8217\'20\'19s abuse and the resulting treatment he got from the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses after seeing a local news story about an attorney filing a lawsuit against the sect on behalf of five clients with their own abuse allegations.\par \par \uc2 Davis said he reached out to that lawyer, who could not assist him because his case unfolded in Louisiana rather than in Texas. Then, in 2019, he contacted New Orleans-based attorney Kristi Schubert, who has represented a number of religious abuse survivors \u8211\'20\'13 but, initially, she couldn\u8217\'20\'19t help because Louisiana laws in effect at the time meant Davis had only until his 28th birthday to sue over his molestation by Hall.\par \par \uc2 Davis was about 40 at the time.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, in 2021, Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s legislature enacted a law that in part temporarily allowed child molestation victims to file lawsuits seeking damages for their abuse no matter how long they had waited.\par \par \uc2 The law\u8217\'20\'19s constitutionality was challenged. But Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/12/louisiana-supreme-court-child-sexual-abuse-catholic-church"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld}}}\uc2  it as constitutional on 12 June 2024.\par \par \uc2 That very same day, Schubert filed a lawsuit in New Orleans\u8217\'20\'19s civil district courthouse on Davis\u8217\'20\'19s behalf. It demanded damages from Hall and the Watchtower Society, including for the mental and physical trauma with which the plaintiff was left.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit has generated exceptionally compelling evidence against Hall, who \u8211\'20\'13 as of a deposition in March \u8211\'20\'13 said he was representing himself without an attorney.\par \par \uc2 In his mandatory response to the lawsuit, Hall wrote that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cguilty of have [sic] an inappropriate relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with Davis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe fondled each other and played with each other sex organs and laid on each other buttocks,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hall\u8217\'20\'19s response, which was replete with typos. He added that he and Davis engaged in oral sex, though the plaintiff at the time could not legally give consent to that act or any of the others Hall mentioned.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, Hall wrote that a book which Davis authored and self-published about his abuse \u8220\'20\'1Cspeaks truthfully to a large degree about [the] encounters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Schubert interrogated Hall under oath during a 27 March videoconference deposition. Hall invoked his constitutional right against self-incrimination \u8211\'20\'13 colloquially known as pleading the fifth amendment \u8211\'20\'13 at least 48 times.\par \par \uc2 But he did answer when Schubert asked him if the letter was true and whether he wrote it of his \u8220\'20\'1Cown free accord\u8221\'20\'1D. Hall\u8217\'20\'19s answer to both questions: \u8220\'20\'1CYes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hall additionally testified about how he had a wife as well as a son \u8211\'20\'13 and how since 2003 he had belonged to a Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses congregation on Monroe Road in Charlotte. He said he was considered what is known as a regular \u8220\'20\'1Cpublisher\u8221\'20\'1D, by which he was regularly participating in organized preaching at his congregation.\par \par \uc2 Despite his being disfellowshipped after Davis reported his molestation, Hall said he does not \u8220\'20\'1Cknow of any rule\u8221\'20\'1D prohibiting from proselytizing around children. He also said there was no mandate for him to disclose the reason for his disfellowship to anyone, including fellow members of his congregation.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in the weeks after the deposition, Davis said Hall\u8217\'20\'19s statements evidently contradict the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses claims in their policies that \u8220\'20\'1Cchildren are a sacred trust\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and their \u8220\'20\'1Cprotection \u8230\'20\'26 is of utmost concern and importance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Davis said he hopes Hall and the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses make him whole for his ordeal. But furthermore, he said he hopes the Jehovah\u8217\'20\'19s Witnesses rethink the way they have let Hall carry on his business within the denomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s upsetting \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s infuriating,\u8221\'20\'1D Davis said. \u8220\'20\'1CI just think that is ludicrous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 In the US, call or text the \uc2 Childhelp\uc2  abuse hotline on 800-422-4453 or visit their website for more resources and to report child abuse or DM for help. For adult survivors of child abuse, help is available at ascasupport.org. In the UK, the \uc2 NSPCC\uc2  offers support to children on 0800 1111, and adults concerned about a child on 0808 800 5000. The \uc2 National Association for People Abused in Childhood\uc2  (Napac) offers support for adult survivors on 0808 801 0331. In Australia, children, young adults, parents and teachers can contact the Kids Helpline on 1800 55 1800, or Bravehearts on 1800 272 831, and adult survivors can contact Blue Knot Foundation on 1300 657 380. Other sources of help can be found at Child Helplines International\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250421el4l001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
