\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Noaa fires hundreds of climate workers after court clears way for dismissals\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon \par \uc2 786 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2025\par 01:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers had spent weeks in limbo amid legal rollercoaster but letters confirm block on terminations no longer in effect\par \par \uc2 Letters went out to hundreds of workers at the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2  (Noaa) on Thursday, informing them their jobs had been terminated \u8211\'20\'13 again.\par \par \uc2 The probationary employees, many who performed important roles at the US\u8217\'20\'19s pre-eminent climate research agency, have spent weeks in limbo after being dismissed in late February, only to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/13/federal-court-orders-fired-workers-doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rehired and put on administrative leave}}}\uc2  in mid-March following a federal court order.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell after about 3 weeks of reinstatement, I, along with other probationary employees at \uc2 NOAA\uc2 , officially got \u8220\'20\'1Cre-fired\u8221\'20\'1D today,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Andy Hazelton, a scientist who worked on hurricane modeling at Noaa posted on X. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat a wild and silly process this has been.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The fired Noaa employees were among the roughly 16,000 people terminated across the federal workforce in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/21/trump-federal-land-wildfire-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sweeping move by the Trump administration}}}\uc2  that targeted workers in \u8220\'20\'1Cprobationary\u8221\'20\'1D status. Some were categorized that way because they were new in their careers, but others had recently received promotions or been added full-time to agencies after years of contract or temporary work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of probationary employees in my office have been with the agency for 10+ years and just got new positions,\u8221\'20\'1D said one worker who still had their job, and who spoke to the Guardian under the condition of anonymity for fear of reprisal in February, when the firings first happened.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we lose them, we\u8217\'20\'19re losing not just the world-class work they do day-to-day, but also decades of expertise and institutional knowledge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This week\u8217\'20\'19s news caps a rollercoaster period for Noaa employees. On Tuesday, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/08/trump-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down the March court}}}\uc2  decision that said fired probationary workers must be rehired, ruling that the nonprofit groups who sued on behalf of the workers did not have legal standing.\par \par \uc2 The letters sent to Noaa staff, reviewed by the Guardian, were signed by John Guenther, acting general counsel of the \uc2 US Department of Commerce\uc2 , and consisted of two simple paragraphs: one reiterating that employees were reinstated and put in non-duty paid status, and a second explaining that the temporary restraining order protecting their jobs was no longer in effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAccordingly, the department is reverting your termination action to its original effective date,\u8221\'20\'1D Guenther wrote, adding that fired employees would not receive any pay beyond their termination date.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether those fired will receive all the pay they are owed. Hazelton told the Guardian that paychecks for the last two weeks have not been issued yet. His access to healthcare, which was terminated immediately, was never reinstated.\par \par \uc2 These firings are already hampering the agency\u8217\'20\'19s ability to provide essential climate and weather intelligence. Noaa is also bracing for more cuts as leaders make moves to comply with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Creduction in force\u8221\'20\'1D, an order that could cull 1,029 more positions.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the Guardian last month, Hazelton said the firings across the agency and the pressures felt by those still there will affect the outcome of the work. Vital work has slowed or stopped as teams try to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/04/doge-noaa-headquarters?%7B%7Burl_parameters_unstripped%7D%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 navigate the chaos}}}\uc2 , along with the threat of severe budget cuts and political restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to create problems across the board,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that people are going to do their best but it will be a lot harder to achieve the mission. \u8220\'20\'1CIt may be a slow process but the forecasts are going to suffer and as a result people will suffer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the losses are expected to have a profound impact on the American public, it will be felt globally, too. Scientists and forecasters around the world depend on Noaa satellites, studies, and intelligence, including data-sharing that tracks severe weather across Europe, coordination for disaster response in the Caribbean, and monitoring deforestation and the effects of the climate crisis in the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  rainforest.\par \par \uc2 The official terminations also came just days after the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/09/trump-national-climate-assessment-usgcrf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled funding for the national climate assessment,}}}\uc2  which summarizes the effects of rising global temperatures on the US.\par \par \uc2 The crackdown on climate science comes as the dangers from extreme weather events and deadly billion-dollar disasters continue to rise. Experts say these cuts, which will do little to limit the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s budget, will only add to the threats.\par \par \uc2 Among 800 positions cut were workers who track El Ni\u241\'00\'F1o-La Ni\u241\'00\'F1a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/07/trump-layoffs-nws?%7B%7Burl_parameters_unstripped%7D%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weather patterns around the world}}}\uc2 , people who model severe storm risks, and scientists contributing to global understanding of what could happen as the world warms.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250411el4b0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
