\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 RFK Jr plans 10,000 job cuts in restructuring of US health department\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 929 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2025\par 18:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Health secretary aims to close regional offices and establish new division called \u8216\'20\'18administration for a healthy America\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr said the nation\u8217\'20\'19s health agencies will cut 10,000 jobs from their 82,000-person workforce \u8211\'20\'13 an enormous reduction the US health secretary characterized as streamlining federal bureaucracy amid internal resistance to the administration\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 The cuts announced on Thursday, along with previous restructuring and voluntary buyouts, mean the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) will lose roughly 20,000 workers.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said the department will also close half of its regional offices and create a new agency called the \u8220\'20\'1Cadministration for a healthy America\u8221\'20\'1D, or \uc2 AHA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe aren\u8217\'20\'19t just reducing bureaucratic sprawl. We are realigning the organization with its core mission and our new priorities in reversing the chronic disease epidemic,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said on Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  is among the largest branches of the federal government, overseeing a $1.7tn budget and agencies that are household names. Among the agencies under \uc2 HHS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s oversight are the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC), the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  (\uc2 NIH\uc2 ), the \uc2 Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services\uc2  (CMS), and the Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The critical work performed by these agencies includes protecting Americans from outbreaks and infectious disease at the CDC, helming the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest publicly funded biomedical and behavioral research agency at the \uc2 NIH\uc2 , providing health insurance to 137 million Americans through the public programs Medicare and Medicaid at the CMS, and approving and regulating the nation\u8217\'20\'19s medical devices, drugs and foods at the \uc2 FDA\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his billionaire ally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , who oversees the massive federal job-cutting initiative via the unofficial \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, have been gutting agencies as part of an effort to shrink the federal bureaucracy, with cuts that have roiled health agencies in particular.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny cut you make to a health agency should be done with incredible care and consideration for the hundreds of millions of Americans who rely on their work to stay healthy and get treatment when they\u8217\'20\'19re sick,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chiquita Brooks-LaSure, previously the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s CMS administrator and now a senior fellow at the \uc2 Century Foundation\uc2 . Taking a \u8220\'20\'1Cwrecking ball\u8221\'20\'1D to health agencies and \u8220\'20\'1Claying off thousands of people \u8230\'20\'26 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t move us forward\u8221\'20\'1D, Brooks-LaSure said.\par \par \uc2 In his announcement, Kennedy also alluded to internal resistance to the upheaval at \uc2 HHS\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIn one case, defiant bureaucrats impeded the secretary\u8217\'20\'19s office from accessing the closely guarded databases that might reveal the dangers of certain drugs and medical interventions.\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy did not specify the databases or medical interventions in question.\par \par \uc2 In a description of the cuts, \uc2 HHS\uc2  said it plans to eliminate 3,500 full-time employees at the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . The administration claimed the cuts would not affect inspectors or drug, medical device and food reviewers. The CDC will lose 2,400 staff members, with the Administration for Strategic Preparedness and Response folded into the CDC. The \uc2 NIH\uc2  will lose a further 1,200 employees across its 27 institutes and centers. The CMS will lose 300 people. \uc2 HHS\uc2  did not provide a detailed breakdown of the programs, services or roles to be cut.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are getting panicked calls from our health agencies about what funding is going to get cut off,\u8221\'20\'1D said Democratic US senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  of Washington state, noting the country is in the midst of a severe flu season and expanding measles outbreak in west Texas. Murray added the administration\u8217\'20\'19s move appears to be an illegal \u8220\'20\'1Cimpounding\u8221\'20\'1D of funds allocated by Congress.\par \par \uc2 The restructuring will also consolidate 28 branches of the department into 15 new divisions, including the new \uc2 AHA\uc2 . \uc2 AHA\uc2  will combine offices in \uc2 HHS\uc2  that address addiction, mental health, toxic substances and occupational safety, among others, into one central office, the agency said. The new units will also centralize functions such as external affairs, human resources and IT, \uc2 HHS\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement is not just a restructuring of the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , it is a catastrophe for the health of every American,\u8221\'20\'1D said Democratic senator Edward Markey of Massachusetts. \u8220\'20\'1CKennedy, Musk and Trump only serve themselves and the wealthiest people in our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Democrats argued the downsizings are in service of extending tax cuts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2019/oct/09/trump-tax-cuts-helped-billionaires-pay-less"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the wealthy}}}\uc2 , consumer advocates also sounded alarms, arguing mass layoffs will inevitably close programs.\par \par \uc2 The consumer group \uc2 Public Citizen\uc2  said cuts to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  increase \u8220\'20\'1Cthe chances that more unsafe drugs and medical devices will be marketed and that all of us will suffer preventable diseases\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The massive restructuring comes as research funding is under threat. The \uc2 NIH\uc2  canceled nearly 400 active grants since the administration took the reins, with diversity, equity and inclusion programs; transgender issues; and research into South Africa and now Covid-19 as targets for defunding. The Office of Long Covid Research and Practice announced this week it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/trump-vaccine-skeptics-research-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 be shuttered}}}\uc2  as part of the reorganization.\par \par \uc2 A report in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-025-00954-y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nature}}}\uc2  on Wednesday revealed that federal workers who manage the government\u8217\'20\'19s research investments with scientists had been directed to cancel Covid-19 research grants, a category potentially encompassing $850m and more than 600 projects. Funding freezes at the same agency have thrown into upheaval critical research on diseases as diverse as pediatric cancer and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/10/alzheimers-research-trump-funding-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alzheimer\u8217\'20\'19s disease}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Do you have a tip on this issue? Please send us a message on Signal at 646-886-8761\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250410el490035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
