\par\par \uc2 UK news\par \b \uc2 Swindon apprentice loses unfair dismissal case after \u8216\'20\'18lunch-tampering\u8217\'20\'19 row\b0\par\par\uc2 Jamie Grierson \par \uc2 580 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2025\par 15:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 15\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Brooklyn Forrester-Hayes threatened co-worker after reporting \u8216\'20\'18finger-sized holes\u8217\'20\'19 in his sandwiches\par \par \uc2 A garage apprentice who threatened a colleague he thought had pranked him by poking \u8220\'20\'1Cfinger-sized holes through his sandwiches\u8221\'20\'1D has lost an unfair dismissal claim.\par \par \uc2 Brooklyn Forrester-Hayes accused a fellow apprentice of \u8220\'20\'1Ctampering with his lunch\u8221\'20\'1D as well as \u8220\'20\'1Csmashing his crisps\u8221\'20\'1D, an employment tribunal was told.\par \par \uc2 The 21-year-old told his colleague he would mess up his toolbox and damage his bike unless he owned up, the tribunal heard.\par \par \uc2 Despite hearing that there was a culture of \u8220\'20\'1Cbanter\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cpranking\u8221\'20\'1D at the \uc2 Scania\uc2  truck depot, the apprentice was sacked after bosses saw \u8220\'20\'1Cabusive messages\u8221\'20\'1D he had been sending.\par \par \uc2 Forrester-Hayes, who the tribunal heard dreamed of becoming a master technician at the Swedish manufacturer, took the company to an employment tribunal, claiming to have been unfairly dismissed over the incident.\par \par \uc2 But the tribunal ruled the company was entitled to conclude his actions amounted to sackable behaviour.\par \par \uc2 Forrester-Hayes started working as an apprentice technician at the Scania Swindon depot in February 2020, when he was 16, the Bristol employment tribunal heard.\par \par \uc2 The culture of \u8220\'20\'1Cpranking\u8221\'20\'1D among the five apprentices at the depot included interfering with each other\u8217\'20\'19s tools or toolboxes, the tribunal was told.\par \par \uc2 The apprentice was handed a final written warning in 2021, after he angrily reacted to one of his tools getting wrapped in electrical tape by a colleague, the hearing was told.\par \par \uc2 Forrester-Hayes \u8220\'20\'1Cgrabbed him by the collar and held on to him\u8221\'20\'1D before a supervisor intervened, the tribunal was told.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after starting his shift in July 2023, he went to the tea room for a drink and found that his \u8220\'20\'1Clunch bag had been tampered with\u8221\'20\'1D, the tribunal heard.\par \par \uc2 He found his \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisps smashed, chocolate bars crushed and someone had opened his sandwich box and poked finger-sized holes through the sandwiches\u8221\'20\'1D. They had also opened teabags and sprinkled tea leaves all over his lunch bag.\par \par \uc2 Forrester-Hayes said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cupset, dismayed and angry, and now had no food until he got home\u8221\'20\'1D. He threw the contents of his lunch box in the bin and then went to report the incident, the tribunal heard.\par \par \uc2 Forrester-Hayes assumed the culprit was an apprentice on the early shift, and told a colleague who was in the tea room: \u8220\'20\'1CI am going to fuck him up for it.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf I see his fucking toolbox open tomorrow \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to fuck everything up in there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Forrester-Hayes sent messages to everyone on the early shift, asking them if they knew who was responsible. In a Snapchat message to an apprentice he suspected, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf i find out it was u \u8230\'20\'26 ur toolbox is fucked. If it was u ur paying for my lunch if u dont ill cut ur tyre valves off \u8230\'20\'26 simple.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The following day, a foreman asked all of the apprentices if they knew what had happened to the lunch, and while nobody owned up, some mentioned the \u8220\'20\'1Cabusive messages\u8221\'20\'1D Forrester-Hayes had been sending. He was suspended, and after further investigation, he was sacked.\par \par \uc2 The tribunal ruled bosses were entitled to conclude his behaviour was unacceptable and that \u8220\'20\'1Cdismissal was necessary to protect employees\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His claims of unfair dismissal, damages for breach of contract, disability discrimination, failure to make reasonable adjustments and harassment related to disability failed.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250409el49001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
