\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Trump and Musk are setting the example\u8217\'20\'19: how companies are becoming emboldened to be more anti-union\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,224 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2025\par 14:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As the White House carries out an anti-worker agenda, labor leaders fear corporate America could also grow more hostile\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s aggressive wave of anti-union actions is already spurring some US employers to take a more hostile stance toward unions, as labor leaders voice fears that the president\u8217\'20\'19s moves will embolden more and more companies to fight harder against unions and slow their recent progress.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, some worker advocates worry that unions will be walloped during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term the way they were under \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  after he crushed the 1981 air traffic controllers\u8217\'20\'19 strike and inspired many corporations to fight harder against unions. As Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  carry out their anti-union agenda in Washington DC, Utah passed a law that prohibits collective bargaining by public sector workers, and a Michigan company refused to move forward with a union election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf history is any indicator on this \u8211\'20\'13 and I think it is \u8211\'20\'13 when you see a president\u8217\'20\'19s administration basically declaring war on unions, that\u8217\'20\'19s going to certainly embolden private sector employers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joseph McCartin, a labor historian at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2  and author of the definitive book about the disastrous 1981 strike by the Professional Air Traffic Controllers Organization (Patco).\par \par \uc2 Labor experts point to several Trump administration actions that show a huge hostility toward unions, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order to end collective bargaining by 50,000 airport screeners and then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/exclusions-from-federal-labor-management-relations-programs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a far-reaching order}}}\uc2  to rip up union contracts and prohibit bargaining for over a million federal employees at more than a dozen agencies, including the state department, the treasury and health and human services. Trump and Musk have also fired tens of thousands of federal workers while disregarding protections in their union contracts. Moreover, Trump fired {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/05/gwynne-wilcox-nlrb-lawsuit-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gwynne Wilcox}}}\uc2 , who was the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) acting chair. Wilcox insists her dismissal was illegal, but on 28 March a federal appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2025/03/28/trump-administration-wins-appeal-remove-agency-leaders/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to reinstate her}}}\uc2 , at least for now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is Patco on steroids,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Sara Nelson\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2 , said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the president saying even the idea of having a union contract and having something in black and white to protect workers and having collective bargaining \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19s saying none of this should exist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s anti-union and anti-worker actions have been piling up. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/rescind-eo-14026-increasing-the-minimum-wage-for-federal-contractors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescinded the $17.75-an-hour minimum wage}}}\uc2  that federal contractors must pay their workers. He issued an order to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/mar/26/doge-labor-agency-fmcs-trump-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kill the Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service}}}\uc2 , which seeks to settle potentially disastrous labor disputes. He nominated a management-side lawyer, Crystal Carey, to be the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s general counsel; her law firm represents anti-union employers, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . Even the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, who has sought good relations with Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/teamsters-union-opposes-nomination-of-crystal-carey-as-nlrb-general-counsel-302411356.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned that appointment}}}\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1CCarey has spent her entire professional career backing Big Business to the detriment of working people \u8230\'20\'26 [S]he wants to decimate labor unions.\u8221\'20\'1D (O\u8217\'20\'19Brien {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/TeamsterSOB/status/1860118006820479289?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did praise}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice of labor secretary, Lori Chavez-DeRemer.)\par \par \uc2 Beyond that, Trump has repeatedly insulted the nation\u8217\'20\'19s 2 million federal workers, saying: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8pMo3Or18ig"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Many of them don\u8217\'20\'19t work at all}}}\uc2 . Many of them never showed up to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eric Blanc, a labor studies professor at \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2 , said these actions have \u8220\'20\'1Cdemonstrated that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric about being pro-worker and pro-union was just that: pure rhetoric. This is an administration that is pushing the limits on how far you can go to destroy the labor movement and people\u8217\'20\'19s labor standards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blanc said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s replacing of the pro-union \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as president, has \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainly emboldened the big corporations that were already stonewalling their unions: \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , REI, where we saw the most emblematic union successes of the past few years\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In February, Utah\u8217\'20\'19s governor signed a law that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/utah-governor-unions-collective-bargaining-76b1fe205aae7b4097c1d0b4a1a13cc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prohibits unions representing}}}\uc2  teachers, firefighters, police officers and other government employees from bargaining for better pay and working conditions. In a move directly inspired by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions, a Michigan amusement and water park {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrbedge.com/p/03132025-regional-director-rejects"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to move forward }}}\uc2  with a union election, believing that the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  was paralyzed after Wilcox was fired, leaving it without a quorum.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCompanies could definitely get more anti-union because Trump and Musk are setting the example,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thomas Kochan, a longtime professor of industrial relations at MIT. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re firing workers who are unionized. They\u8217\'20\'19re ignoring their labor contracts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kochan said he fears the consequences for unions if the supreme court upholds the firing of federal workers despite their contract protections or upholds Trump\u8217\'20\'19s dismissal of Wilcox, leaving the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  without a quorum. \u8220\'20\'1CThen I think we will see companies come out of the woodwork to be more anti-union because there\u8217\'20\'19s so little risk,\u8221\'20\'1D Kochan said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll see companies like \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  just ignore the law because there will be no consequences. That\u8217\'20\'19s the big risk now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his high-profile role, taking a figurative chainsaw to federal agencies and firing tens of thousands of workers, the fiercely anti-union Musk could inspire corporate executives to follow in his anti-union footsteps. \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  is even seeking to have the \uc2 NLRB{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/10/starbucks-trader-joes-spacex-challenge-labor-board"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared unconstitutional}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CMusk is sort of the praetorian guard of the anti-union movement,\u8221\'20\'1D McCartin said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s the tip of the spear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Blanc said corporate executives might hesitate about following Musk. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is extremely unpopular, and his policies are not popular,\u8221\'20\'1D Blanc said. \u8220\'20\'1CCorporate America is not blind to that, and they\u8217\'20\'19ll think twice about unleashing a backlash like the one Musk has unleashed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Labor experts said it could take a few years before many companies become visibly more hostile toward unions. That was the case after the Patco strike. It was not until two or three years after that strike that several prominent employers \u8211\'20\'13\uc2 International Paper\uc2 , Greyhound and \uc2 Phelps Dodge\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 showed a harder attitude toward unions. They broke their unions\u8217\'20\'19 strikes by hiring large numbers of replacement workers \u8211\'20\'13 an unusual move at the time.\par \par \uc2 That tougher behavior under former president \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  sped the decline of private sector unions. Today, just 6% of private sector workers are in unions, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/pdf/union2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 32% of public sector workers}}}\uc2  are. Anti-union ideologues are increasingly targeting public sector unions, which often support Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause almost half of the labor movement is now in the public sector, the assault that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing now is really focused on the public sector,\u8221\'20\'1D McCartin said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat really threatens to break the spine of the labor movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The flight attendants\u8217\'20\'19 Nelson said it\u8217\'20\'19s imperative for the labor movement to stand up and stand together to resist Trump\u8217\'20\'19s and Musk\u8217\'20\'19s anti-union actions: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s on all of us to use the power we have to stop this before everything is broken and every safety net is stolen by the oligarchs,\u8221\'20\'1D including Musk. Nelson said the labor movement has very few options at this point except to mobilize for a general strike.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 7 April 2025 to clarify the timing of an order to rip up union contracts and an appeals court declining to reinstate Gwynne Wilcox.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250407el47001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
