\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 UK firms ditching diversity and inclusion \u8216\'20\'18face higher risk of lawsuits\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Butler \par \uc2 479 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2025\par 11:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Top employment lawyer issues warning after large US companies roll back policies amid Trump pushBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 British businesses face a greater risk of legal action if they follow their US counterparts in ditching efforts to improve diversity and inclusion in the wake of Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to office, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s leading authority on employment law has warned.\par \par \uc2 The Employment Lawyers Association (ELA), which has 7,000 members, has said British companies could open themselves up to \u8220\'20\'1Cadverse findings of discrimination\u8221\'20\'1D if they unpick policies designed to enable diversity equity and inclusion (DEI).\par \par \uc2 In an open letter to businesses, Caspar Glyn KC, the chair of the ELA, said that defending a company against discriminatory acts made by an employee was already difficult but \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be hopeless\u8221\'20\'1D without DEI policies in place.\par \par \uc2 Glyn also said employers without DEI policies would be unlikely to be able to demonstrate that they had taken \u8220\'20\'1Call reasonable steps\u8221\'20\'1D to prevent sexual harassment, for example, which they are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/news/new-protections-from-sexual-harassment-come-into-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legally required to do}}}\uc2 . The employment rights bill, due to be approved by parliament, will strengthen that requirement.\par \par \uc2 Trump has prompted a rollback of DEI programmes in the US, after he signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/26/trump-executive-orders-dei"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 series of executive orders}}}\uc2  overturning such measures.\par \par \uc2 Several large US corporations, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/15/walmart-dei-diversity-equity-inclusion-rollback"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walmart}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jan/06/mcdonalds-diversity-programs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , Ford and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/10/amazon-ending-dei-programs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2 , have either scrapped or are scaling back their DEI schemes.\par \par \uc2 Fears have grown that UK companies could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/feb/28/uk-based-british-pharma-gsk-pauses-diversity-work-citing-trump-orders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow suit}}}\uc2 . \uc2 The Bank of England\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s regulatory arm, \uc2 the Prudential Regulation Authority\uc2 , and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/financial-conduct-authority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Financial Conduct Authority}}}\uc2  have said they would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/mar/12/bank-of-england-decides-against-new-rules-on-improving-diversity-and-inclusion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not bring in}}}\uc2  new diversity and inclusion rules for financial companies. Instead, they are supporting \u8220\'20\'1Cvoluntary industry initiatives\u8221\'20\'1D aimed at increasing diversity and inclusion in the financial sector.\par \par \uc2 However, Glyn warned businesses: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you operate in Great Britain and roll back your DEI policies for workers here in response to the US administration\u8217\'20\'19s recent approach towards DEI policies, you will increase the risk of adverse findings of discrimination against your business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 UK law differs from US law in that it mandates equality but \u8220\'20\'1Cpositive action\u8221\'20\'1D has never permitted using race or other protected characteristics, such as gender, sex or religion, as a selection criterion to favour particular workers in applying for jobs or promotions, with an exception as a tie-breaker when candidates are equal.\par \par \uc2 In the UK it would be unlawful to hire someone simply because they are a woman, for example. However, if women are underrepresented in a company, then it can take steps to promote vacancies to that group or to provide extra support for them to apply.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA company rolling back its DEI policies in the UK, in response to the chilling of such practices in the US, would be legally incoherent and increase the risk of adverse findings of discrimination against it,\u8221\'20\'1D Glyn said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250407el47001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
