\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Afternoon Update Election 2025: Dutton\u8217\'20\'19s policy U-turn; ASX \u8216\'20\'18bloodbath\u8217\'20\'19; and one man\u8217\'20\'19s way into the White House group chat\b0\par\par\uc2 Elias Visontay \par \uc2 913 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2025\par 07:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Want to get this in your inbox every weekday? Sign up for Afternoon Update: Election 2025 here, and start your day with our Morning Mail newsletter.\par \par \uc2 Hello readers, and welcome to today\u8217\'20\'19s election edition of Afternoon Update.\par \par \uc2 We are officially into week two of the campaign, and we have our first proper about-face of the election thanks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/peter-dutton-coalition-backflip-wfh-work-from-home-public-service-cuts-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Dutton ditching some of his apparently unpopular flagship policies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, societal angst shifted to the economy, after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/falling-australian-aus-dollar-aud-to-usd-value-exchange-rate-travel-shopping"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catastrophic morning for the Aussie dollar }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/asx-200-sp-share-market-australian-dollar-sheds-opening-us-tariffs-trade-war-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 share market \u8220\'20\'1Cbloodbath\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new tariff regime.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2  predicted the events {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2025/apr/07/australia-election-2025-live-coalition-labor-federal-peter-dutton-anthony-albanese-job-cuts-redundancies-batteries-solar?page=with%3Ablock-67f348ba8f08f7ab2f00f16e#block-67f348ba8f08f7ab2f00f16e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would lead to a rate cut in May and }}}\uc2  other effects across Australia\u8217\'20\'19s economy, Treasury officials are not yet predicting a recession for the country.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s big stories\par \par \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  admitted he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/dutton-has-changed-his-tune-on-forcing-public-servants-back-into-the-office-again-heres-what-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmade a mistake\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cgot it wrong\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  as he backtracked on policies to restrict work from home arrangements for public servants and sack 41,000 government employees.\par \par \uc2 Dutton first softened the policy to a return to pre-pandemic levels of remote work \u8211\'20\'13 when 20% of public servants worked from home \u8211\'20\'13 then watered it down to only apply to government workers in Canberra, before axing the policy on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Also on Monday, the opposition appeared to dilute its public service job cuts policy, with the shadow public service spokesperson, \uc2 Jane Hume\uc2  (pictured), clarifying the Coalition would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/peter-dutton-coalition-backflip-wfh-work-from-home-public-service-cuts-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csensibly reduce\u8221\'20\'1D the APS by 41,000 positions over five years through a hiring freeze and natural attrition}}}\uc2 , with a commitment to no forced redundancies.\par \par \uc2 With Dutton\u8217\'20\'19s backflip and a horror morning for the economy \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/asx-200-sp-share-market-australian-dollar-sheds-opening-us-tariffs-trade-war-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $160bn was wiped off the ASX 200}}}\uc2  and the Australian dollar sank to 59.64 US cents, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/falling-australian-aus-dollar-aud-to-usd-value-exchange-rate-travel-shopping"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its lowest point since April 2020}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 stealing the headlines on Monday, you\u8217\'20\'19d be forgiven for missing Anthony Albanese on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2025/apr/07/australia-election-2025-live-coalition-labor-federal-peter-dutton-anthony-albanese-job-cuts-redundancies-batteries-solar?page=with%3Ablock-67f2fe398f0843b305e4c3c7#block-67f2fe398f0843b305e4c3c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started Monday in Melbourne}}}\uc2  alongside the Victorian premier, \uc2 Jacinta Allan\uc2 , spruiking his previously announced $2bn upgrade to Sunshine station, emphasising one of the main difference between Labor and the Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s (slightly cheaper) plan to progress a rail link to Melbourne\u8217\'20\'19s Tullamarine airport.\par \par \uc2 While he might have hoped the appearance would bring supporters on board the Albo Express, he instead had to dodge questions about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/05/election-labor-anthony-albanese-jacinta-allan-victoria-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether Allan\u8217\'20\'19s waning popularity }}}\uc2  was akin to an oncoming freight train threatening Labor\u8217\'20\'19s chances in Victoria.\par \par \uc2 What they said\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know my rent has gone up significantly \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m a renter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s how the Kooyong Liberal candidate, Amelia Hamer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/reel/C7yelnSy1bT/?igsh=eG1oa29qcW44NWw2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pitched herself to voters last year}}}\uc2 , as she began laying the foundations for her campaign to oust independent \uc2 Monique Ryan\uc2  from the blue-ribbon Melbourne seat. However, it\u8217\'20\'19s now clear that Hamer is much more than just a renter.\par \par \uc2 The grandniece of former Victorian premier Sir Rupert Hamer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/amelia-hamer-liberal-candidate-pitched-herself-as-renter-owns-two-properties-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also owns two investment properties}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an apartment in London and another in Canberra.\par \par \uc2 How social media saw it\par \par \uc2 The opposition have built much of their campaign on attacking Labor\u8217\'20\'19s performance across a range of areas, from taxation and energy management to inflation and cost of living pressures.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes zooming out on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/truthinpoliti10/status/1909011652407914950"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where Australia is among its fellow OECD nations}}}\uc2  can provide a little more perspective.\par \par \uc2 The big picture\par \par \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  may have slowly retreated on his public sector workforce policies, but the man is clearly standing behind his plan to halve the fuel excise.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Dutton gathered media at a petrol station in Adelaide, where he pumped fuel into a van advertising \uc2 Nicolle Flint\uc2 , the Liberal candidate for the seat of Boothby.\par \par \uc2 It was the fourth time in four days Dutton has posed for cameras at a petrol bowser to spruik his policy that will see drivers (of petrol-reliant vehicles) save 25c a litre if elected.\par \par \uc2 Watch\par \par \uc2 Ben Britton was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/06/coalition-dumps-liberal-candidate-who-said-women-should-not-serve-in-adf-combat-roles-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dumped as the Liberal candidate for the New South Wales seat of Whitlam}}}\uc2  after it was revealed he had expressed a string of controversial views (such as that Australia\u8217\'20\'19s education system \u8220\'20\'1Cbrainwashed\u8221\'20\'1D students and that women shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t serve in combat positions in the army) on fringe podcasts before his preselection.\par \par \uc2 Britton was taken off the Liberal party\u8217\'20\'19s website, and the party has confirmed he was no longer being endorsed, with the party quickly replacing him with Nathaniel Smith.\par \par \uc2 And in other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/bondi-junction-stabbing-attack-court-hearing-inquest-victims-families-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No \u8216\'20\'18one voice\u8217\'20\'19 for families of Bondi Junction victims, court hears after John Singleton says inquest is \u8216\'20\'18waste of time\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/apr/07/the-south-australian-retired-farmer-i-only-vote-because-ive-got-to"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The South Australian retired farmer: \u8216\'20\'18I only vote because I\u8217\'20\'19ve got to\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/06/signal-group-chat-leak-how-it-happened"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Exclusive: how the Atlantic\u8217\'20\'19s Jeffrey Goldberg got added to the White House Signal group chat}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/07/asian-share-markets-nikkei-kospi-asx-stocks-routed-early-trading-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Asian share markets routed in early trading as Trump says \u8216\'20\'18you have to take medicine\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/06/musk-doge-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doge\u8217\'20\'19s attack on social security causing \u8216\'20\'18complete, utter chaos\u8217\'20\'19, staff says}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2025/apr/06/adhd-medication-drugs-risks-benefits-children-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benefits of ADHD medication outweigh health risks, study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily word game\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s starter word is: SIT. You have five goes to get the longest word including the starter word. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wordiply.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Play Wordiply}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive this Afternoon Update: Election 2025 briefing to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/oct/13/afternoon-update-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 , or start your day with a curated breakdown of the key stories you need to know with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/sep/23/morning-mail-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up-inbox-subscribe?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our Morning Mail newsletter}}}\uc2 . You can follow the latest in US politics by signing up for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/election-newsletter-sign-up-stakes?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This Week in Trumpland}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250407el47000xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
