\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Doge\u8217\'20\'19s attack on social security causing \u8216\'20\'18complete, utter chaos\u8217\'20\'19, staff says\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,555 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 April 2025\par 16:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Understaffed agency sent into \u8216\'20\'18death spiral\u8217\'20\'19 as employees warn Musk-led cuts will lead to structural collapse\par \par \uc2 Office closures, staffing and service cuts, and policy changes at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Social Security Administration}}}\uc2  (SSA) have caused \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete, utter chaos\u8221\'20\'1D and are threatening to send the agency into a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath spiral\u8221\'20\'1D, according to workers at the agency.\par \par \uc2 The SSA operates the largest government program in the US, administering social insurance programs, including retirement, disability and survivor benefits.\par \par \uc2 An average of almost 69 million Americans per month will receive a social security benefit in 2025, totaling about $1.6tn in benefits paid during the year and accounting for 22% of the federal budget. While expensive and challenged by an ageing population, social security remains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://navigatorresearch.org/a-majority-of-americans-oppose-cuts-to-social-security-and-medicare/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2024/08/12/americans-see-many-federal-agencies-favorably-but-republicans-grow-more-critical-of-justice-department/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 popular}}}\uc2  with Americans. But the agency has been dubbed a \u8220\'20\'1CPonzi scheme\u8221\'20\'1D by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , the billionaire whose so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) is currently slashing its staff and budgets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have these \u8216\'20\'18concepts of plans\u8217\'20\'19 that they\u8217\'20\'19re hoping are sticking but in reality, are really hurting American people,\u8221\'20\'1D said a longtime SSA employee and military veteran who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one knows what\u8217\'20\'19s going on. They\u8217\'20\'19re just coming up with ideas at the top of their head.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The SSA website has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/03/25/social-security-phones-doge-cuts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crashed}}}\uc2  several times this month. Wired {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wired.com/story/doge-rebuild-social-security-administration-cobol-benefits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  Doge staff want to migrate all social security data and rewrite code in months, which could cause system collapse and further outages.\par \par \uc2 The agency plans to eliminate the jobs of 7,000 workers at the agency through voluntary buyouts, resignations or firings, though the union representing SSA employees anticipate even more firings beyond cutting staff to 50,000 workers.\par \par \uc2 Acting commissioner Leland Dudek has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/recording-reveals-leland-dudek-thoughts-trump-doge-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acknowledged }}}\uc2  to staff that Doge are making the decisions at the agency. Musk, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and others have claimed action is being taken to tackle widespread fraud at the agency.\par \par \uc2 Dudek was appointed acting commissioner after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/03/06/doge-is-driving-social-security-cuts-will-make-mistakes-acting-head-says-privately/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly secretly shared}}}\uc2  information with Doge staff. He has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://socialsecurityworks.org/2025/03/21/trump-admin-threatens-social-security-shutdown/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened }}}\uc2  to shut down the agency in response to a court order barring Doge from accessing the data.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just been a lot of craziness, a lot of foolishness. Until they get rid of Doge and the person in office right now, and the Republicans actually get a backbone and stand up for something for once in their lives, things are just going to be complete chaos. That\u8217\'20\'19s really the best word to describe SSA right now, just complete, utter chaos,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker added. \u8220\'20\'1CThey couldn\u8217\'20\'19t understand the coding, so everything they said SSA was doing illegally, they weren\u8217\'20\'19t. Common sense is something they lack. They don\u8217\'20\'19t know what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rich Couture, a spokesperson for the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2  general committee, the union representing roughly 42,000 social security workers, said Doge\u8217\'20\'19s public targets for cuts make no sense.\par \par \uc2 Why are they cutting 7,000 jobs, asked Couture. \u8220\'20\'1CIt has never been explained with any degree of clarity how they came up with that figure. What\u8217\'20\'19s being served by that by a loss of 7,000 jobs? How does any of that supposedly makes this operation more efficient? How does it improve service? How does it improve productivity? Our position is that losing 7,000 people doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do any of those things,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think they\u8217\'20\'19re going to stop at 7,000 people lost. If they lose 10,000 or 12,000, they\u8217\'20\'19re running up their high score. They\u8217\'20\'19re able to brag about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Departments at the agency have been closed and reorganized, with workers forced to take reassignments or risk firings, and all workers have been ordered to return to the office five days a week.\par \par \uc2 Couture noted the return to office order occurred a day before a buyout offer was set to expire, in violation of union contract agreements, and the offices were not prepared or equipped to handle it, as many workers had no desks or equipment to work.\par \par \uc2 Phone services for the public have also been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/03/25/social-security-phones-doge-cuts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut}}}\uc2 , and field and regional offices are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/social-security-offices-closures-doge-trump-b2b1a5b2ba4fb968abc3379bf90715ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slated for closure}}}\uc2  around the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no safe office in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D added Couture. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a concerted attack on the legitimacy of social security itself. The promise that this country has made to the public with respect to income security is being broken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The cuts come as staffing is already at a 50-year low despite the agency serving a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ssa.gov/oact/STATS/OASDIbenies.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record number of recipients}}}\uc2  as the US population above the age of 65 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.census.gov/topics/population/older-aging.html#:~:text=Featured&text=The%20U.S.%20population%20age%2065,increase%20in%20just%2010%20years.&text=Learn%20about%20age%2C%20sex%2C%20and,%2C%20counties%2C%20and%20census%20tracts."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The office of the inspector general at SSA {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oig.ssa.gov/news-releases/2024-08-08-record-breaking-backlog-increases-improper-payments-by-over-1b/#:~:text=As%20a%20backlog%20of%20payment,%241.1%20billion%20in%20improper%20payments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  in August 2024 that a record backlog of payment actions impacting social security beneficiaries was due to lack of staffing, increased workloads, and decreased funding for the agency, driving improper payments because staff weren\u8217\'20\'19t available to update records.\par \par \uc2 Couture noted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ssa.gov/legislation/testimony_032124.html#:~:text=Under%20the%20current%20system%2C%20Social,in%20less%20than%2030%20days."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 operating overhead}}}\uc2  of the agency, as a share of benefits paid out, has shrunk by 20% over the last 10 years and is now less than 1%. He disputed any claims of inefficiency or waste at the agency, claiming the agency is already a model of efficiency and as effective as possible under its fiscal and staffing constraints.\par \par \uc2 He said he was concerned the situation was creating a \u8220\'20\'1Cnegative feedback loop\u8221\'20\'1D where, as more employees leave, more work is put on those remaining, depressing morale and inducing more to leave \u8220\'20\'1Cuntil the agency ends up in a death spiral with staffing, inducing office closures\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re going to see a wholesale collapse in the agency\u8217\'20\'19s service structure. Call wait times will skyrocket, wait times for appointments, processing times, all of it going to skyrocket because there won\u8217\'20\'19t be enough people to do the jobs, which opens the door to privatization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Musk has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/newsroom/videos/watch/elon-musk-called-social-security-the-biggest-ponzi-scheme-of-all-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  social security \u8220\'20\'1Cthe biggest Ponzi scheme of all time\u8221\'20\'1D and has consistently pushed false claims and conspiracies about the program.\par \par \uc2 On senator Ted Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s podcast last month, Musk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aMcmuKTfr54"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated}}}\uc2  a white supremacist conspiracy theory that Democrats use entitlements to \u8220\'20\'1Cattract and retain\u8221\'20\'1D undocumented immigrants as voters.\par \par \uc2 This week, Musk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/musk-trump-immigrants-social-security-numbers-1235307351/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared a chart}}}\uc2  of immigrants receiving social security numbers, falsely claiming they were receiving benefits, though the program of providing social security numbers to legal immigrants began under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term as part of program to facilitate employment. He\u8217\'20\'19s also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/social-security-payments-deceased-false-claims-doge-ed2885f5769f368853ac3615b4852cf7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsely claimed}}}\uc2  dead people are receiving benefits, despite the acting commissioner of the SSA has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/social-security-doge-100-150-year-olds-cobol-elon-musk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dispelled the claim}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 2024, social security direct deposit fraud was at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dallasnews.com/timeless-in-texas/2025/03/30/more-misinformation-social-security-fraud-allegations-clarified/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rate }}}\uc2  of 0.00625% and less than 1% of social security payments had been found to be incorrect.\par \par \uc2 US commerce secretary and billionaire Howard Lutnick claimed in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=182ckTL2KBA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  on a podcast earlier this month that only a \u8220\'20\'1Cfraudster\u8221\'20\'1D would complain about missing a social security benefit check.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI worked there for 32 and a half years, and I rarely saw cases of fraud,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Oertel, a retired SSA employee for over 32 years in Redding, California.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause the agency is so understaffed that people who report their income, that\u8217\'20\'19s not getting reported into the system. Musk and his group are saying look at all these people who are being overpaid, they must be committing fraud. They\u8217\'20\'19re not committing fraud. They\u8217\'20\'19re doing what they\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to be doing, but because there are so few employees, none of that information is getting into the system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oertel also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/social-security-payments-deceased-false-claims-doge-ed2885f5769f368853ac3615b4852cf7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  false claims from Trump and Musk that dead people are getting social security benefits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t understand or they don\u8217\'20\'19t care. Those people aren\u8217\'20\'19t collecting benefits, but the numbers are still technically active, because you can\u8217\'20\'19t just erase social security numbers,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, noting that the numbers began being issued in the 1930s and are not deleted or reused, so they still remain in the system. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and whoever the next commissioner is going to be, I really think their ultimate goal is just to destroy social security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the SSA deferred to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ssa.gov/news/press/releases/2025/#2025-02-28"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press releases}}}\uc2  on the cuts and reorganization of the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have listened to our customers, Congress, advocates and others, and we are updating our policy to provide better customer service to the country\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable populations,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dudek, the SSA\u8217\'20\'19s acting commissioner. \u8220\'20\'1CIn addition to extending the policy\u8217\'20\'19s effective date by two weeks to ensure our employees have the training they need to help customers, Medicare, Disability and \uc2 SSI\uc2  applications will be exempt from in-person identity proofing because multiple opportunities exist during the decision process to verify a person\u8217\'20\'19s identity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They said in regard to office closures, that \u8220\'20\'1Cto use our space more efficiently, we provided [the \uc2 General Services Administration\uc2 ] a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ssa.gov/news/efficiencies/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 list of leases}}}\uc2  for termination,\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed that the return-to-office mandate was ordered to ensure \u8220\'20\'1Cmaximum staffing is available to support the stronger in-person identity proofing requirement\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On claims of waste, fraud and abuse, a spokesperson said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CThe agency will continue to monitor and, if necessary, make adjustments to ensure it pays the right person the right amount at the right time while safeguarding the benefits and programs it administers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250406el46000mc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
