\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US health agency layoffs gut mine safety, infertility and smoking programs\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza and Marina Dunbar \par \uc2 966 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2025\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Thousands lost jobs as sweeping cuts reshape public health, leaving experts and lawmakers scrambling\par \par \uc2 Experts in everything from mine safety to smoking and infertility were hit by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/29/health-department-private-sector-takeover"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mass layoffs}}}\uc2  after the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) secretary Robert F Kennedy Jr\u8217\'20\'19s plan to downsize nearly a quarter of the 82,000-person workforce took effect.\par \par \uc2 Even as the sprawling nature of layoffs became apparent on Tuesday, a complete accounting was elusive. Layoffs were undertaken with few public details, with even apoplectic congressional lawmakers left in the dark.\par \par \uc2 The result was a day of desperate crowdsourcing, as employees themselves and experts outside government became aware of programs and positions eliminated \u8211\'20\'13 and then processed how it would ultimately affect American lives.\par \par \uc2 Layoff notices started coming down earlier in the day, embodied by lines of staffers wrapping the sidewalk of the Parklawn building in Maryland \u8211\'20\'13 waiting to see if their badges would still work, and employees in building elevators carrying boxes of personal belongings.\par \par \uc2 But the cuts rippled out far from the DC area. In just one example in Morgantown, West Virginia, the secretary\u8217\'20\'19s cuts gutted the respiratory division that protects coal miners from pneumoconiosis, a disease colloquially known as \u8220\'20\'1Cblack lung\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and one condition that has increased astronomically among young coal miners in Appalachia.\par \par \uc2 The cuts at \uc2 HHS\uc2  come alongside others to the \uc2 Mine Safety and Health Administration\uc2 , a separate government division that monitors mine safety conditions, housed in the Department of Labor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure they realize that eliminating these jobs within [the National Institute for Occupational Health and Safety] and these offices is going to affect the miners in these offices,\u8221\'20\'1D said Erin Bates, spokesperson for the United Mine Workers International.\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC), cuts hit an entire branch devoted to infertility \u8211\'20\'13 a cause that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had championed only days earlier, calling himself the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/video/trump-touts-ivf-expansion-calls-himself-fertilization-president-at-women-s-event-235451973833"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fertilization president}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing today\u8217\'20\'19s layoffs at the CDC, there will be no experts on infertility who will be able to inform public policy, brief members of Congress, publish articles and reports, and advance public awareness on the causes and treatments for infertility,\u8221\'20\'1D Barbara Collura, president of \uc2 Resolve: The National Infertility Association\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The loss stood alongside the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s Division of Environmental Health Science and Practice (DEHSP), \u8220\'20\'1Cslated to be eliminated in its entirety\u8221\'20\'1D, according to an internal email from the center\u8217\'20\'19s director, Ari Bernstein, obtained by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eenews.net/articles/trump-admin-guts-cdcs-climate-and-environment-offices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico\u8217\'20\'19s E&E News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The division is responsible for preventing exposures to harmful environmental hazards and responding to the climate crisis. It also oversees the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s climate health activities and its branches on lead poisoning, asthma and air quality, water, emerging hazards, and environmental public health tracking.\par \par \uc2 Among the losses at the Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) was the division devoted to crafting tobacco policy. Taxpayers will save no money \u8211\'20\'13 it was paid for by tobacco companies themselves.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese cuts conflict with the repeatedly stated commitments of President Trump and Secretary Kennedy to reduce chronic disease and protect children\u8217\'20\'19s health,\u8221\'20\'1D said Yolonda C Richardson, president and CEO of the \uc2 Campaign for Tobacco-Free Kids\uc2 , who said in a statement that smoking is still responsible for 30% of all cancer deaths in the US. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot achieve these goals and make America healthy if our nation backs off its efforts to reduce tobacco use.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The director of the FDA\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Tobacco Products, Brian King, told staff in an email he was placed on administrative leave the same day: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is with a heavy heart and profound disappointment that I share I have been placed on administrative leave,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/fda-tobacco-rfk-brian-king-cf2d5657e5d55410073aece19592be09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Administration for Community Living\uc2  (ACL) at the health department was hit by significant cuts, in effect dismantling the teams focused on serving the disabled and elderly.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Autism Society of America\uc2  opposed that cut as well as those to the \uc2 Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration\uc2  as decisions that could curtail bipartisan support for disabled Americans.\par \par \uc2 Former CDC director Dr \uc2 Tom Frieden\uc2  said the cuts, particularly to programs on smoking and to global health, would not \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18trim the fat\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 they will undermine our ability to prevent deaths from tobacco and disease outbreaks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Multiple communications teams at the \uc2 FDA\uc2  were also cut, including the entire media affairs division and most of the communications team of the FDA\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Drug Evaluation and Research, reportedly about 50 people, sources told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/widespread-job-cuts-begin-health-agencies-rcna198859"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 . This team was responsible for managing public databases on drug approvals, which includes informing the public about potential risks of \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drugs, as well as managing the drug-shortages database.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/rfk-jr-health-department-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10,000 jobs}}}\uc2  would be cut from the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  on Thursday afternoon \u8211\'20\'13 offering few specifics beyond the promise that the cuts would \u8220\'20\'1Cstreamline our agency\u8221\'20\'1D. The cuts are compounded by losses already made by the unofficial \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) run by billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . All told the $1.7tn health department is expected to lose up to 20,000 people, or one-quarter of its 82,000-person workforce.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, nearly 2,000 members of the \uc2 National Academies of Science, Engineering and Medicine\uc2  issued an open letter to warn Americans of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/31/scientists-letter-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assault on science}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the cuts came into focus, former leaders of \uc2 HHS\uc2  stood in awe of their vast reach.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FDA\uc2  as we\u8217\'20\'19ve known it is finished with most of the leaders with institutional knowledge and a deep understanding of product development and safety no longer employed,\u8221\'20\'1D former \uc2 FDA\uc2  commissioner Dr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/in/robert-califf-69040016/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Califf}}}\uc2  told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.massdevice.com/mass-layoffs-hhs-fda-nih-cdc-rfk-jr-trump-elon-musk-doge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mass Device}}}\uc2 , calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ca dark day for public health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250402el42001jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
