\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Trump claimed he was pro-worker. His new order shows how absurd that was\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,295 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 April 2025\par 16:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Last week, he moved to end collective bargaining rights for 1 million people. And would anyone who cared about workers hire this staff?\par \par \uc2 If any workers are still holding on to the notion that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is pro-worker or pro-union, his move last week to terminate union bargaining rights for 1 million federal workers should disabuse them of that notion. As a candidate Trump often wooed workers by promising to fight for them, but ever since he returned to the White House, he has taken dozens of anti-worker and anti-union actions.\par \par \uc2 In an unprecedented anti-union action last Thursday, the president moved to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/28/trump-order-union-rights-federal-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end collective bargaining}}}\uc2  for a million federal employees and scrap union contracts nearly that number, while attacking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/03/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-exempts-agencies-with-national-security-missions-from-federal-collective-bargaining-requirements/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their unions as \u8220\'20\'1Chostile\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  merely because they were doing what unions are supposed to do: battling to save the jobs of tens of thousands of union members whom Trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  had summarily fired.\par \par \uc2 In an era when many workers are demanding respect, Trump keeps showing disrespect toward the country\u8217\'20\'19s 2.3 million federal workers. He and Musk have cavalierly fired more than 50,000 federal employees, ignoring contractual protections saying they could only be terminated for poor performance. Then Trump blamed the victims, saying, without evidence: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8pMo3Or18ig"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Many of them don\u8217\'20\'19t work at all}}}\uc2 . Many of them never showed up to work.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump views federal employees not as dedicated workers who serve the nation\u8217\'20\'19s 340 million people, but as deplorables who work for the detested deep state.\par \par \uc2 Not stopping there, Trump has named several vehemently anti-union figures to be his right-hand men. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/10/who-is-russell-vought-trump-office-of-management-and-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russell Vought}}}\uc2 , head of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s office of management and budget, has shown true sadism toward workers. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want the bureaucrats to be traumatically affected,\u8221\'20\'1D Vought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/10/who-is-russell-vought-trump-office-of-management-and-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a video disclosed}}}\uc2  by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  and the research group Documented. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen they wake up in the morning, we want them to not want to go to work, because they are increasingly viewed as the villains \u8230\'20\'26 We want to put them in trauma.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Would anyone who cared an iota about workers name such a callous, anti-worker person to a top position?\par \par \uc2 Then there\u8217\'20\'19s the aggressively anti-union Mr Musk. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-and-musk-discussed-firing-striking-workers-the-uaw-is-now-seeking-an-nlrb-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised Musk}}}\uc2  over the idea of firing striking workers, an action that is illegal and would go far to cripple labor\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful weapon: the strike. Musk has become a pariah in Scandinavia for his extreme anti-union animus: \uc2 Tesla\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/europe/2023/12/08/elon-musk-tesla-union-troubles-scandinavia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to recognize a union there}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 something that virtually all Scandinavian corporations do. Like Trump, Musk has a penchant for disrespecting workers, repeatedly tarring federal employees as being guilty of \u8220\'20\'1Cwaste, fraud and abuse\u8221\'20\'1D. Last week on Fox News, Musk insulted the intelligence of federal workers by falsely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/elon-musk-fox-news-interview-doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CBasically almost no one [no federal employee] has gotten fired.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Again, would anyone who cared a whit about workers and unions tap Musk for such a powerful position?\par \par \uc2 One has to strain to think of even one or two pro-worker or pro-union moves that Trump has taken\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first two months back in office have been filled with anti-worker and anti-union actions. In an unseemly move, the Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c78wn5qg3nyo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on federal workers}}}\uc2  to snitch on each other, to report on co-workers who promote diversity and inclusion. Trump fired Gwynne Wilcox, the acting chair of the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/06/trump-labor-board-firing-gwynne-wilcox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a move she says is illegal}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 leaving the board without a quorum to penalize employers that break the law when fighting against unionization. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/01/28/nx-s1-5277103/nlrb-trump-wilcox-abruzzo-democrats-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also fired}}}\uc2  the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vigorously pro-union general counsel, \uc2 Jennifer Abruzzo\uc2 , and wants to replace her with a management-side lawyer whose firm represents many anti-union companies, including \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the supposed champion of workers, has done little to raise workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages. As in his first term, he\u8217\'20\'19s done zilch to increase the federal minimum wage, which has been stuck at a shockingly low $7.25 an hour for 15 years. He also rescinded \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s order securing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/rescind-eo-14026-increasing-the-minimum-wage-for-federal-contractors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $17.75-an-hour minimum wage}}}\uc2  for federal contractors. As a candidate Trump wooed tipped workers by vowing to end the income tax on employee tips, but he has failed to get the House budget bill to end that tax, although that bill tentatively includes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kiplinger.com/taxes/whats-happening-with-taxes-on-overtime-pay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 idea not to tax overtime pay}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Labor leaders have denounced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order to gut union bargaining for 1 million workers. Randy Erwin, president of the National Federation of Federal Employees, called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nffe.org/nffe_news/federal-employees-union-president-rebukes-trumps-eo-gutting-collective-bargaining-rights-for-over-one-million-federal-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the biggest assault on collective bargaining rights}}}\uc2  we have ever seen in this country\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , president of the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2 , said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/afge-condemns-trumps-retaliatory-attempt-to-outlaw-federal-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a disgraceful and retaliatory attack}}}\uc2  on the rights of hundreds of thousands of patriotic American civil servants \u8211\'20\'13 nearly one-third of whom are veterans \u8211\'20\'13 simply because they are members of a union that stands up to his harmful policies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Anti-union CEOs and ideologues will no doubt applaud Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order. By targeting unionization among 1 million workers, Trump aims to weaken the nation\u8217\'20\'19s 14-million-member labor movement. If successful, his move would end bargaining for those 1 million workers, holding down employee pay and thereby making more money available for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tax cuts for the rich.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers will love Trump\u8217\'20\'19s move because it undermines a key financial pillar for the Democrats. Half of US union members are government employees, and their unions are often major funders of Democratic candidates. Trump certainly knows that \u8211\'20\'13 10 minutes after the supreme court issued its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2018/6/14/17437832/janus-afscme-supreme-court-union-teacher-police-public-sector"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Janus decision}}}\uc2  in 2018, ruling that no federal, state or local government employee can be required to pay union dues, Trump tweeted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realDonaldTrump/status/1011975204778729474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1011975204778729474%7Ctwgr%5E28f973f608d796b3dcda596e750c81ddc14c8dee%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2018%2F06%2F27%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Fsupreme-court-unions-organized-labor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbig loss for the coffers}}}\uc2  of the Democrats!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new executive order will further skew a huge imbalance: Open Secrets, a research group that tracks political contributions, found that in the 2024 election cycle, business {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/elections-overview/business-labor-ideology-split"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 out-donated unions by 16 to one}}}\uc2 . Corporations donated $6.1bn to unions\u8217\'20\'19 $264m, which is less than the gazillionaire Musk gave all by himself.\par \par \uc2 Trump also won over many workers by vowing to cut prices. Not only did he vow to cut egg prices, he boldly said he\u8217\'20\'19d {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/donald-trump-says-hell-cut-164522310.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut auto insurance prices }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/09/22/nx-s1-5118358/fact-checking-former-president-trumps-promise-to-cut-u-s-energy-costs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 energy prices}}}\uc2  in half. But Trump has totally failed to do any of that. Moreover, his 25% auto tariff will cause auto prices to soar.\par \par \uc2 One has to strain to think of even one or two pro-worker or pro-union moves that Trump has taken. The White House says his tariffs are pro-worker and pro-union, insisting they will bring back manufacturing jobs. But many economists say Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs will hurt myriad industries and workers. His auto tariffs, for instance, will increase car prices and as a result, auto sales, auto production and auto jobs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/mar/27/trump-auto-tariffs-backfire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will decline}}}\uc2 , at least short-term. Not only that, other countries\u8217\'20\'19 retaliation will pummel various US industries and trigger additional layoffs. Moreover, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs will undermine GDP growth and perhaps push the US into recession. Bottom line: Trump remains obsessed with tariffs, even though they\u8217\'20\'19re likely to result in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/mar/24/trumps-tariff-obsession"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more pain than gain}}}\uc2  for US workers.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to worker issues, Trump resembles the emperor in the famous fairytale: he sees himself wearing magnificent union-made clothes covered with buttons containing pro-worker slogans. But more and more Americans realize that when it comes to helping workers, Trump is like Hans Christian Andersen\u8217\'20\'19s emperor: his nakedness is showing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Steven Greenhouse is a journalist and author focusing on labor and the workplace, as well as economic and legal issues\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250401el410020b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
