\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Doge gains access to federal payroll system despite staff warnings\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts \par \uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 March 2025\par 18:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Officials said accessing system that processes 276,000 employees\u8217\'20\'19 salaries could put unit at risk of cyber-attacks\par \par \uc2 Members of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) reportedly gained access to a payroll system over the weekend that processes salaries for about 276,000 federal employees across various government agencies, despite warnings from senior staff about the potential risks.\par \par \uc2 According to two people familiar with the situation who spoke with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/31/us/politics/doge-musk-federal-payroll.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2 , Doge employees had spent about two weeks trying to obtain administrative access to the program, known as the Federal Personnel and Payroll System.\par \par \uc2 Then, toward the end of last week, senior career officials at the interior department reportedly issued a memo highlighting the unusual nature of the request and the associated risks with granting it.\par \par \uc2 The memo, reviewed by the Times, stated that \u8220\'20\'1Csuch elevated access to critical high-value asset systems is rare with respect to individual systems and no single [Department of Interior] official presently has access to all HR, payroll and credentialing systems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The senior employees reportedly warned that granting Doge employees this level of access would allow them to be able to view highly sensitive personal information that is subject to controls under the Privacy Act and cautioned that individuals given this elevated access could become targets for cybersecurity attacks by terrorists, nations or other malicious actors.\par \par \uc2 The memo emphasized that gaining administrative access to the system \u8220\'20\'1Ctypically requires training and certification\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout formal qualifications, the Department may experience significant failure because of operator error,\u8221\'20\'1D the memo said.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the federal employees reportedly asked the Doge workers to deliver the memo to \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the interior secretary, for his signature, thereby assuming the legal responsibility for the associated risks.\par \par \uc2 However, Burgum reportedly never signed the memo.\par \par \uc2 But on Saturday, interior department officials reportedly granted at least two Doge employees the access they had requested, the two people told the Times.\par \par \uc2 With this access, the Doge employees now have visibility into sensitive employee information, like social security numbers, and are able to more easily hire and fire federal workers, according to the Times, citing the two people with knowledge who spoke with the newspaper on condition of anonymity due to fear of retribution.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Tyler Hassan, the recently named interior department\u8217\'20\'19s acting assistant secretary of policy, management and budget and a former Doge employee, reportedly placed two of the IT officials who had resisted the Doge employees on administrative leave and under investigation for their \u8220\'20\'1Cworkplace behavior\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the two sources.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, a spokesperson for the interior department said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are working to execute the President\u8217\'20\'19s directive to cut costs and make the government more efficient for the American people and have taken actions to implement President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Executive Orders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250331el3v002s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
