\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Organizers accuse Trump of trying to silence federal workers with union order\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 856 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 March 2025\par 11:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Union leaders say president is union-busting as he seeks to eliminate collective bargaining across agencies\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Union}}}\uc2  leaders have accused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  of union-busting in a \u8220\'20\'1Cblatant\u8221\'20\'1D attempt to silence them after the president stepped up his attacks on government unions on Thursday, signing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/exclusions-from-federal-labor-management-relations-programs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an executive order}}}\uc2  that attempts to eliminate collective bargaining for hundreds of thousands of federal workers.\par \par \uc2 The order limits the departments and classifications of federal workers who can organize a union and instructs the government to stop engaging in any collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 The office of personnel management {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/latest-memos/guidance-on-executive-order-exclusions-from-federal-labor-management-programs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued}}}\uc2  a memo following the directive, providing guidance to the departments and subdivisions on the order, which includes terminating their collective bargaining agreements and ending voluntary union dues collection through payrolls.\par \par \uc2 Following the order the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.licdn.com/dms/document/media/v2/D4E1FAQE6R7cgSMj2aA/feedshare-document-pdf-analyzed/B4EZXcYj2mGgAY-/0/1743159191278?e=1744243200&v=beta&t=qn2hMwteDVo1W3BndA20eNbadfRkyg0JflMurnsC5Do"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  in a Texas court to support its move to end collective bargaining, claiming collective bargaining agreements (CBAs) \u8220\'20\'1Csignificantly constrain\u8221\'20\'1D the executive branch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlaintiffs wish to rescind or repudiate those CBAs, including so they can protect national security by developing personnel policies that otherwise would be precluded or hindered by the CBAs. But to ensure legal certainty and avoid unnecessary labor strife, they first seek declaratory relief to confirm that they are legally entitled to proceed with doing so,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit states.\par \par \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest federation of labor unions in the US, said the move was \u8220\'20\'1Cstraight out of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, the rightwing \uc2 Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s manifesto to remake the federal government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis executive order is the very definition of union-busting. It strips the fundamental right to unionize and collectively bargain from workers across the federal government at more than 30 agencies,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shuler. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s clear that this order is punishment for unions who are leading the fight against the administration\u8217\'20\'19s illegal actions in court \u8211\'20\'13 and a blatant attempt to silence us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 , 29.9% of federal employees are union members as of 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/pdf/union2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 representing}}}\uc2  more than 1.2 million workers.\par \par \uc2 Unions representing federal workers have criticized the order and vowed to take immediate legal action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest executive order is a disgraceful and retaliatory attack on the rights of hundreds of thousands of patriotic American civil servants \u8211\'20\'13 nearly one-third of whom are veterans \u8211\'20\'13 simply because they are members of a union that stands up to his harmful policies,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2 , the largest union representing federal workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese threats will not work. Americans will not be intimidated or silenced. \uc2 AFGE\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t going anywhere. Our members have bravely served this nation, often putting themselves in harm\u8217\'20\'19s way, and they deserve far better than this blatant attempt at political punishment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kelley added: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 AFGE\uc2  is preparing immediate legal action and will fight relentlessly to protect our rights, our members, and all working Americans from these unprecedented attacks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/live/?ref=watch_permalink&v=987598853477493"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press conference}}}\uc2  with Democratic lawmakers on Friday afternoon at the US Capitol, during which Kelley criticized the invocation of national security to strip federal workers of their union rights and called for support from the public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t about safety or security. It\u8217\'20\'19s about silencing workers who are courageously standing up to this non integrity, non accountability in the government,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelley. \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t be silenced.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The congressman Jamie Raskin said the Trump order was an attempt to bring \u8220\'20\'1Cchaos and retaliation\u8221\'20\'1D against the US labor movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s clear as day that they are retaliating against the labor movement for standing up for the rights of workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Raskin. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen rightwing coups and authoritarian takeovers happen all over the world, the first thing they do is they attack the civil service, and then they attack the labor movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unions representing federal workers can only bargain over conditions of employment, with wages, benefits, and classifications set by law and Congress. Bargaining is governed by the 1978 Civil Service Reform Act. Federal workers are also barred from conducting strikes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to unlawfully eliminate the right to collectively bargain for hundreds of thousands of federal workers is blatant retribution,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Lee Saunders\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2  (\uc2 AFSCME\uc2 ). \u8220\'20\'1CThis attack is meant to silence their voices, so {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  and his minions can shred the services that working people depend on the federal government to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sara Nelson\uc2 , the international president of the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants-CWA\uc2 , warned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order was a warning for more attacks on workers and labor unions to come from this administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we allow this administration to tear up federal union contracts, fire federal workers who stand up for our legal rights and target federal unions and union activists, they won\u8217\'20\'19t stop there,\u8221\'20\'1D Nelson said. \u8220\'20\'1CAn injury to one is an injury to all. It is time for the labor movement and the American workforce to rise up for our rights and fight for our country \u8211\'20\'13 whatever it takes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250328el3s001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
