\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Alarm as Florida Republicans move to fill deported workers\u8217\'20\'19 jobs with children: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s insane, right?\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe in Miami \par \uc2 1,139 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 March 2025\par 10:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  leads push to loosen child labor laws as immigration crackdown leads to workforce shortage\par \par \uc2 Beneath the smugness of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , at Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wlrn.org/government-politics/2025-03-21/florida-ice-police-sheriff-deportation-task-force-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading the nation}}}\uc2  in immigration enforcement lies something of a conundrum: how to fill the essential jobs of the scores of immigrant workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/latino/immigration-florida-deportation-fears-desantis-trump-rcna188942"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeted for deportation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The answer, according to Florida lawmakers, is the state\u8217\'20\'19s schoolchildren, who as young as 14 could soon be allowed to work overnight shifts without a break \u8211\'20\'13 even on school nights.\par \par \uc2 A bill that progressed this week through the Republican-dominated state senate seeks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5cd5801dfdf7e5927800fb7f/67e1b4e9a2b15644d9fb9449_childlaborbill_march2025%201.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remove numerous existing protections}}}\uc2  for teenage workers, and allow them, in the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s words, to step into the shoes of immigrants who supply Florida\u8217\'20\'19s tourism and agriculture industries with \u8220\'20\'1Cdirt cheap labor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s wrong with expecting our young people to be working part-time now? That\u8217\'20\'19s how it used to be when I was growing up,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said at an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mrEIaj5nPRE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration forum}}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D, Tom Homan, in Sarasota last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do we say we need to import foreigners, even import them illegally, when teenagers used to work at these resorts, college students should be [doing] all this stuff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, the proposal has alarmed immigration advocates and watchdog groups concerned about child labor abuses and exploitation.\par \par \uc2 They point out that there is nothing \u8220\'20\'1Cpart-time\u8221\'20\'1D in the language of the companion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2025/918/BillText/Filed/PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 senate}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2025/1225/BillText/Filed/PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 house}}}\uc2  bills currently before lawmakers, which instead will permit unlimited working hours without breaks for 14- and 15-year-olds who are schooled at home or online, and allow employers to require 16- and 17-year-olds to work for more than six days in a row.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s essentially treating teens who have developing bodies and minds like adults, and this will allow employers to schedule them for unlimited hours, overnight and without breaks, and this is during the school year,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alexis Tsoukalas, senior policy analyst at the Florida Policy Institute (FPI), an independent research and economic analysis group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important to remind people that teens can work. They can get that experience and some extra money if they need it. But there have to be protections in place to protect our most vulnerable, and if we pass this that\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely not going to happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, an attempt by the state senator who sponsored the bill, the Sarasota Republican Jay Collins, to paint it as an issue of parental rights rather than a way to cover Florida\u8217\'20\'19s deportation-driven labor shortfall also failed to impress critics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not talking about The Jungle by Upton Sinclair,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the chamber on Wednesday, referring to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2006/aug/05/featuresreviews.guardianreview24"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1906 novel}}}\uc2  that described horrific and dangerous conditions endured by cheap immigrant laborers, including children, in Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s meat-packing industry \u8211\'20\'13 an environment that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/child-labor-iowa-pork-plant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still exists today}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, he insisted, \u8220\'20\'1Cis talking about those soft skill benefits to children growing\u8221\'20\'1D, and said his bill was aimed at teenagers working in places like grocery stores.\par \par \uc2 Tsoukalas rejected Collins\u8217\'20\'19s claim. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s different arguments that people will put on the floor in order to do what they think it takes to get a bill passed. Given some of the justifications that state leaders have made in recent days, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that they are linking the immigration issue and child labor,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the sweeping {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.floridapolicy.org/posts/top-five-things-to-know-about-sb-1718-floridas-new-immigration-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-immigrant bill of 2023}}}\uc2  passed, we did warn there would be impacts on the labor force and the economy given how reliant we are on immigrant labor. Of course, not all of those people are undocumented, but as we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen recently at the federal level all types of people, even permanent residents, are getting threatened with deportation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCombined with what\u8217\'20\'19s going on at the state level, that absolutely is a concern. It\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that last year, and then again this year, we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about the need to fill gaps with other forms of labor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 US Census Bureau\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usafacts.org/answers/what-percent-of-jobs-in-the-us-are-held-by-immigrants/state/florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 27%}}}\uc2  of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s workforce is foreign-born.\par \par \uc2 The Farmworker Association of Florida, which represents tens of thousands of low-income, immigrant laborers, says about 60% of its membership is undocumented, and most vulnerable to detention and deportation. Others are among half a million Haitians nationwide who Trump has ordered to leave the US by August after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/03/ohio-haitians-immigration-tps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescinded their temporary protected status}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pushback from FPI and other groups persuaded Florida lawmakers to drop some of the harsher provisions in a child labor law that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www2.myfloridalicense.com/child-labor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed last year}}}\uc2 , and opponents are dismayed to find them back under consideration.\par \par \uc2 The state was singled out in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governingforimpact.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/GFI-EPI-CLC-Child-Labor-FLSA-Report_FINAL-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 report}}}\uc2  by Governing for Impact and the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2  that recorded a surge in workplace injuries and violations involving minors \u8211\'20\'13 some in the agricultural industry where hazards include exposure to toxic chemicals and dangerous machinery.\par \par \uc2 The report noted a corresponding push in at least 30 mostly Republican-controlled states to weaken workplace protections for children, and warned the second Trump administration would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/child-labor-regulations-project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seek to escalate the rollback}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been saying since 2023 that this is a way for them to exploit minors, it was when they passed this large, anti-immigrant omnibus and the same year that they tried to pass the first law gutting child labor protection,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thomas Kennedy, spokesperson for the Florida Immigrant Coalition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only short-term answer to workforce shortages has always been net migration and they\u8217\'20\'19ll never go for that because of their politics. So their only answer is to widen the parameters of who can work, and you either go older or you go younger, and they chose to go younger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy and Tsoukalas are hopeful that Republicans who said they were uncomfortable with some parts of the bill will ultimately decide to vote against it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article302920599.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Miami Herald}}}\uc2 , the Republican state senators Nick DiCeglie and Tom Wright helped move it out of the commerce and tourism committee on a 5-4 vote, but said it \u8220\'20\'1Cneeded work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Joe Gruters\uc2  joined three Democrats in voting against, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to let kids be kids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, however, pointed to another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridapolitics.com/archives/726029-house-panel-advances-bill-to-pay-interns-and-apprentices-less-than-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican bill that progressed this week}}}\uc2  that would allow employers to pay interns and apprentices less than minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo recap, they made the state hostile to immigrants. They deported a bunch of people, or scared people into not coming, or moving out of the state. They exacerbated worker shortages, so now they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to gut child labor protection standards, while at the same time passing a law that would allow them to classify these children and other workers as interns,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s insane, right?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250329el3t00108\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
