\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Labor defies criticism to add 3,400 public service roles\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Basford Canales \par \uc2 679 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 March 2025\par 22:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Katy Gallagher says staffing increases are necessary and an \u8216\'20\'18investment in the future\u8217\'20\'19Live updates: Australia federal budget 2025 latest news and reactionExplore all of our 2025 Australia federal budget coverage\par \par \uc2 The Albanese government will increase the federal public service by 3,400 roles over the next year, adding to the more than 40,000 roles created since Labor came to power.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/mar/25/australia-federal-budget-2025-main-policies-tax-cuts-medicare-donald-trump-tariffs-jim-chalmers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The budget papers }}}\uc2  also include another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/mar/24/finance-minister-reveals-a-further-2bn-in-savings-before-labors-next-federal-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit to the bottom lines of consultancy and labour hire firms}}}\uc2 , with Labor committing to slash a further $719m in external resourcing by 2028-29, totalling $4.7bn since 2022.\par \par \uc2 The size and efficiency of the public service has come under attack from the opposition, which has pledged to introduce a government efficiency agency, if elected, in an attempt to mirror Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bureaucratic razor gang in the US.\par \par \uc2 The opposition leader, \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 , and his frontbench have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/feb/10/littleproud-says-hardly-any-public-servant-jobs-to-go-under-coalition-government-in-significant-backdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly suggested the Coalition}}}\uc2  would slash a number of jobs in a quest for budget savings.\par \par \uc2 In defiance of the criticism, Labor has increased its average staffing level by 3,436 jobs for 2025-26, the budget papers show, with the total number of roles now expected to reach 213,439.\par \par \uc2 Most of those roles went to the \uc2 National Disability Insurance Agency\uc2 , the tax office and the defence department.\par \par \uc2 The budget shows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/feb/17/peter-dutton-wants-to-cut-public-service-jobs-in-canberra-heres-what-happened-last-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11,800 permanent roles have been created since May 2022}}}\uc2  to replace work previously undertaken by consultants and contractors.\par \par \uc2 The converted jobs make up about 28% of the 41,411 jobs added to the public service since Labor took office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s breaking news email}}}\par \par \uc2 One in five of those converted jobs were created in the \uc2 NDIA\uc2 , tasked with steering changes to the disability insurance scheme relied upon by more than 700,000 Australians with disability.\par \par \uc2 The public service minister, Katy Gallagher, defended the increases as necessary after \u8220\'20\'1Calmost a decade of outsourcing, underinvestment and reduced service outcomes\u8221\'20\'1D under former Coalition governments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn investment in our public service and its capability is an investment in the future security and prosperity of Australia,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallagher wrote in her budget preface.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Australian government recognises it cannot deliver outcomes for Australians without the foundations of a strong public service.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The minister\u8217\'20\'19s budget comments also point to a growing demand for services due to the country\u8217\'20\'19s ageing population, the changing geostrategic environment and increasing economic complexities.\par \par \uc2 Claims on Services Australia, the central welfare support agency, have increased by 35% since 2012, the preface said.\par \par \uc2 Gallagher also highlighted the fact that public servants made up 1.6% of the labour force in 2006-07 under the Howard government, compared with 1.5% in 2025-26, despite the overall headcount increasing by more than 45,000.\par \par \uc2 The shadow public service minister, \uc2 Jane Hume\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/mar/24/finance-minister-reveals-a-further-2bn-in-savings-before-labors-next-federal-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said the opposition would curb}}}\uc2  the number of bureaucrats in Canberra but said frontline services, such as those in Services Australia, would be spared from any cuts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s face it, services haven\u8217\'20\'19t improved but the cost and size of the public service has expanded and bloated exponentially,\u8221\'20\'1D she told Sky News on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Dutton has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/jan/31/peter-dutton-push-to-axe-dei-public-service-positions-compared-to-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously floated targeting diversity and inclusion positions}}}\uc2  in the \uc2 Australian Public Service\uc2  as well as \u8220\'20\'1Cchange managers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunication specialists\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The opposition has yet to outline where it would focus on first in its efforts to find savings beyond targeting non-frontline roles in Canberra. About 37% of APS jobs are in Canberra.\par \par \uc2 A ceiling on the number of public servants was previously introduced in the 2015-16 budget under the Turnbull government.\par \par \uc2 It used the average staffing level to cap the public service at or below 167,596 \u8211\'20\'13 equivalent to staffing levels in 2006-07.\par \par \uc2 Departments and agencies subsequently used labour hire firms and contractors to bring on additional staff to circumvent the staffing cap.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/may/05/morrison-government-spent-208bn-on-consultants-and-outsourcing-public-service-in-final-year-audit-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labor audit of the Morrison government in 2023}}}\uc2  found 112 agencies had spent $20.8bn on external firms, employing the equivalent of 53,900 full-time staff.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250325el3p000un\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
