\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US education department insiders warn student loan system at risk: \u8216\'20\'18The gatekeepers are gone\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 842 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 March 2025\par 11:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mass firings spark concern as department employees say cuts set stage for widespread fraud and abuse\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of firings inside the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s student aid department have sparked concern among workers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/student-debt-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 student loan}}}\uc2  advocates, who warn that the student loan system is at risk.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/03/linda-mcmahon-confirmed-education-secretary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Linda McMahon}}}\uc2 , the wrestling industry billionaire now serving as education secretary, has presented the sweeping cuts as an efficiency drive. But employees within the \uc2 US Department of Education\uc2  warn they set the stage for widespread fraud and abuse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey got rid of all of the quality checkers. It\u8217\'20\'19s only a matter of time [before] they cause the whole system to fail,\u8221\'20\'1D said one senior official who was spared by the cuts. They requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf this was a bank, and they fired all the quality assurance team, their regulator would have shut them down,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the opposite of safety.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Federal Student Aid, a unit within the education department, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/dismantling-education-department-student-loans/story?id=118730549"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oversees}}}\uc2  $1.6tn in student loans. At least 300 of its employees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/education/2025/03/16/education-department-waste-fraud-abuse-cuts/82370646007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were dismissed last week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following the firings, Trump signed an executive order on Thursday instructing McMahon to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/20/trump-executive-order-education-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 start dismantling the Department of Education}}}\uc2 , in an apparent attempt to circumvent the need to obtain congressional approval to formally close a federal department.\par \par \uc2 The Free Application for Federal Student Aid (Fafsa) website also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/student-loans-education-department-outage-layoffs-5afb5a0a1b51bbe50e5961a63b419041"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced}}}\uc2  an hours-long outage. Officials denied it was related to the cuts.\par \par \uc2 The senior official argued the blitz will likely result in more issues, such as longer wait times to get in contact with loan service providers, and more errors. \u8220\'20\'1CAs an organization, we were already doing a lot more work than our staffing provides. We would need 10 times more people for a bank of our size,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration is also \u8220\'20\'1Clying\u8221\'20\'1D about how the cuts were targeted, according to the official. \u8220\'20\'1CThey said they got rid of low performers, but they didn\u8217\'20\'19t do any of that assessment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the Guardian, the Department of Education claimed that no employees working on the Fafsa or student loan servicing were affected by last week\u8217\'20\'19s cuts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe department will deliver high-quality customer service to borrowers,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said. They pointed to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/about/news/press-release/us-department-of-education-initiates-reduction-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release}}}\uc2  on the firings, which stated that the department would continue to deliver on \u8220\'20\'1Call statutory programs\u8221\'20\'1D under its agency\u8217\'20\'19s purview, including student loans.\par \par \uc2 Student financial aid administrators, policy experts and trade unions are skeptical.\par \par \uc2 A fired Federal Student Aid employee explained that their department worked with academic institutions and state agencies to ensure compliance, process applications and recertify institutions seeking federal funds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were already severely understaffed. Without our office, these schools are stuck in limbo,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s mind-boggling. Everything we do is under statute.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They explained that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/about/ed-organization/functional-statements/fsa-functional-statements/partner-participation-and-oversight#:~:text=School%20Eligibility%20and%20Oversight%20Service,in%20Federal%20Student%20Aid%20programs."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 School Eligibility and Oversight Group}}}\uc2  handled recertifications, initial applications, updates, mergers, changes in ownerships, program reviews and cash monitoring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat Linda McMahon has done is given 5,000 institutions the green light to cause massive amounts of taxpayer fraud and abuse of federal financial aid dollars financed by taxpayers without any check and balances in place,\u8221\'20\'1D the fired employee said, comparing it to the 1980s, when for-profit academic institutions engaged in abuse and fraud that propelled the sector\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tcf.org/content/report/president-george-h-w-bush-cracked-abuses-profit-colleges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 student loan default rate}}}\uc2  to a record 41%.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe gatekeepers are gone,\u8221\'20\'1D the source added. \u8220\'20\'1CState agencies are now scrambling with how they have to move forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The mass firings alarmed advocates for student borrowers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese civil servants were working to ensure students and families can pay for college, working to protect students and families from predatory for-profit colleges, and holding servicers accountable for pushing millions further into debt,\u8221\'20\'1D said Aissa Canchola Ba\u241\'00\'F1ez, policy director at the Student Borrower Protection Center Policy.\par \par \uc2 The Institute for College Access and Success is \u8220\'20\'1Cparticularly concerned\u8221\'20\'1D about how the cuts could threaten college students and student loan borrowers, Sameer Gadkaree, its president, said. \u8220\'20\'1CCore functions of the department could experience outages or breakages, leaving students struggling to get or renew financial aid or campus-based aid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStudent loan borrowers, meanwhile, will struggle to access the benefits current law provides. And they can\u8217\'20\'19t be sure they will get reliable, accurate advice on student loan repayment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the \uc2 American Federation of Teachers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/19/teachers-union-sues-education-department-student-loans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  against the Department of Education over its suspension of applications and reviews of all income-driven repayment plans, a move which affects millions of borrowers.\par \par \uc2 Administrators are dubious of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s claims that the education department will continue to deliver all statutory programs, as it has claimed. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is hard for anyone to believe,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas McWhorter, dean of student financial services at \uc2 Northeastern University\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/thomas-mcwhorter-195962_it-has-been-a-hard-week-for-education-the-activity-7306424449073893376-2ONo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on LinkedIn}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt means oversight is gone, and approvals may never happen or there is no enforced compliance of statutory regulations,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd students will be impacted with these changes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250324el3o001mo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
