\par\par \uc2 Music\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Drake lost a rap battle\u8217\'20\'19: Universal files motion to dismiss rapper\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18misguided\u8217\'20\'19 lawsuit\b0\par\par\uc2 Dee Jefferson \par \uc2 721 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 March 2025\par 02:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Drake\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys accuse Universal of being \u8216\'20\'18a greedy company\u8217\'20\'19 that is \u8216\'20\'18finally being held responsible for profiting from dangerous misinformation\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Universal Music Group\uc2  have moved to dismiss Drake\u8217\'20\'19s defamation suit, characterising it as \u8220\'20\'1Ca misguided attempt\u8221\'20\'1D by the Canadian rapper to \u8220\'20\'1Csalve his wounds\u8221\'20\'1D after he \u8220\'20\'1Clost a rap battle\u8221\'20\'1D with rival Kendrick Lamar.\par \par \uc2 In the motion, filed on Monday in the US district court for the southern district of New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/universal-music"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Universal Music Group}}}\uc2  (\uc2 UMG\uc2 ), which represents both artists, claimed that Drake \u8220\'20\'1Clost a rap battle that he provoked and in which he willingly participated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of accepting the loss like the unbothered rap artist he often claims to be, he has sued his own record label in a misguided attempt to salve his wounds. Plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s complaint is utterly without merit and should be dismissed with prejudice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/may/10/drake-and-kendricks-rap-beef-explained-is-this-a-forever-thing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long-term rivalry between Drake and Kendrick Lamar}}}\uc2  escalated in March 2024 with the rapid-fire, tit-for-tat release of diss tracks by both artists, culminating in the release of Not Like Us on 4 May, in which Lamar framed Drake as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccertified pedophile\u8221\'20\'1D. The track proved immensely popular, topping the Billboard Global 200 chart and winning Record and Song of the Year at the 2025 Grammys.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2025/jan/15/drake-withdraws-legal-petition-over-kendrick-lamar-diss-track#:~:text=The%20suit%20alleges%20that%20UMG,to%20vigilante%20justice%20in%20response%E2%80%9D."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Drake filed a lawsuit in January}}}\uc2  accusing \uc2 UMG\uc2  of defamation and harassment, and alleging that \uc2 UMG\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Capproved, published and launched a campaign to create a viral hit out of a rap track\u8221\'20\'1D that was \u8220\'20\'1Cintended to convey the specific, unmistakable, and false factual allegation that Drake is a criminal pedophile, and to suggest that the public should resort to vigilante justice in response\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Drake\u8217\'20\'19s suit noted that the artwork for Not Like Us features a picture of his Toronto home with markers used to identify the homes of registered sex offenders; and referred to a shooting that occurred outside the residence days after the track\u8217\'20\'19s release in which a security guard was injured, and two attempted trespassings in the subsequent days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis lawsuit is not about the artist who created \u8216\'20\'18Not Like Us,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the filing by Drake\u8217\'20\'19s team read. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is, instead, entirely about \uc2 UMG\uc2 , the music company that decided to publish, promote, exploit, and monetize allegations that it understood were not only false, but dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In its motion to dismiss, Universal argue that Drake fails to make a claim for defamation, saying that Not Like Us \u8220\'20\'1Cconveys nonactionable opinion and rhetorical hyperbole, not fact,\u8221\'20\'1D and noting that the rapper has relied on \uc2 UMG\uc2  to promote his own diss tracks against Lamar and others.\par \par \uc2 Drake\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit, \uc2 UMG\uc2  says in its filing, \u8220\'20\'1Cdisregards the other Drake and Lamar diss tracks that surrounded \u8216\'20\'18Not Like Us\u8217\'20\'19 as well as the conventions of the diss track genre \u8230\'20\'26 diss tracks are a popular and celebrated artform centered around outrageous insults, and they would be severely chilled if Drake\u8217\'20\'19s suit were permitted to proceed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLess than three years ago, Drake himself signed a public petition criticizing \u8216\'20\'18the trend of prosecutors using artists\u8217\'20\'19 creative expression against them\u8217\'20\'19 by treating rap lyrics as literal fact,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 UMG\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s motion continues. \u8220\'20\'1CAs Drake recognized, when it comes to rap, \u8216\'20\'18[t]he final work is a product of the artist\u8217\'20\'19s vision and imagination\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDrake was right then and is wrong now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Universal also denies that its promotion of Not Like Us invited harassment of Drake, stating that the rapper is attempting \u8220\'20\'1Cto contort violent metaphors in the lyrics into incitement\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CAs with his defamation claim, Drake seeks to chill a form of artistic expression that he himself has embraced,\u8221\'20\'1D the motion reads.\par \par \uc2 In a statement provided to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2025/music/news/drake-kendrick-lamar-not-like-us-lawsuit-motion-dismiss-1236339456/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Variety}}}\uc2 , Drake\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Michael J. Gottlieb responded to Universal\u8217\'20\'19s motion to dismiss, saying: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 UMG\uc2  wants to pretend that this is about a rap battle in order to distract its shareholders, artists and the public from a simple truth: a greedy company is finally being held responsible for profiting from dangerous misinformation that has already resulted in multiple acts of violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis motion is a desperate ploy by \uc2 UMG\uc2  to avoid accountability, but we have every confidence that this case will proceed and continue to uncover \uc2 UMG\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s long history of endangering, abusing and taking advantage of its artists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250318el3i000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
