\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Johns Hopkins to lose 2,000 jobs after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s $800m cut in \uc2 USAid\uc2  funding\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 March 2025\par 12:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 University says cut in funding \u8216\'20\'18forcing us to wind down critical work\u8217\'20\'19 as academics rally against job losses\par \par \uc2 Johns Hopkins University\uc2  announced it was planning to cut more than 2,000 jobs after the Trump administration slashed $800m in grants to the renowned academic institution.\par \par \uc2 The funding for the positions had come from the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2 , which the administration has gutted with enormous cuts. A total of 247 domestic US workers and another 1,975 positions abroad in 44 countries will be affected by what amounts to the largest layoff in the history of the university.\par \par \uc2 The job losses will affect the university\u8217\'20\'19s Bloomberg School of Public Health, its medical school and its affiliated non-profit for international health, Jhpiego. The school of public health includes more than 80 research institutions that focus on issues such as gun violence, maternal health and the economic impacts of Alzheimer\u8217\'20\'19s disease.\par \par \uc2 The grant elimination announcement comes on the same day that hundreds of professors, researchers and other staff with the school of public health held a rally meant to show support for \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican scientists and science amid federal layoffs and cuts to research funding\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hub.jhu.edu/2025/03/10/stand-up-for-science-2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to }}}\uc2  the Hub, a publication of the public health school.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a difficult day for our entire community. The termination of more than $800m in \uc2 USAid\uc2  funding is now forcing us to wind down critical work here in Baltimore and internationally,\u8221\'20\'1D the university said in a statement shared with media.\par \par \uc2 Johns Hopkins receives the most federal research funding, and is the largest private employer, in both Maryland and Baltimore and employs more than 150,000 people, the university said in a statement to the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Those who lost their jobs due to the most recent grant funding cuts will be given 60 days\u8217\'20\'19 advance notice before they are laid off or furloughed, the statement continued.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has taken a major role in the administration as the head of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, have sought to dismantle \uc2 USAid\uc2 . Both have spread conspiracy theories and misinformation about supposed rampant fraud and waste within the agency.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has canceled more than 80% of all the programs at \uc2 USAid\uc2  following a six-week review, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , the US secretary of state, said on Monday. Johns Hopkins is also being impacted by the White House\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into dozens of US universities over pro-Palestinian protests.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the US canceled $400m in grants and contracts to \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s Columbia University\uc2 . The Trump administration is also seeking to deport Mahmoud Khalil, a Palestinian graduate who has played a prominent role in pro-Palestinian protests at Columbia.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250314el3e001jo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
