\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge orders Trump administration to reinstate most fired probationary staff\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 613 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 March 2025\par 16:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling by California judge applies to thousands of employees dismissed from six federal agencies\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in California granted a preliminary injunction to reinstate thousands of fired probationary workers at federal agencies as part of a lawsuit filed by the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruling by the judge William H Alsup in the US district court for the northern district of California applies to fired probationary employees at the Department of Defense, Department of Veterans Affairs, Department of Agriculture, Department of Energy, Department of the Interior and the Department of the Treasury.\par \par \uc2 Hours later, the US district judge James Bredar in Maryland agreed with 20 Democratic-led states that 18 agencies that had fired probationary employees en masse in recent weeks had violated regulations governing the laying off of federal workers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/03/13/doge-federal-workers-probationary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least 30,000}}}\uc2  probationary employees working for the federal government have been fired as part of the efforts of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D to slash the federal workforce and government expenditures.\par \par \uc2 Many of the employees were fired with the cited reason being poor performance, though workers have disputed this based on positive performance evaluations.\par \par \uc2 Alsup said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Clie\u8221\'20\'1D that the probationary workers who were fired had performance issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is sad, a sad day when our government would fire some good employee and say it was based on performance when they know good and well that\u8217\'20\'19s a lie,\u8221\'20\'1D Alsup said in court on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The judge also forbade the office of personnel management from providing any guidance to federal agencies on which employees should be terminated. Alsup authorized depositions and ordered further briefing on whether the administrative channel for fired workers to appeal their terminations is available or has been destroyed due to firings at the appeals board and office of special counsel personnel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[The] \uc2 AFGE\uc2  is pleased with Judge Alsup\u8217\'20\'19s order to immediately reinstate tens of thousands of probationary federal employees who were illegally fired from their jobs by an administration hellbent on crippling federal agencies and their work on behalf of the American public,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , national president of the union said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are grateful for these employees and the critical work they do, and \uc2 AFGE\uc2  will keep fighting until all federal employees who were unjustly and illegally fired are given their jobs back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, said on Thursday that the judge overstepped his bounds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA single judge is attempting to unconstitutionally seize the power of hiring and firing from the executive branch,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump administration will immediately fight back against this absurd and unconstitutional order . \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before the judge\u8217\'20\'19s order, the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/top-trump-administration-official-lie-mass-firings-federal/story?id=119679685"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  to make the acting head of the office of personnel management, Charles Ezell, available to testify on the firings in court.\par \par \uc2 In an earlier ruling, Alsup {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/federal-court-finds-firing-of-probationary-federal-employees-illegal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on 27 February that the firing of probationary employees was illegal because the office of personnel management had no authority to order it.\par \par \uc2 The OPM updated the 20 January memo on probationary employees, which the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2  argued reveals an admission it unlawfully directed the firings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COPM\u8217\'20\'19s revision of its Jan 20 memo is a clear admission that it unlawfully directed federal agencies to carry out mass terminations of probationary employees \u8211\'20\'13 which aligns with Judge Alsup\u8217\'20\'19s recent decision in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.mediaoutreach.meltwater.com/ls/click?upn=u001.5xyEJBgu5wyZZWYkONOSUCj78QAVTC3Nn5bLxIPgG0Zb7vugCnXuV0P72c-2B4LNxI6RNHmFkk2eN8FeCYZYmmm367F52Agv-2BpFIcTD693VYAk96DrZFSrjEXr2Avbu6M4-2BfeHu50JRAu9SCqBFIqFvw-3D-3Dga_r_p4A4YQt8epDIK9HlKea9sXuodp2-2FADEAQkVJz8qv9t2hYA8QvN-2BbA8YkBtuqJbFvaexJBJnbF3DZnqs4O6Z06mk3OSKoNLy9vWziKPa-2FwCBFWBx0u6zyAkp31aGhrmKjtyPlqJ6L96HdEu64jhoeTLqyzkRUGNzLDK8vGqe7goXIwMUfaJvD1kuQfwehk0vQuLeZTBevE-2FKYVZ5E1O2H2PZ9EEQk-2BrMPwv7Db-2F1QAVhv5KvorzsXkx2xgdY0TNODuRDl90JTqtCEP2dLfxVuphhlVGj6lKFuqW8NTOz-2FxPHsGdEY-2B01PndHSUNLb8jHHd2ZMggIlicpmMXBeRc8Uog-2Bb9ffReDphcmcEWH-2B6WoAaM5rt9lKjugXHuzptY2L0A0fIYqKNSyd6DsHgmVpDJA-3D-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit challenging these illegal firings}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the union said in a statement earlier this month. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery agency should immediately rescind these unlawful terminations and reinstate everyone who was illegally fired.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250313el3d002ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
