\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Guess what? You don\u8217\'20\'19t matter\u8217\'20\'19: what Trump\u8217\'20\'19s war on DEI means for every American who\u8217\'20\'19s not a straight white man\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 2,321 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 March 2025\par 11:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move to abolish diversity, equity and inclusion policies is a naked attempt to appeal to prejudice \u8211\'20\'13 but it may well backfire\par \par \uc2 Almost a decade ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rentaminority.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I started a business called Rent-A-Minority}}}\uc2 , which enabled companies to hire a minority ethnic person whenever they needed an injection of diversity to boost their image. I had a variety of inclusivity-enriching hires available, including an \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically ambiguous\u8221\'20\'1D category and a selection of smiling Muslim women (guaranteed not to support Islamic State or your money back).\par \par \uc2 Like every good startup, Rent-A-Minority posted testimonials from clients and influencers on its website. I made up all the blurbs, because that is the Silicon Valley way: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jan/04/elizabeth-holmes-verdict-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fake it till you make it}}}\uc2 . One of those fake comments was from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who was still considered a long shot for the presidency in January 2016, when my business launched. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I\u8217\'20\'19m president, I\u8217\'20\'19ll shut this site down,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blurb read.\par \par \uc2 My business, just in case you are reeling in horror, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/commentisfree/2016/feb/17/rent-a-minority-one-stop-solution-to-create-the-illusion-of-diversity-at-your-company"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was a joke}}}\uc2 . I launched it to satirise the superficial and patronising way in which many companies were approaching diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI). Not to toot my gay Palestinian horn, but the website went viral. Ironically, it briefly got one minority ethnic person (me) a lot of business speaking to companies around the world about how to approach diversity in a more meaningful manner.\par \par \uc2 Rent-A-Minority may have been a joke, but that fake Trump testimonial seems to have been a prophecy. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term has become a crusade against DEI. Hours into his presidency, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/22/trump-orders-immediate-closure-of-all-us-federal-diversity-offices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed two executive orders}}}\uc2  targeting \u8220\'20\'1Cradical and wasteful\u8221\'20\'1D DEI programmes. If a federal initiative has anything remotely to do with the issue, Trump has decreed that it must be eliminated. References to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/dei-purge-images-pentagon-diversity-women-black-8efcfaec909954f4a24bad0d49c78074"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Enola Gay}}}\uc2  aircraft that dropped an atomic bomb on Japan, for example, were marked for deletion by the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2 . Why? Because the aircraft\u8217\'20\'19s name has the word \u8220\'20\'1Cgay\u8221\'20\'1D in it.\par \par \uc2 DEI has been turned into a scapegoat. When a passenger jet and a US army helicopter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/11/dc-plane-crash-ntsb-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crashed over Washington DC}}}\uc2  in January, killing 67 people, one of the first things Trump said was that the collision could have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/feb/01/trump-responds-washington-plane-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the result of diversity hiring}}}\uc2 . This has been a favourite talking point of the right for a while \u8211\'20\'13 in January 2024, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  spluttered on X about how the aviation industry had \u8220\'20\'1Cprioritized DEI hiring over safety\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but it has gone from the fringe of politics to the frontline.\par \par \uc2 Now that the political landscape has changed, many companies that used to talk the big talk about inclusivity have changed their tune. Some, such as \uc2 Costco\uc2  and \uc2 Apple\uc2 , have defended their diversity policies and chosen to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/costco-shareholder-proposal-diversity-dei-0330f448741b35f2f788a36948ff3f95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stay the course}}}\uc2 . But roughly 20% of companies in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/stock-markets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 S&P 100}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.raconteur.net/talent-culture/dei-rollback-listicle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including Meta, Amazon, Target and McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 have retreated from DEI commitments since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s re-election, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/lot-chaos-companies-try-sense-140009119.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg News analysis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To understand where we are today in the US, we have to look at where we have been. DEI may be a relatively new term, but the idea has roots in the civil rights movement of the 50s and 60s. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/STATUTE-78/pdf/STATUTE-78-Pg241.pdf#page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Civil Rights Act of 1964}}}\uc2  made it illegal for most employers with 25 or more staff (reduced to 15 or more by the Equal Employment Opportunity Act of 1972) to discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, sex and national origin. At the same time, affirmative action policies emerged to try to redress the historical under-representation of racial minorities and women.\par \par \uc2 There is one group in workplaces where over 90% believe they are working in meritocracies \u8211\'20\'13 and that\u8217\'20\'19s white men\par \par \uc2 Joan Williams\par \par \uc2 That under-representation was immense: in 1966, African Americans comprised about 11% of the US population yet held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eeoc.gov/special-report/african-americans-american-workforce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fewer than 1%}}}\uc2  of all \u8220\'20\'1Cofficials and managers\u8221\'20\'1D roles (the most senior category defined by the \uc2 Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2 , which captured the data). By 2013, that had risen to 6.8%. As for women, they made up 9.4% of officials and managers in 1966, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eeoc.gov/special-report/american-experiences-versus-american-expectations#women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising to 38.6% in 2013}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While DEI has its roots in addressing injustices, there is a strong business case for it. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mckinsey.com/featured-insights/diversity-and-inclusion/diversity-matters-even-more-the-case-for-holistic-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research by McKinsey}}}\uc2 , companies with a representation of women exceeding 30% (which puts them in the top quartile) are significantly more likely to perform well financially than those with 30% or fewer. Companies in McKinsey\u8217\'20\'19s top quartile for ethnic diversity show an average \u8220\'20\'1Cfinancial advantage\u8221\'20\'1D of 27% over others.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uclawsf.edu/people/joan-williams/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan Williams}}}\uc2 , a law professor and the founding director of the Equality Action Center at UC Law San Francisco, has done data-based research that shows that, when approached properly, DEI initiatives result in more effective organisations. And \u8220\'20\'1Cproperly\u8221\'20\'1D doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean forcing employees to sit through one-off training sessions on unconscious bias, Williams stresses; it means introducing structural tweaks that remove bias in hiring and performance reviews, such as \u8220\'20\'1Ckeeping track of who\u8217\'20\'19s rejected based on lack of \u8216\'20\'18culture fit\u8217\'20\'19 and looking for demographic patterns\u8221\'20\'1D. In other words, when you create an environment where all talent \u8211\'20\'13 regardless of what they look like or where they come from \u8211\'20\'13 can rise to the top, rather than just the people whose faces and backgrounds \u8220\'20\'1Cfit\u8221\'20\'1D, you are more likely to get something approaching meritocracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all want a meritocracy, but too often we don\u8217\'20\'19t have them,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams says. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is one group in professional workplaces where over 90% believe they are working in meritocracies \u8211\'20\'13 and that\u8217\'20\'19s white men. Every other group has sharply less confidence that they are working in meritocracies because they feel that they are being held to a different standard.\u8221\'20\'1D And those people tend to be correct. \u8220\'20\'1CWe did 22 DEI experiments inside companies,\u8221\'20\'1D says Williams. \u8220\'20\'1COne company was horrified to find that they were hiring white men who had lower ratings than women and people of colour who weren\u8217\'20\'19t hired.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In short, DEI should always have been treated as a serious business issue. Instead, it has often been approached as a box-ticking exercise or a PR manoeuvre. Never was that truer than after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/apr/21/the-guardian-view-on-the-of-george-floyd-a-racial-reckoning-begins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the murder of George Floyd}}}\uc2  in 2020: as racial justice demonstrations erupted around the world, corporations suddenly started shouting about DEI from the rooftops. Listings for roles in DEI {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.shrm.org/resourcesandtools/hr-topics/talent-acquisition/pages/new-dei-roles-spike-after-racial-justice-protests.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased by 55%}}}\uc2  in the two months after Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death, according to the recruitment website \uc2 Glassdoor\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe amount of money I made starting May 2020 until about 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19ve never made so much money in my entire life,\u8221\'20\'1D says Akilah Cadet, a DEI practitioner and the author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/White-Supremacy-All-Around-Disabled/dp/0306831031"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White Supremacy Is All Around}}}\uc2 . Some of that money came from brands who genuinely seemed to care, she says, but others were just in it to look good. Now, however, the jobs have dried up. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve laid off my staff. I have a much smaller team. I\u8217\'20\'19m being punished as a result of people no longer wanting to care about people they should have been caring about in the first place,\u8221\'20\'1D Cadet says.\par \par \uc2 She is not the only one feeling punished. \u8220\'20\'1CImagine that you were working for a company where you had tools in place, access to an executive coach, a programme that got you into a leadership track,\u8221\'20\'1D Cadet says. \u8220\'20\'1CThese individuals had support and were told they were valued. Heterosexual, non-disabled, cisgendered white men and women have always had that [validation] in the workplace. And it will still be there after the attack on DEI, but it won\u8217\'20\'19t be for people who don\u8217\'20\'19t identify as those groups.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the bigger unfortunate thing that\u8217\'20\'19s happening here: \u8216\'20\'18You mattered \u8211\'20\'13 and guess what? I\u8217\'20\'19m going to remind you that you don\u8217\'20\'19t matter again.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s crusade seems to be less about effectiveness and more about reminding certain people that they don\u8217\'20\'19t matter. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not about diversity, equity and inclusion,\u8221\'20\'1D says Verna Myers, a DEI pioneer who was the vice-president of inclusion strategy at \uc2 Netflix\uc2  until September 2023. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a takedown of structures that have been put together for over 30, 40 years to really get us to be the America that we say we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Karen Attiah shares that sentiment. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s call this what it really is: resegregation,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2025/02/06/dei-gop-segregation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a column last month}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI mean it in the sense that a Black woman would never even be considered for a federal job or a management position at a big company \u8211\'20\'13 the way it was in, say, the 1960s. It is not \u8216\'20\'18inclusion\u8217\'20\'19 the Republicans want to get rid of, it\u8217\'20\'19s integration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s purge of DEI sympathisers within federal ranks has already affected some high-ranking people of colour. In late February, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/21/trump-hegseth-joint-chiefs-cq-brown-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly fired}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US air force\uc2  general CQ Brown Jr as chair of the joint chiefs of staff. Pete Hegseth, the former Fox News host who is now the defence secretary, had previously questioned whether Brown had been made chair because he was Black. \u8220\'20\'1CWas it because of his skin colour? Or his skill? We\u8217\'20\'19ll never know, but always doubt \u8211\'20\'13 which on its face seems unfair to CQ. But since he has made the race card one of his biggest calling cards, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really much matter,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Hegseth in one of his books.\par \par \uc2 Other Trump staffers have been even more blunt. \u8220\'20\'1CCompetent white men must be in charge if you want things to work,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/trump-darren-beattie-state-department/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Darren Beattie}}}\uc2 , who now has a senior job in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/02/03/politics/kfile-darren-beattie-state-department-controversial-tweets-white-nationalist-conference/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state department}}}\uc2 , on X in October. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, our entire national ideology is predicated on coddling the feelings of women and minorities, and demoralizing competent white men.\u8221\'20\'1D The implication seems to be that white men should be automatically considered competent until proved otherwise; everyone else should be seen as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdiversity hire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Heather Mac Donald, a fellow of the right-leaning thinktank the Manhattan Institute and the author of the book The Diversity Delusion, makes a similar argument. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you know that every institution is practising race and gender preferences, you have no confidence that, if you\u8217\'20\'19re in an emergency room and a Black doctor walks through the door, that doctor has been hired on the basis of merit and not race,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 But what about white men? Wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t it be ignorant to assume that every white man in a position of prominence was chosen solely on the basis of his qualifications and not, say, because he played golf with the right people or his face \u8220\'20\'1Cfitted\u8221\'20\'1D? \u8220\'20\'1CToday, to be a white male is to be at the bottom of the hiring pool,\u8221\'20\'1D Mac Donald says. \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to be twice, three times as good to be considered as a white male. The main elite institutions have made absolute preference for anybody other than heterosexual white males.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The idea that being white or male puts you at a disadvantage in the recruitment process is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/features/2024-07-29/white-men-the-most-likely-to-get-hired-even-with-dei-finds-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not reflected in reality}}}\uc2 , says Williams. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have over 10 years of data, including very recent data that shows that, in professional workplaces, white men report wildly less bias and wildly more fairness,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some white men who are really hurting, but those are non-elite white men. The economic and cultural position of elite white men is still pretty peachy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 White men still occupy most of the top-level roles in US companies. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cfodive.com/news/people-of-color-women-still-hold-under-15-of-c-suite-roles-crist-kolder/691689/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 2023 study}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cethnically and racially diverse executives hold just 12.5% of CEO, CFO and COO positions in Fortune 500 and S&P 500 companies \u8230\'20\'26 while women occupy 13.7% of the seats\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/04/11/1243713272/resume-bias-study-white-names-black-names"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Plenty of studies show}}}\uc2  that white-sounding names get called back for jobs more than Black-sounding ones.\par \par \uc2 No matter what the data says, however, there is still a sense among a lot of white men that women, LGBTQ+ people and racial minorities are suddenly the ones getting every advantage in life while they are being discriminated against. The podcast host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/article/2024/may/04/scott-galloway-algebra-of-wealth-pivot-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scott Galloway}}}\uc2 , who is very far from a rabid rightwinger, has argued that anti-discrimination laws exist already and there is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.campaignasia.com/article/scott-galloway-claims-diversity-initiatives-lead-to-reverse-racism/497839"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no need for DEI}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CCorporations and universities are now advantaging 76% of the populace [minority groups and women in the US] \u8211\'20\'13 and when you\u8217\'20\'19re advantaging 76% of the populace, you\u8217\'20\'19re not advantaging anybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Galloway is right that some DEI interventions haven\u8217\'20\'19t benefited anyone: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hbr.org/2016/07/why-diversity-programs-fail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 numerous studies}}}\uc2  show that the most common programmes, including mandatory diversity training, increase resentment in the workplace.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToo often in the past, DEI language used highly technical \u8216\'20\'18social justice warrior\u8217\'20\'19 language and you had scolding training without much guidance,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams says. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people found it irritating.\u8221\'20\'1D This isn\u8217\'20\'19t to say that we should just tear up DEI altogether, however. We have an opportunity to remake it in a more meaningful and effective manner. We are at an inflection point, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to be a regressive one, says Williams: \u8220\'20\'1CThe hope is \u8211\'20\'13 and there\u8217\'20\'19s some evidence of this \u8211\'20\'13 that the attack on DEI will cause people to actually focus on the evidence and making structural changes that make sure people are treated consistently.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Myers is also optimistic. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve made so many inroads that it will be very hard, especially in the young generation, to convince them that somehow a whitewashed version of talent is a place where they want to be,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason that I\u8217\'20\'19m optimistic is because I believe that humanity is always evolving. We will always move forward. Will there be obstacles and retrenchment? Yes. But I think we\u8217\'20\'19re better positioned than we ever have been to resist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250313el3d000jk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
