\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and Texas governor celebrate firing of worker over pronouns in email signature\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 799 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2025\par 20:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Billionaire Trump ally and Greg Abbott tweet about Frank Zamora, who was let go after refusing to remove pronouns\par \par \uc2 The Texas governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greg Abbott}}}\uc2 , and, later, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  showed support on Wednesday for the firing of a state employee who refused to remove his pronouns from his work email signature.\par \par \uc2 Frank Zamora, 31, was let go from his job as a program manager at the Texas real estate commission (TREC) last month because he refused to comply with a mandate from the organisation to employees to remove gender pronouns from email signatures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI actually anticipated this coming, just because we knew that many changes that were being made at the federal level were being mimicked at the state level,\u8221\'20\'1D Zamora said.\par \par \uc2 Abbott celebrated the move on X, sharing a report from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://subscribe.statesman.com/restricted?return=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.statesman.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Fpolitics%2Fstate%2F2025%2F03%2F05%2Ftexas-agency-orders-remove-pronouns-fires-employee-who-refused%2F80020922007%2F&gps-source=CPROADBLOCKDH&itm_source=roadblock&itm_medium=onsite&itm_campaign=premiumroadblock&gca-cat=p&gca-uir=true&gca-epti=z11----p119050c119050e000700v007888o11----b0062xxd006265&gca-ft=13&gca-ds=sophi&sltsgmt=1010_B&theme=twentyfour&hideGrid=true&gnt-eid=control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Austin American-Statesman}}}\uc2  on the firing and writing: \u8220\'20\'1CA Texas state employee refused to remove pronouns from email signature. He was fired before noon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Musk, who was appointed by Donald Trump to lead the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D tasked with reducing federal spending, replied to Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s post with two fire emojis.\par \par \uc2 Soon after Trump signed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/defending-women-from-gender-ideology-extremism-and-restoring-biological-truth-to-the-federal-government/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive order}}}\uc2  on 20 January titled \u8220\'20\'1CDefending Women from Gender Ideology Extremism and Restoring Biological Truth to the Federal Government\u8221\'20\'1D, which recognized only two sexes \u8211\'20\'13 male and female \u8211\'20\'13 Abbott issued his own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gov.texas.gov/news/post/governor-abbott-directs-texas-state-agencies-to-reject-woke-gender-ideologies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directive}}}\uc2  for the state on 30 January with similar language.\par \par \uc2 State agencies like the TREC interpreted Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s directive for themselves and issued rules and guidelines to employees accordingly, which included removing gender pronouns from official work communications, including email signatures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGreetings all. It was a beautiful weekend in Austin and I hope you were able to enjoy it \u8230\'20\'26 On a very different note, based on a recent directive from Governor Abbott, the agency is modifying its employee email signature block template by removing preferred pronouns,\u8221\'20\'1D read an email seen by the Guardian from Zamora\u8217\'20\'19s supervisor at the TREC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe new template is attached. Please look at your signature and make sure yours complies. I understand this change may have an impact on employees and I am sensitive to that. The Governor, however, has directed the agency to act and so we will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was the first time Zamora had been asked to comply with an order that went against his personal beliefs, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I have long felt that there was a disconnect between my personal beliefs and my personal politics and that of the state which I live in, I always sort of wrote it off as separate entities,\u8221\'20\'1D Zamora said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolitics can change every two and four years, but a good career can be for life, so I sort of kept those two entities compartmentalized. I kept them separate. But I was firm in my convictions and I made the stand that I felt was right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zamora announced his refusal to comply in a letter penned to his supervisors, which read in part: \u8220\'20\'1CI recognize that my employer has the right to dictate the manner in which I address the public. I also recognize that in the grand scheme of things, the layout of an email signature block is a fairly innocuous and inconsequential piece of our daily duties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever \u8230\'20\'26 it is clear that this latest directive is part of a broader effort to wipe out the acknowledgement of non-binary, intersex and transgender persons throughout Texas as well as sending the societal message that these individuals are not accepted in this state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After sending the letter, Zamora said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cultimately given the choice between removing the pronouns, resigning or being terminated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He chose to keep the pronouns and refused to resign. He was then fired in the first week of February.\par \par \uc2 When asked about the response from Abbott and Musk, Zamora said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t really have a response to that. They are doing what they must to appease the groups that have kept them in power. That would be my only comment on the subject.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zamora added: \u8220\'20\'1CPronouns are grammar. They\u8217\'20\'19re a function of almost every sentence that we speak. Their origins go back to old English and the Vikings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, we have chosen to make them a politicized topic and a hot-button issue. I felt that this order was strictly passed down to appease a certain political movement, and that it was strictly done, essentially, to win a culture war. And I do not believe that the LGBTQ+ community \u8211\'20\'13 trans individuals, non-binary, intersex or any individuals who choose to display their preferred pronouns \u8211\'20\'13 deserve to be made political collateral or to be put on the chopping block.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The TREC did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250306el3600336\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/10/2026\cell \pard \ql \